{"level":30,"time":1776703114542,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HwxdvqA3tf3mPk2Fo8HNQ4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've read the grouping file. This is about tree clearances from overhead electric lines. Let me understand the key points:\n\n**Grouping Overview:**\n- **Title**: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n- **Subject**: Tree placement requirements near overhead electric distribution and transmission lines\n- **Key Regulations**: UCM § 1.10.10.4 and related sections\n\n**Key Thresholds:**\n- Distribution lines (< 60kV): \n  - < 15 ft: Only utility-compatible trees\n  - 15-25 ft: Utility-compatible OR trees < 40 ft mature height\n  - > 25 ft: All trees OK\n- Transmission lines (≥ 60kV): 50 ft minimum, only utility-compatible within that zone\n- 10 ft from utility poles (any tree)\n- 10 ft from pad-mounted equipment\n- 5 ft from underground equipment\n- 20 ft from underground equipment requires root barriers\n\n**Checklist Items (15 total):**\n1. EL-2.1: Non-UC trees within 15 ft of distribution\n2. EL-2.2: Non-UC trees within 50 ft of transmission\n3. EL-2.3: Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution\n4. EL-2.4: Large trees (40+ ft) within 50 ft of transmission\n5. EL-2.5: Trees in transmission easement\n6. EL-2.6: Trees within 10 ft of utility pole\n7. EL-2.7: Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment\n8. EL-2.8: Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment\n9. EL-2.9: Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment lack root barriers\n\n\n10. EL-2.10: Plant schedule doesn't identify species\n11. EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated on plans\n12. EL-2.12: Clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor\n13. EL-2.13: Clearances measured from tree canopy instead of trunk\n14. EL-2.14: Trees not shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead facilities\n15. EL-2.15: Trees in prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval\n\nNow I need to check project applicability by reviewing the facts and README files, then examine site plans to understand existing conditions and evaluate each checklist item against the project specifics.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3648,"cache_read_input_tokens":23755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3648},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"0d97b0f9-6b46-43f6-8a9d-c1618d13d04f"}
