 SIGN\n- G. GAS MARKER SIGN\n- T. APPARENT GAS TEST STATION\n\n## Block 12: table — A table listing trees found on the property, providing an ID number, size (caliper in inches), and type (species) for each tree.\n\nTREE TABLE\n| NO # | SIZ. | TYPE |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4000 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4001 | 15\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4002 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4003 | 12\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4004 | 22\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4006 | 13\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4007 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4008 | 13\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4009 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4010 | 18\" | CHINA BERRY |\n| 4011 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4012 | 12\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4013 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4014 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4015 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4016 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4017 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4019 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4022 | 24\" | PECAN |\n| 4023 | 24\" | M |\n| 4024 | 8\" | ELM |\n| 4025 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4026 | 28\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4027 | 15\" | M |\n| 4028 | 36\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4030 | 14\" | PECAN |\n| 4031 | 16\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4032 | 18\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4033 | 11\" | ELM |\n| 4034 | 20\" | CHINA BERRY |\n| 4035 | 16\" | ELM |\n| 4036 | 14\" | PECAN |\n| 4037 | 11\" | ASH |\n| 4038 | 20\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4040 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4041 | 13\" | ELM |\n| 4042 | 34\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4043 | 15\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4044 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4045 | 20\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4046 | 17\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4047 | 16\" | PINE |\n\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776703133337,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01SAzmEREkgVg6tDofjrFnCe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on what I've read so far, it appears that:\n\n1. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows the layout of buildings, driveways, parking, detention pond, utility lines, and easements. There is a note about \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date\" but this doesn't necessarily indicate overhead electric lines present.\n\n2. Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows \"underground electric lines\" with transformers, pull boxes, and meters.\n\n3. The facts.md mentions 5' electric easements in the plat documents.\n\nThe key issue is: Are there OVERHEAD electric facilities on or adjacent to the site? The grouping is specifically about overhead electric lines and clearances from them. If the site uses underground electric service exclusively, then most or all of the checklist items would not be applicable.\n\nHowever, I should check Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) and possibly look at the vision analysis of the site plan sheets to see if there are overhead utility poles visible on the site or immediately adjacent to it.\n\nLet me check if there's any vision analysis already done on Sheet 9 or if I need to request it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5730,"cache_read_input_tokens":43513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5730},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","uuid":"75ec65d1-e0be-4e28-810c-3127d0751623"}
