{"level":30,"time":1776703140043,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GN5RCo3q4q4nULEBZtHfm1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have good information. Let me summarize what I've found:\n\n**Tree Species Proposed (from Sheet 35 plant schedule):**\n\nShade Trees:\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana), 100 gal, 4\" cal\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia), 100 gal, 4\" cal\n\nOrnamental Trees:\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora), 45 gal, 2.5\" cal\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana), 45 gal, 2.5\" cal\n\nShrubs:\n- 12 Dwarf Palmetto (Sabal minor), 5 gallon\n- 24 Big Muhly (Muhlenbergia lindheimerii), 1 gallon\n- 29 Gulf Muhly (Muhlenbergia capillaris 'Regal Mist'), 1 gallon\n- 8 Texas Sage (Leucophyllum frutescens 'Green Cloud'), 7 gallon\n- 8 Dwarf Wax Myrtle (Myrica cerifera 'Don's Dwarf'), 7 gallon\n\nGroundcovers:\n- 92 Obedient Plant (Phydrotegia virginiana), 4\" flat\n- 72 Frogfruit (Phyla nodiflora), 4\" flat\n\n**Key Finding from Sheet 31:** \nThe landscape plan shows \"Overhead Electric\" (OHE) utility lines on the site. This is important!\n\n**Electrical Infrastructure:**\n- Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows UNDERGROUND electric lines, transformers, and pull boxes\n- But Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows that overhead electric lines ARE present on the site\n\n\n- I need to identify which trees are positioned near those overhead lines and cross-reference their mature heights against ECM Appendix F utility compatibility requirements. Let me examine the landscape plan visually to locate the overhead electric lines and see which species are planted in proximity to them.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7884,"cache_read