{"level":30,"time":1776703163189,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Identify and describe the location of all transformer pads shown on this electrical plan. For each transformer, provide: (1) its location relative to building numbers and site features, (2) whether it appears to be on private property or in easements, (3) any visible clearances or proximity to buildings, structures, driveways, sidewalks, fire lanes, or parking areas, (4) any fencing, bollards, or protective elements shown around the transformer, (5) the general orientation and whether the access door faces any confined areas or adjacent structures.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" there are five distinct transformer pads explicitly labeled as \"Electrical Transformer Pad.\" They are denoted by a solid square surrounded by a dashed rectangular outline.\n\nHere is the detailed information for each, based strictly on what is visually represented in the plan:\n\n### 1. Northwest Transformer Pad (Near Bldg. 1)\n*   **Location:** Located in the northwest quadrant of the site, positioned west of \"Bldg. 1\" (specifically adjacent to \"Unit 101\") and north of the primary curved entrance driveway.\n*   **Property/Easement:** It appears to be located on private property within the development's boundary line. It is surrounded by a dashed rectangular line, which typically indicates a utility easement or dedicated clearance zone for the pad, though it is not explicitly labeled with text as an easement at that specific spot. It is located near a labeled \"Sidewalk Easement\" running along the western boundary.\n*   **Clearances/Proximity:** It is situated very close to the northern edge of the curved driveway (curb and gutter). It is also positioned between the western property boundary/sidewalk and Bldg. 1.\n*   **Protective Elements:** There are no visual indications of fencing, bollards, or other protective structural elements explicitly drawn or labeled around this transformer pad.\n*   **Orientation/Access Doors:** The pad is drawn as a simple square oriented parallel to the western property line. There are no access doors, hinges, or swing arcs visually depicted, so the direction the doors face cannot be determined from this plan.\n\n### 2. West Central Transformer Pad (Near Bldg. 2)\n*   **Location:** Located on the western edge of the site, positioned west of \"Bldg. 2\" (specifically adjacent to \"Unit 201\") and south of the primary curved entrance driveway.\n*   **Property/Easement:** It is located inside the western property boundary line. Like the others, it is surrounded by a dashed rectangular outline, suggesting a dedicated clearance area or specific pad easement, though it lacks an explicit text label stating so. It is adjacent to the labeled \"Sidewalk Easement.\"\n*   **Clearances/Proximity:** It is in close proximity to the western sidewalk and the western wall of Unit 201.\n*   **Protective Elements:** There are no visible bollards, fences, or protective elements drawn or labeled around the pad.\n*   **Orientation/Access Doors:** Drawn as a simple square parallel to Bldg. 2. No access doors are visually depicted, making it impossible to determine facing or confined space interactions related to doors.\n\n### 3. Southwest Transformer Pad (Near Bldg. 8)\n*   **Location:** Located in the southwest quadrant of the site, positioned directly west of \"Bldg. 8\" (specifically adjacent to \"Unit 801\").\n*   **Property/Easement:** It is located inside the western property boundary, surrounded by a dashed rectangular outline. A \"Vault Easement\" is labeled nearby, and a \"Sidewalk Easement\" runs along the property edge to its west.\n*   **Clearances/Proximity:** It is situated very close to the western boundary line/sidewalk and the western wall of Unit 801.\n*   **Protective Elements:** No bollards, fencing, or protective barriers are visibly drawn or labeled.\n*   **Orientation/Access Doors:** Drawn as a simple square parallel to Bldg. 8. No access doors are visually indicated.\n\n### 4. East Central Transformer Pad (Between Bldg. 4 & Bldg. 5)\n*   **Location:** Located centrally in the eastern half of the site, positioned in the open space between \"Bldg. 4\" (east of \"Unit 404\") and \"Bldg. 5\" (west of \"Unit 504\").\n*   **Property/Easement:** It is located deep within the private property limits. It is surrounded by a dashed rectangular outline indicating a clearance zone or specific pad easement.\n*   **Clearances/Proximity:** It is situated in a pedestrian area or open corridor between two residential buildings, near connecting sidewalks. It is flanked by buildings to its east and west.\n*   **Protective Elements:** There are no visible bollards, fencing, or other protective elements drawn or labeled.\n*   **Orientation/Access Doors:** Drawn as a simple square aligned with the surrounding buildings. No access doors are visually depicted.\n\n### 5. Southeast Transformer Pad (Near Bldg. 7)\n*   **Location:** Located in the southeast quadrant of the site, positioned east of \"Bldg. 7\" (specifically adjacent to \"Unit 704\") and south of Bldg. 6.\n*   **Property/Easement:** Located within the private property bounds, surrounded by the standard dashed rectangular outline seen on the other pads.\n*   **Clearances/Proximity:** It is situated near the eastern wall of Unit 704 and adjacent to a paved pathway/sidewalk area. An \"Electrical Pull Box\" is located immediately to its south.\n*   **Protective Elements:** No bollards, fencing, or protective barriers are visibly drawn or labeled around it.\n*   **Orientation/Access Doors:** Drawn as a simple square parallel to Bldg. 7. No access doors are visually indicated on the plan.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"