{"level":30,"time":1776703167815,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Please examine the electrical site plan and identify:\n\n1. The locations of all transformer pads shown on this electrical plan. For each transformer:\n   - Describe its location on the site (e.g., \"southeast area near Building 3\")\n   - Note whether dimensions or clearance measurements are provided to adjacent buildings, property lines, or site features\n   - Identify the access door orientation if visible\n   - Note if the pad dimensions are specified (e.g., \"5'x5'\" or \"10'x10'\")\n   - Note if there are any service type specifications (single-phase or three-phase)\n\n2. Describe the routing of electrical lines from transformers to meters\n\n3. Identify the proximity of transformers to:\n   - Buildings and their finished floor elevations\n   - Property lines and easements\n   - Parking areas, driveways, or vehicle routes\n   - Any utility lines or infrastructure shown on the plan\n   - Sidewalks or public areas\n\n4. List any notes or specifications related to transformer installations, pad details, or electrical design\n\nPlease be specific with locations and spatial relationships to help evaluate clearance compliance.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here is a detailed visual analysis addressing your specific questions:\n\n### 1. Transformer Pad Locations and Details\nThere are four specific locations labeled \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\" on this site plan. None of the transformers show specified pad dimensions (e.g., 5'x5'), clearance measurements, access door orientations, or service type specifications (single/three-phase) in the visual layout or annotations.\n\n*   **Transformer 1**: Located on the northwest side of the site, situated west of **Bldg. 1** near the unit labeled **Unit 101**. It is drawn as a simple square with an \"E\" inside.\n*   **Transformer 2**: Located on the mid-west side of the site, situated west of **Bldg. 2** near **Unit 201**.\n*   **Transformer 3**: Located on the eastern side of the site, situated east of **Bldg. 5** near **Unit 504**.\n*   **Transformer 4**: Located in the south-central area of the site, situated between **Bldg. 7** (east of **Unit 703**) and **Bldg. 6** (south of **Unit 602**).\n\n### 2. Routing of Electrical Lines\n*   The routing is depicted via solid blue lines connecting the various electrical components. \n*   A line on the western side is explicitly labeled with a callout pointing to it that reads \"**Underground Electric Line**\", indicating the routing method.\n*   The general routing path shown traces from the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations to designated \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" locations (indicated by blue squares), and then branches out to connect to the \"**Electrical Meters**\" which are mounted on the exterior boundaries of the various building units.\n\n### 3. Proximity of Transformers to Site Features\nBecause exact clearance dimensions are not provided on this sheet, proximity is described based on visual adjacency on the scaled plan.\n\n*   **Buildings and Finished Floor Elevations (FFE)**:\n    *   Transformer 1 is immediately adjacent to the west wall of **Bldg. 1** (**FFE = 687.50**).\n    *   Transformer 2 is immediately adjacent to the west wall of **Bldg. 2** (**FFE = 686.50**).\n    *   Transformer 3 is immediately adjacent to the east wall of **Bldg. 5** (**FFE = 683.0**).\n    *   Transformer 4 is positioned closely between **Bldg. 7** (**FFE = 686.0**) and **Bldg. 6** (**FFE = 683.0**).\n*   **Property Lines and Easements**: \n    *   Transformers 1 and 2 are located near the western boundary line, proximate to a \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n    *   Transformer 3 is located near the eastern property boundary, adjacent to a \"25' Drainage Easement\".\n*   **Parking Areas, Driveways, or Vehicle Routes**:\n    *   Transformers 1 and 4 are situated directly adjacent to the internal concrete driveways/parking loops. \n*   **Utility Lines or Infrastructure**: \n    *   All transformers are shown proximate to gray lines indicating existing or proposed water, wastewater, and storm infrastructure, but no specific clearance radii from these utilities are drawn. \n    *   Transformer 3 is located very close to an \"**Existing Retaining Wall**\" shown on the eastern boundary.\n*   **Sidewalks or Public Areas**:\n    *   Transformers 1 and 2 are located adjacent to external perimeter sidewalks along the western edge of the development.\n\n### 4. Notes or Specifications Related to Electrical Design\nThere are no dedicated notes or tables on this specific sheet detailing transformer installation specs, structural pad details, or electrical load designs. The available text blocks are standard utility and excavation notes:\n\n**Utility Notes** (bottom right):\n> \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"\n> \"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"\n> \"3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\"\n> \"4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\"\n\n**Note** (bottom left):\n> \"This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provided that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\"\n\n*(Note: If strict clearance validations are required, a secondary electrical detail sheet or specification document would be needed, as this plan only illustrates