{"level":30,"time":1776703184249,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Does this existing conditions survey show any overhead utility poles or overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) on or adjacent to the property? If yes, please describe their location(s) on the site and any associated labels or annotations. Look for the symbol for utility poles and overhead utility lines in the legend and identify where they appear on the survey drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey, yes, there are overhead utility poles and overhead utility lines shown on and adjacent to the property.\n\nHere are the specific details and locations found on the drawing:\n\n**Legend Symbols:**\n*   The legend identifies a **\"UTILITY POLE\"** with a symbol that appears as a circle with a cross or plus sign inside it (⊕).\n*   Overhead utility lines are represented on the drawing by a line periodically broken by the text **\"- OH -\"**.\n\n**Locations on the Site Plan:**\n\n1.  **Along the Western Boundary (Valley View Road):**\n    *   There is a continuous overhead utility line (marked with \"- OH -\") running north-south, roughly parallel to the western property line along Valley View Road. It appears to be located primarily within the right-of-way, just outside the property boundary.\n    *   Along this line, there are at least three **\"UTILITY POLE\"** symbols shown:\n        *   One is located near the southwest corner of the property.\n        *   A second one is located further north, roughly midway along the property's Valley View Road frontage.\n        *   A third is located near the northwest corner of the property's frontage.\n\n2.  **Crossing onto the Property:**\n    *   An overhead utility line (marked with \"- OH -\") branches off from the middle utility pole located on the Valley View Road frontage.\n    *   This line runs eastwards, crossing the western property line and extending over the property.\n    *   It passes over an area labeled \"CONC.\" and terminates at the existing building on the site.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1385,"outputTokens":352,"totalTokens":4237,"reasoningTokens":2500},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Does this existing conditions survey show any overhead utility poles or overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) on or adjacent to the property? If yes, please describe their location(