tility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n    21→* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n    22→* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n    23→* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n    24→* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n    25→* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n    26→* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n    27→* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n    28→\n    29→---\n    30→\n    31→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    32→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b1b0506-f5d7-4ee0-b799-49f4ef36919d","uuid":"97c8d1d1-87ef-401f-854b-12cdb1493b2a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 20 — Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile\n\nUtility tap public plan and profile for townhomes project.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the public plan and profile for a proposed utility tap (Water Line A) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the connection to an existing AC water main, the transition to new DI pipe, and the installation of a new fire demand meter, vault, and fire hydrant.\n\n**Key values:**\n* Proposed Pipe Segments: 47.0 lf of 8\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 5.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ -0.00% slope), 12.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 3.0 lf of 6\" C900, 5.0 lf of 6\" C900\n* Flowline Elevations: FL 8\" = 674.33', FL In 6\" = 674.42', FL Out 6\" = 674.42'\n* Restraints: 52' of restraints required from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52\n* Benchmarks: BM #1 = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n* Pressure Reducing Valve (PRV) Threshold: 65 psi\n* Geologist Inspection Trench Depth Threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\n* **Block 2**: drawing — Plan View of Utility Tap. Top-down layout showing the proposed connection to the existing 6\" water line, the new fire hydrant, vault, and various utility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776703202230,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan carefully and identify:\n1. Are there ANY overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this site plan? If yes, describe their location, routing, and any labels.\n2. Where are utility poles shown, if any?\n3. What trees are shown on the plan and where are they located relative to any overhead lines or poles?\n4. Is there a utility legend or notes indicating what overhead utilities are present or planned?\nPlease be very specific about locations (north, south, east, west areas of the site) and any distance or dimension callouts shown.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are there ANY overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this site plan? If yes, describe their location, routing, and any labels.**\nYes, there is an overhead electric line shown on the plan.\n*   **Location & Routing:** It is located along the southern boundary of the site (assuming standard orientation where the North arrow points up, which is confirmed by the North arrow in the bottom right corner). It runs horizontally (East-West) parallel to and very close to the southern property line.\n*   **Labels:** The line is denoted by a specific line type with the text label **\"-OHE-\"** embedded directly within it, visible near the center of the southern boundary.\n\n**2. Where are utility poles shown, if any?**\nThere are no symbols explicitly labeled as \"utility poles\" on the drawing or in a legend. However, there are small circular markings along the routing of the \"-OHE-\" line that typically represent poles on such plans:\n*   There is a small circle on the line near the far Southwest corner of the site plan area.\n*   There is another small circle with a dot in the center located near the Southeast corner, along the same boundary line.\n*   *Note: Because there is no utility legend to confirm, these can only be identified as possible pole locations based on their position on the OHE line.*\n\n**3. What trees are shown on the plan and where are they located relative to any overhead lines or poles?**\nThere are numerous trees shown planted along the southern boundary of the property, directly adjacent to and underneath the indicated \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **Location relative to OHE:** A row of new trees is planned in the landscape buffer strip along the southern edge. The circles representing the canopies of these trees overlap or are immediately adjacent to the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **Specific Trees:** Scanning from West to East along the southern boundary near the OHE line, the following tree symbols and tags are visible:\n    *   A large symbol indicating an existing tree is located at the Southwest corner, very close to the start of the OHE line.\n    *   Moving east, there are trees designated with the tag **\"M\"** (which the key defines as \"MITIGATION TREE\").\n    *   Further east, there is a tree tagged **\"PL\"** (defined as \"PARKING LOT TREE\").\n    *   Continuing east, there are additional trees tagged **\"M\"**.\n*   All of these trees along the southern property line appear to be planted directly in the path of or very near the overhead electric line.\n\n**4. Is there a utility legend or notes indicating what overhead utilities are present or planned?**\nNo, there is no specific utility legend or notes section regarding overhead utilities on this sheet.\n*   The provided legends are **\"IRRIGATION NOTES:\"**, **\"NOTE:\"** (referencing finished elevations, vegetation establishment, and supplemental irrigation), and **\"KEY NOTES:\"** (referencing paving, yard types, fences, and sod).\n*   There is a small key for tree tags (SY, PL, P, M) located on the right side of the plan.\n*   The presence of the overhead electric line is indicated solely by the **\"-OHE-\"** label embedded in the line type on the drawing itself.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1435,"outputTokens":726,"totalTokens":4449,"reasoningTokens":2288},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Landscape Plan carefully and identify:\n1. Are there ANY overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this site plan? If yes, describe their location, routing, and any labels.\n2. Where are utility poles shown, if any?\n3. What trees are shown on the plan and where are they located relative to any overhead lines or poles?\n4. Is there a utility legend or notes indicating what overhead utilities are present or planned?\nPlease be very specific about locations (north, south, east, west areas of the site) and any distance or dimension callouts shown."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-zsreCb3SVeB16E3KUkjMpHI5","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Mon, 20 Apr 2026 16:40:02 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::9zvbz-1776703154932-e92517ecad0b"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are there ANY overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this site plan? If yes, describe their location, routing, and any labels.**\nYes, there is an overhead electric line shown on the plan.\n*   **Location & Routing:** It is located along the southern boundary of the site (assuming standard orientation where the North arrow points up, which is confirmed by the North arrow in the bottom right corner). It runs horizontally (East-West) parallel to and very close to the southern property line.\n*   **Labels:** The line is denoted by a specific line type with the text label **\"-OHE-\"** embedded directly within it, visible near the center of the southern boundary.\n\n**2. Where are utility poles shown, if any?**\nThere are no symbols explicitly labeled as \"utility poles\" on the drawing or in a legend. However, there are small circular markings along the routing of the \"-OHE-\" line that typically represent poles on such plans:\n*   There is a small circle on the line near the far Southwest corner of the site plan area.\n*   There is another small circle with a dot in the center located near the Southeast corner, along the same boundary line.\n*   *Note: Because there is no utility legend to confirm, these can only be identified as possible pole locations based on their position on the OHE line.*\n\n**3. What trees are shown on the plan and where are they located relative to any overhead lines or poles?**\nThere are numerous trees shown planted along the southern boundary of the property, directly adjacent to and underneath the indicated \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **Location relative to OHE:** A row of new trees is planned in the landscape buffer strip along the southern edge. The circles representing the canopies of these trees overlap or are immediately adjacent to the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **Specific Trees:** Scanning from West to East along the southern boundary near the OHE line, the following tree symbols and tags are visible:\n    *   A large symbol indicating an existing tree is located at the Southwest corner, very close to the start of the OHE line.\n    *   Moving east, there are trees designated with the tag **\"M\"** (which the key defines as \"MITIGATION TREE\").\n    *   Further east, there is a tree tagged **\"PL\"** (defined as \"PARKING LOT TREE\").\n    *   Continuing east, there are additional trees tagged **\"M\"**.\n*   All of these trees along the southern property line appear to be planted directly in the path of or very near the overhead electric line.\n\n**4. Is there a utility legend or notes indicating what overhead utilities are present or planned?**\nNo, there is no specific utility legend or notes section regarding overhead utilities on this sheet.\n*   The provided legends are **\"IRRIGATION NOTES:\"**, **\"NOTE:\"** (referencing finished elevations, vegetation establishment, and supplemental irrigation), and **\"KEY NOTES:\"** (referencing paving, yard types, fences, and sod).\n*   There is a small key for tree tags (SY, PL, P, M) located on the right side of the plan.\n*   The presence of the overhead electric line is indicated solely by the **\"-OHE-\"** label embedded in the line type on the drawing itself.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1435,"outputTokens":726,"totalTokens":4449,"reasoningTokens":2288},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":2123916.830395,"endTime":2170879.175849,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"s1bmaeKwHd-JxtUPtK2jyQg"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.