{"level":30,"time":1776703204581,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Examine the existing conditions survey and identify any overhead utility poles, overhead utility lines, or overhead electric infrastructure shown on or adjacent to the property boundaries. Specifically look for: (1) Utility poles along Valley View Road or property boundaries; (2) Overhead lines crossing the property or adjacent to it; (3) Any labels or notations indicating the presence of existing overhead electrical facilities. If overhead infrastructure is present, describe its location relative to the property and the extent to which it appears on the drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Existing Conditions Survey,\" here is a detailed report regarding overhead utility poles, lines, and electrical infrastructure on or adjacent to the property:\n\n### 1. Utility Poles\nUtility poles are indicated on the drawing by small circular symbols with an \"x\" or cross inside, serving as connection points for dashed lines.\n\n*   **Along Valley View Road / Western Boundary:** A utility pole symbol is located just outside the Northwest corner of the property boundary, near the end of the property line labeled `N27°29'01\"E 96.10'`. Overhead lines connect to this pole.\n*   **On the Property:** There is a utility pole symbol located on-site, in the southern portion of the property, situated south of the main building \"SLAB\". This pole acts as a central junction point where three separate overhead lines converge.\n*   **Adjacent to Southern Boundary:** A utility pole symbol is located off-site, just south of the southern property boundary line (labeled `S63°03'28\"E 419.96'`), within the adjacent area labeled \"LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS\".\n*   **Guy Anchors:** There are symbols labeled `GUY ANCHOR` which indicate supporting infrastructure for poles:\n    *   One is located near the Southwest corner of the property, near Valley View Road.\n    *   Another is located just south of the southern property line, near the middle of the boundary.\n\n### 2. Overhead Lines\nOverhead electrical lines are depicted as dashed lines crossing the drawing.\n\n*   **Adjacent to the Property (Valley View Road):** A dashed line runs North-South along the western boundary of the property, roughly parallel to Valley View Road. It connects to the utility pole near the Northwest corner.\n*   **Crossing the Property (East-West):** A dashed line enters the property from the East, crossing the boundary line labeled `S27°19'26\"W 146.15'`. It runs Westward across the southern portion of the site, connecting to the on-site utility pole mentioned above. From this on-site pole, a line continues West across the front driveway area, connecting to the North-South line running along Valley View Road.\n*   **Crossing the Property (North-South):** A dashed line runs South from the on-site utility pole, crossing the southern property boundary (`S63°03'28\"E 419.96'`) to connect to the off-site pole located in \"LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS\".\n\n### 3. Labels and Notations\nThe following specific text labels on the drawing indicate the presence of overhead electrical facilities:\n\n*   **Line Labels:** The dashed lines described above are repeatedly labeled directly on the line itself with the text:\n    `O.H. ELECTRIC`\n*   **Easement Notations:** There are specific easements labeled on the drawing that appear to correspond with the path of the overhead electrical infrastructure in the southern portion of the site.\n    *   Near the East-West line crossing the south side of the property, a label reads:\n        `10' ELEC. EASEMENT`\n        `VOL. 6464, PG. 74`\n        `P.R.T.C.TX.`\n    *   Near the Southwest corner, adjacent to where the overhead lines run, a label reads:\n        `5' ELEC. EASEMENT`\n        `VOL. 5048, PG. 888`\n        `D.R.T.C.TX.`","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1411,"outputTokens":779,"totalTokens":5744,"reasoningTokens":3554},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the existing conditions survey and identify any overhead utility poles, overhead utility lines, or overhead electric infrastructure shown on or adjacent to the property boundaries. Specifically look for: (1) Utility poles along Valley View Road or property boundaries; (2) Overhead lines crossing the property or adjacent to it; (3) Any labels or notations indicating the presence of existing overhead electrical facilities. If overhead infrastructure is present, describe its location relative to the property and the extent to which it appears on the drawing."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-wcOzj7oGmDkVhHuXWZk6vglR","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Mon, 20 Apr 2026 16:40:04 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::wq7rp-1776703139939-413cb6022c88"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Existing Conditions Survey,\" here is a detailed report regarding overhead utility poles, lines, and electrical infrastructure on or adjacent to the property:\n\n### 1. Utility Poles\nUtility poles are indicated on the drawing by small circular symbols with an \"x\" or cross inside, serving as connection points for dashed lines.\n\n*   **Along Valley View Road / Western Boundary:** A utility pole symbol is located just outside the Northwest corner of the property boundary, near the end of the property line labeled `N27°29'01\"E 96.10'`. Overhead lines connect to this pole.\n*   **O