{"level":30,"time":1776703215532,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine this site plan carefully for the proximity of proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, fences, retaining walls, and other structures relative to the existing overhead utility lines shown along the western boundary on Valley View Road. The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows three overhead utility poles along the western property line in the right-of-way. On this site plan, identify: 1) The locations of these poles or overhead lines if visible; 2) The distance and clearance from proposed buildings to any overhead lines; 3) Any proposed driveways, parking areas, or sidewalks that might be beneath overhead lines; 4) Any proposed fences or walls near the utility poles. Provide specific details about what is proposed near the overhead lines and the apparent clearances between structures and the lines.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan image (Sheet 9 of 39), here is an analysis of the western boundary along Valley View Road regarding the existing overhead utility lines and proposed structures:\n\n**1) Locations of poles or overhead lines if visible:**\nOverhead utility lines and poles are visible along the western property line within what appears to be the Right-of-Way for Valley View Road.\n*   A dashed line labeled **\"- - OHE - -\"** (indicating Overhead Electric) runs generally parallel to the western property line along the street frontage.\n*   Near the top-left (northwest) section of the frontage, a symbol is labeled **\"AT&T Pole\"**.\n*   Near the northern proposed driveway, there is a square symbol with a circle inside, indicative of a utility pole, located just north of the driveway entrance.\n*   Near the southern proposed driveway, there is another similar pole symbol located just north of the driveway entrance, and the **\"- - OHE - -\"** line is shown crossing directly over the driveway apron.\n*   At the far bottom-left (southwest) corner, another pole symbol is visible near a line labeled **\"Guy Wire\"**.\n\n**2) Distance and clearance from proposed buildings to any overhead lines:**\nThe proposed buildings closest to the western boundary are labeled **\"Bldg. 1\"** (top left) and **\"Bldg. 8\"** (bottom left).\n*   **Distance:** The site plan provides horizontal dimensions from these buildings to the property line.\n    *   From the western edge of **\"Bldg. 1\"** to the property line, a dimension of **\"26.1'\"** is shown.\n    *   From the western edge of **\"Bldg. 8\"** to the property line, a dimension of **\"26.0'\"** is shown.\n    *   Because the **\"- - OHE - -\"** lines run outside the property line in the Right-of-Way, the horizontal distance from the buildings to the overhead lines is greater than the 26.0' - 26.1' building setbacks.\n*   **Clearance:** This is a 2D plan view. There are no vertical elevation or clearance dimensions provided on this sheet to indicate the height of the overhead lines relative to the proposed buildings.\n\n**3) Proposed driveways, parking areas, or sidewalks that might be beneath overhead lines:**\n*   **Driveways:** There are two proposed driveways on the western boundary, both labeled **\"Construct Type III Driveway See Detail 1/33-2\"**. The dashed line indicating the overhead lines (**\"- - OHE - -\"**) passes directly across the aprons of both of these proposed driveways in the Right-of-Way.\n*   **Sidewalks:** A proposed sidewalk labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 4/325-1\"** runs along the entire Valley View Road frontage. Based on the line placement, portions of this sidewalk run parallel to and likely beneath the path of the overhead utility lines.\n*   **Parking Areas:** There are no proposed parking spaces located along the western boundary beneath the overhead lines. All parking appears internal to the site, east of the proposed buildings.\n\n**4) Any proposed fences or walls near the utility poles:**\n*   **Fences:** There are no visible perimeter fence lines proposed along the Valley View Road frontage running parallel to the overhead lines.\n*   **Walls:** Near the southwest corner of the property (bottom left), adjacent to the southernmost utility pole symbol and \"Guy Wire\", there is a label pointing to a line stating **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"**. This wall begins near the property corner and runs eastward into the site, perpendicular to the road, rather than parallel beneath the lines.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1472,"outputTokens":808,"totalTokens":4738,"reasoningTokens":2458},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this site plan carefully for the proximity of proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, fences, retaining walls, and other structures relative to the existing overhead utility lines shown along the western boundary on Valley View Road. The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows three overhead utility poles along the western property line in the right-of-way. On this site plan, identify: 1) The locations of these poles or overhead lines if visible; 2) The distance and clearance from proposed buildings to any overhead lines; 3) Any proposed driveways, parking areas, or sidewalks that might be beneath overhead lines; 4) Any proposed fences or walls near the utility poles. Provide specific details about what is proposed near the overhead lines and the apparent clearances between structures and the lines."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-2U0e51wygQrEk1WflvD8QFIX","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Mon, 20 Apr 2026 16:40:15 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::npm8h-1776703186593-e06d311a20e0"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan image (Sheet 9 of 39), here is an analysis of the western boundary along Valley View Road regarding the existing overhead utility lines and proposed structures:\n\n**1) Locations of poles or overhead lines if visible:**\nOverhead utility lines and poles are visible along the western property line within what appears to be the Right-of-Way for Valley View Road.\n*   A dashed line labeled **\"- - OHE - -\"** (indicating Overhead Electric) runs generally parallel to the western property line along the street frontage.\n*   Near the top-left (northwest) section of the frontage, a symbol is labeled **\"AT&T Pole\"**.\n*   Near the northern proposed driveway, there is a square symbol with a circle inside, indicative of a utility pole, located just north of the driveway entrance.\n*   Near the southern proposed driveway, there is another similar pole symbol located just north of the driveway entrance, and the **\"- - OHE - -\"** line is shown crossing directly over the driveway apron.\n*   At the far bottom-left (southwest) corner, another pole symbol is visible near a line labeled **\"Guy Wire\"**.\n\n**2) Distance and clearance from proposed buildings to any overhead lines:**\nThe proposed buildings closest to the western boundary are labeled **\"Bldg. 1\"** (top left) and **\"Bldg. 8\"** (bottom left).\n*   **Distance:** The site plan provides horizontal dimensions from these buildings to the property line.\n    *   From the western edge of **\"Bldg. 1\"** to the property line, a dimension of **\"26.1'\"** is shown.\n    *   From the western edge of **\"Bldg. 8\"** to the property line, a dimension of **\"26.0'\"** is shown.\n    *   Because the **\"- - OHE - -\"** lines run outside the property line in the Right-of-Way, the horizontal distance from the buildings to the overhead lines is greater than the 26.0' - 26.1' building setbacks.\n*   **Clearance:** This is a 2D plan view. There are no vertical elevation or clearance dimensions provided on this sheet to indicate the height of the overhead lines relative to the proposed buildings.\n\n**3) Proposed driveways, parking areas, or sidewalks that might be beneath overhead lines:**\n*   **Driveways:** There are two proposed driveways on the western boundary, both labeled **\"Construct Type III Driveway See Detail 1/33-2\"**. The dashed line indicating the overhead lines (**\"- - OHE - -\"**) passes directly across the aprons of both of these proposed driveways in the Right-of-Way.\n*   **Sidewalks:** A proposed sidewalk labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 4/325-1\"** runs along the entire Valley View Road frontage. Based on the line placement, portions of this sidewalk run parallel to and likely beneath the path of the overhead utility lines.\n*   **Parking Areas:** There are no proposed parking spaces located along the western boundary beneath the overhead lines. All parking appears internal to the site, east of the proposed buildings.\n\n**4) Any proposed fences or walls near the utility poles:**\n*   **Fences:** There are no visible perimeter fence lines proposed along the Valley View Road frontage running parallel to the overhead lines.\n*   **Walls:** Near the southwest corner of the property (bottom left), adjacent to the southernmost utility pole symbol and \"Guy Wire\", there is a label pointing to a line stating **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"**. This wall begins near the property corner and runs eastward into the site, perpendicular to the road, rather than parallel beneath the lines.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1472,"outputTokens":808,"totalTokens":4738,"reasoningTokens":2458},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptF