{"level":30,"time":1776703449100,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159jRNtNYZNjocWXo9TCwZH","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 1 — Cover\n     2→\n     3→Cover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n    11→*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n    12→*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n    13→*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n    14→*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n    15→*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n    16→*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n    17→*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n    18→*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n    19→*   Private Hydrants: 1\n    20→*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n    25→*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n    26→*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n    27→*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n    28→*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n    29→*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n    30→*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n    31→*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n    32→*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n    33→\n    34→---\n    35→\n    36→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    37→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","uuid":"9f60adbf-bfc8-4964-bf93-073714ac349c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Cover\n\nCover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n*   Private Hydrants: 1\n*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
