{"level":30,"time":1776703449103,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the southern boundary of the site where the overhead electric (OHE) line is located.\n1. Identify each tree tag/symbol shown along the southern boundary (particularly those near the OHE line - e.g., \"M\", \"PL\", \"SY\" tags)\n2. For each tag, try to match it to the plant list. What species do each symbol represent? The legend shows:\n   - SY = Street Yard Tree\n   - PL = Parking Lot Tree\n   - P = Parking Buffer Point Tree\n   - M = Mitigation Tree\n3. Looking at the tags/symbols and the legend on this sheet and on Sheet 35, what are the specific tree species planted along the southern boundary near the OHE line?\n4. Are there any dimensions or clearance callouts shown between the trees and the OHE line?\nDescribe your findings with reference to locations on the plan (e.g., \"at the southwest corner\", \"along the south side from west to east\", etc.)","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the findings regarding the southern boundary and the overhead electric (OHE) line:\n\n**Orientation:** Based on the North arrow in the bottom right corner (pointing up), the southern boundary is the bottom edge of the plan sheet. The Overhead Electric line is designated by a dashed line labeled \"- OHE -\" running horizontally along this bottom edge, just outside the property line/Limits of Construction (LOC).\n\n**1. Identification of tree tags/symbols along the southern boundary:**\nScanning the southern boundary from West (left) to East (right), just north of the OHE line:\n*   **Southwest corner/Western half:** There are several large tree symbols that appear to represent existing trees (indicated by a crossed-circle symbol within the canopy line). One c