{"level":30,"time":1776703449104,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Examine the Existing Conditions Survey and identify:\n1. Are there utility poles marked on the survey (look for symbols indicating \"UTILITY POLE\")?\n2. Are there overhead utility lines shown (marked as \"O.H.U.L.\" or similar)?\n3. What is the spatial location of these utility poles and overhead lines relative to the property boundaries?\n4. Describe any electric easements shown on the survey\n5. Provide an overall description of the existing infrastructure and utility locations on the site.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"BOUNDARY, IMPROVEMENTS, TOPOGRAPHIC & TREE SURVEY\" document, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n### 1. Utility Poles\nYes, there are utility poles marked on the survey. According to the document's \"LEGEND\" (located in the upper-left corner of the drawing area), the symbol for a utility pole is a circle with an \"X\" inside. These symbols are present on the plan.\n\n### 2. Overhead Utility Lines\nYes, overhead utility lines are shown. The legend indicates that an \"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\" is represented by a dashed line accompanied by the text \"**O.H.U.L.**\". These dashed lines are clearly visible traversing parts of the site plan.\n\n### 3. Spatial Location of Poles and Lines Relative to Boundaries\nThe utility poles and overhead lines are primarily located near the perimeter of the property boundaries, specifically along the Northern, Eastern, and Southern edges.\n\n*   **Northern Boundary (along line labeled $S83^{\\circ}02'28''E$ $419.89'$):** A utility pole is located just outside the property line near the Northwest corner. From this general area, an \"O.H.U.L.\" runs roughly parallel to the Northern property boundary, dipping slightly inside the property line. It connects to another utility pole located near a large tree (labeled 4028) just inside the Northeast property corner.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** From the pole in the Northeast corner, the \"O.H.U.L.\" continues southward, generally following the Eastern property line.\n*   **Southern Boundary (along lines labeled $N83^{\\circ}50'57''W$ and $S26^{\\circ}15'01''W$):** There is a utility pole located just outside the property line near the Southeast corner. Overhead utility lines (\"O.H.U.L.\") connect to this pole, running roughly parallel to the Southern property boundaries.\n\n### 4. Electric Easements Shown\nThe survey indicates several electric easements located along the property perimeters, corresponding closely with the locations of the overhead utility lines.\n\n*   **Northern Boundary:** There is a dashed rectangular box indicating an easement midway along the Northern property line. The text exactly reads: \"**5' ELEC. EASEMENT / VOL. 73, PG. 76 / P.R.T.C.TX.**\"\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** There is a dashed rectangular box along the Eastern property line. The text exactly reads: \"**5' ELEC. EASEMENT / VOL. 73, PG. 76 / P.R.T.C.TX.**\"\n*   **Southern Boundary:** There is a dashed rectangular box midway along the main Southern property line. The text exactly reads: \"**5' ELEC. EASEMENT / VOL. 73, PG. 76 / P.R.T.C.TX.**\"\n*   **Southeast Corner:** There is another defined easement area near the Southeast boundary corner. The text exactly reads: \"**5' ELEC. EASEMENT / VOL. 5186, PG. 888 / D.R.T.C.TX.**\"\n\n### 5. Overall Description of Existing Infrastructure and Utilities\nThe site currently contains significant existing infrastructure.\n*   **Structures & Paving:** The center of the property is dominated by a large building footprint (indicated by outlines labeled \"SLAB\"). This structure is surrounded by extensive paved areas, marked as \"ASPHALT\" and \"CONC.\" (concrete), which appear to be parking lots and driveways.\n*   **Access:** The main access to the site is from \"**VALLEY VIEW ROAD**\" on the Western boundary, featuring a concrete drive entrance.\n*   **General Utilities:** In addition to the perimeter overhead electrical lines, other utilities are present. A water meter (symbol 'W' in a box) is located near the entrance on Valley View Road. Clean-outs (symbol 'CO') and a gas meter (symbol 'G' in a box) are located immediately adjacent to the main central building. Air conditioning units (\"A/C\") are also marked on pads next to the building.\n*   **Other Features:** Various fences (wood privacy, rock wall, chain link) run along portions of the property boundaries and within the site. A retaining wall is noted near the Eastern/Southeastern boundary.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1417,"outputTokens":956,"totalTokens":4854,"reasoningTokens":2481},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\