l Feature Identification\n\n**(1) Buildings, Parking Areas, Driveways, and Fire Lanes**\n*   **Buildings**: There are 8 separate multi-family structures denoted as \"Bldg. 1\" through \"Bldg. 8\". They are arranged centrally, primarily in two north-south groupings. Individual units are labeled inside the footprints (e.g., \"Unit 101\", \"Unit 202\"). \n*   **Driveways & Fire Lanes**: Vehicular access is located on the western boundary via two distinct entrance points, both labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway\". The northern and southern entry points feature \"Access Gates\" and lead into an internal, looping \"Concrete Drive\" equipped with \"Curb & Gutter (Typ)\" and \"Ribbon Curb\". This loop circulates traffic between the rows of buildings.\n*   **Parking**: The plan does not show vast open parking lots; instead, parking is integrated into the residential units. The Parking Data table notes \"16 Surface / 76 Garage\" spaces. The diagram shows small concrete pads immediately adjacent to the building units, indicating driveway and garage access directly off the internal loop.\n\n**(2) Detention Pond and Retaining Walls**\n*   **Detention Pond**: A large \"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\" is located in the northeast corner of the site. It is bordered by a \"Pond Perimeter Fence\".\n*   **Retaining Walls**: The pond is structurally supported by walls labeled \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"End Concrete Retaining Wall\". The eastern property line features an \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\". The southern boundary features a complex wall system labeled: \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" that transitions into \"End Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n\n**(3) Tree Locations**\n*   Trees are represented by irregular scalloped circular symbols. Many trees feature a dashed outer circle, representing the Critical Root Zone (noted textually in the \"Fence Note\" as \"Critical Root Zone (CRZ)\").\