d outer circle, representing the Critical Root Zone (noted textually in the \"Fence Note\" as \"Critical Root Zone (CRZ)\").\n*   The trees are primarily preserved along the outer buffer zones of the property (north, south, and east boundaries). Scattered clusters also exist internally, such as the open spaces between the driveway loops, and bordering the pedestrian pathways.\n\n**(4) Property Boundaries and Easements**\n*   **Boundaries**: The property perimeter is marked by a heavy, dashed-and-dotted line with bearings (e.g., \"N 62° 02' 28\" E\", \"S 28° 35' 57\" W\"). \n*   **Easements**: Multiple easements line the perimeter. Identified text includes:\n    *   Western boundary: \"Wastewater Easement Doc#...\" and \"Sidewalk Easement Doc#...\"\n    *   Northeast/East boundary near pond: \"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n    *   Eastern boundary: \"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" and \"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 2011021137 O.P.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n    *   Southern boundary area: \"Electric Easement...\"\n\n**(5) Sidewalks and Pedestrian Pathways**\n*   **Exterior**: A pathway labeled \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk\" spans the outer western frontage along the public right-of-way.\n*   **Interior Concrete**: Sidewalks labeled \"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ)\" weave through the internal development, running parallel to the driveways and directly connecting the front entrances of the townhomes.\n*   **Decomposed Granite**: In the northern section, bordering Buildings 1 and 3 near the pond, there are pathways labeled \"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\".\n\n### 3. General Site Layout Overview\nThe site layout demonstrates a highly structured central core optimized for residential development, surrounded by open spaces and environmental controls on the perimeter. The developed area (impervious cover) consists of the 8 multi-family buildings and the internal concrete driveway loop, densely clustered in the western and central portions of the site. \n\nThe eastern and northern perimeters are primarily designated as open space and infrastructure buffers. The northeast quadrant is entirely dedicated to stormwater management (the detention pond), while the remaining boundaries (north, east, and south) feature significant tree preservation areas and structural retaining walls that mediate the transition between the site's grading and neighboring properties. The pedestrian pathways act as transitional zones, shifting from concrete within the dense central development to decomposed granite near the open, naturalized pond area.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":2295524.837909,"endTime":2376534.690315,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"vVbmad7iJ4ye-7UPxcujwA4"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.129604","marketCost":"0.129604","inferenceCost":"0.129604","inputInferenceCost":"0.002812","outputInferenceCost":"0.126792","generationId":"gen_01KPNW5M2TC89KS009R30EBMRH"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
