{"level":30,"time":1776703458823,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QhdgDBoqQYQMP9WmkYHnrW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sheet 37 contains general landscaping details (tree protection, tree planting, shrub planting) but doesn't specify which tree species go where on the site. \n\nNow I need to use a different approach. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees with specific tags/symbols (SY, PL, M, P). From Sheet 35, I know:\n- Shade Trees: Live Oak (2) and Cedar Elm (10) - shown with specific symbols\n- Ornamental Trees: Texas Mountain Laurel (2) and Mexican Redbud (6) - shown with specific symbols\n\nBut I need to know WHERE these trees are located on the plan. The key information from the vision analysis is that along the southern boundary near the OHE line, there are trees marked with \"M\" (mitigation trees) and \"PL\" (parking lot trees).\n\nFrom Sheet 35, the mitigation trees that count towards mitigation are:\n- Existing trees being preserved (various species)\n- The proposed 12 shade trees (2 Live Oak + 10 Cedar Elm) which provide 68 inches (counted as B)\n- Less required trees = 55 mitigation inches\n\nSo the 12 proposed shade trees are the primary new plantings. I need to check:\n1. Are these trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm) utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F?\n2. What are their mature heights?\n3. Are they being planted within restricted zones from the overhead electric line?\n\nLet me check the grouping again for ECM Appendix F information and search for any documents that reference this appendix. But first, I should also check Sheet 21 (Electrical) more closely to see if there's any information about the utility infrastructure and any coordination notes about tree clearances.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details"