compatible trees are marked with \"UC\" in ECM Appendix F\n\n\n- Cedar Elm appears to be utility-compatible as a common utility tree\n- Mexican Redbud is likely utility-compatible given its smaller stature\n- Texas Mountain Laurel reaches 25 feet at maturity and is specifically designated as utility-compatible\n- Live Oak's utility compatibility depends on its UC designation in the appendix\n\nI need to verify which of these proposed species actually qualify as utility-compatible and confirm their mature heights to ensure compliance with the overhead electric line constraints. lines are shown but the clearances aren't dimensioned. Looking back at the requirement for EL-2.14, the trees are actually depicted on the plan in relation to the overhead facilities, so that's not the issue. What I need to do is identify those three \"M\" trees in the southeast corner, verify their utility compatibility and mature heights, then measure distances to confirm they're violating clearance standards. The vision analysis already indicates the problem—the canopy circles for these three trees are drawn directly overlapping the overhead electric line on the plan itself, which appears to be a clear violation shown visually.\n\nTo confirm this, I should measure the actual spacing between the trees and the line or check if the plan specifies the species and mature heights needed to assess utility compatibility.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_read_input_tokens":53510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"cee9abf1-d821-4c94-9537-6c1ad9d5cc0a"}
