{"level":30,"time":1776703478580,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan drawing and identify any reference to existing or proposed overhead electric lines, poles, conductors, clearances, or electric easements shown. Specifically: (1) Are overhead electric lines shown on the site plan? (2) Are overhead electric poles or structures shown? (3) Are electric easements marked or labeled? (4) Are there dimension lines or clearance annotations related to overhead electric facilities? (5) How do the proposed buildings, parking areas, driveways, and other features relate spatially to any shown overhead infrastructure?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the details regarding overhead electric infrastructure, broken down by your specific questions:\n\n**(1) Are overhead electric lines shown on the site plan?**\nYes. An overhead electric line is clearly denoted by a linetype containing \"**- OHE -**\" running horizontally across the entire bottom (southern) boundary of the site plan, along the right-of-way/property edge. \n\n**(2) Are overhead electric poles or structures shown?**\nYes. Along the \"**- OHE -**\" line at the bottom of the plan, there are several circular symbols with a dot in the center, which typically denote utility poles supporting the overhead lines. While not explicitly labeled with the word \"pole,\" they are integrated directly into the overhead electric line path (one near the bottom-left driveway entrance, one near the bottom-center, and one towards the bottom-right).\n\n**(3) Are electric easements marked or labeled?**\nYes, specific electric easements are labeled with exact text in several locations:\n*   On the far right (eastern) boundary edge, there is a label stating: \"**5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n*   Near the bottom right corner (inside the property boundary), there is another label pointing to an easement line: \"**5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n*   Just outside the bottom right property line, there is a label stating: \"**5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n*   Additionally, Public Utility Easements (P.U.E.) are noted, such as a \"**5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" along the top (northern) boundary.\n\n**(4) Are there dimension lines or clearance annotations related to overhead electric facilities?**\nNo. There are no vertical drop clearance annotations, radial clearance zones, or specific setback dimensions labeled as being measured directly to or from the overhead electric lines or poles shown on this sheet. \n\n**(5) How do the proposed buildings, parking areas, driveways, and other features relate spatially to any shown overhead infrastructure?**\n*   **Buildings:** The proposed buildings closest to the overhead electric line are \"**Bldg. 7**\" and \"**Bldg. 8**\" in the southern portion of the site. They are set back from the southern property line and the \"**- OHE -**\" line. \n*   **Separation:** A \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall**\" and an area of landscaping/open space physically separate the building pads from the boundary line where the overhead electric runs.\n*   **Driveways:** The proposed entrance driveway on the bottom left (labeled \"**Construct Type III Driveway**\") extends southward out to the main road, meaning vehicular traffic will pass directly under or closely adjacent to the \"**- OHE -**\" line path at the site's ingress/egress point.\n*   **Parking:** All parking areas and internal drives are located internal to the site (north of the retaining walls) and do not appear to directly conflict with the overhead line path on the southern boundary.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1418,"outputTokens":759,"totalTokens":4609,"reasoningTokens":2432},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan drawing and identify any reference to existing or proposed overhead electric lines, poles, conductors, clearances, or electric easements shown. Specifically: (1) Are overhead electric lines shown on the site plan? (2) Are overhead electric poles or structures shown? (3) Are electric easements marked or labeled? (4) Are there dimension lines or clearance annotations related to overhead electric facilities? (5) How do the proposed buildings, parking areas, driveways, a