{"level":30,"time":1776703481036,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Can you identify: 1) The location of the overhead electric line (OHE) shown on the landscape plan; 2) The location and distance of trees (indicated by circles or tree symbols) in relation to the OHE line; 3) Which trees (if any) are planted within 10 feet lateral distance of the overhead electric conductor; 4) Are there any annotations or distance callouts showing clearances between trees and the OHE line?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here is the information regarding the overhead electric line (OHE) and the trees:\n\n1)  **Location of the overhead electric line (OHE):**\n    *   The overhead electric line is located along the bottom edge (southern boundary, based on the North arrow) of the site plan. It is represented by a continuous line periodically interrupted by the text **\"-OHE-\"**.\n\n2)  **Location and distance of trees in relation to the OHE line:**\n    *   There is a row of proposed trees (indicated by circular canopies with central crosshairs) planted along the same bottom (southern) boundary of the site.\n    *   The **\"-OHE-\"** line appears to run directly over or immediately adjacent to the center points (trunks) of this entire row of trees.\n\n3)  **Trees planted within 10 feet lateral distance of the OHE:**\n    *   Based on visual estimation using the provided graphic scale (**\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"**), the entire row of trees located along the southern property boundary appears to be planted well within a 10-foot lateral distance of the overhead electric conductor. In several instances, the center crosshair of the tree symbol lies directly on top of the **\"-OHE-\"** line.\n\n4)  **Annotations or distance callouts showing clearances:**\n    *   There are **no** annotations, dimension lines, or distance callouts provided on this plan that indicate the specific lateral clearance or distance between the proposed trees and the OHE line.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1405,"outputTokens":337,"totalTokens":3430,"reasoningTokens":1688},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Can you identify: 1) The location of the overhead electric line (OHE) shown on the landscape plan; 2) The location and distance of trees (indicated by circles or tree symbols) in relation to the OHE line; 3) Which trees (if any) are planted within 10 feet lateral distance of the overhead electric conductor; 4) Are there any annotations or distance callouts showing clearances between trees and the OHE line?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-U772qNcHuR1r2kNp7nAa2sWN","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Mon, 20 Apr 2026 16:44:41 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::sq978-1776703461612-5054fdf21063"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here is the information regarding the overhead electric line (OHE) and the trees:\n\n1)  **Location of the overhead electric line (OHE):**\n    *   The overhead electric line is located along the bottom edge (southern boundary, based on the North arrow) of the site plan. It is represented by a continuous line periodically interrupted by the text **\"-OHE-\"**.\n\n2)  **Location and distance of trees in relation to the OHE line:**\n    *   There is a row of proposed trees (indicated by circular canopies with central crosshairs) planted along the same bottom (southern) boundary of the 