{"level":30,"time":1776703488708,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and identify:\n1. Are there any OVERHEAD electric lines or poles shown on this site plan? Describe their location if present.\n2. What underground electrical infrastructure is shown (transformers, pull boxes, conduits, lines)? Where are they located?\n3. Are there any notes or callouts referencing overhead electric utilities, tree clearances, or coordination with the landscape plan?\n4. What does the note at Block 5 say about \"Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule\"? What specific reference is made about trees?\n5. Based on this electrical plan, is overhead distribution expected on this site, or are all utilities underground?\nPlease be specific about locations and any text visible in notes or legends.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), here are the details addressing your questions:\n\n**1. Are there any OVERHEAD electric lines or poles shown on this site plan? Describe their location if present.**\nYes, there are overhead electric lines indicated. Along the far left (west) property boundary edge, near the street frontage and parallel to the \"Sidewalk Easement,\" there is a dashed line periodically labeled with \"- OHE -\". This indicates an existing overhead electric line running along the perimeter of the site.\n\n**2. What underground electrical infrastructure is shown (transformers, pull boxes, conduits, lines)? Where are they located?**\nThe site's interior electrical distribution is shown using solid blue lines with specific blue callout boxes. The following infrastructure is explicitly labeled:\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Solid blue lines routed throughout the site's interior driveways and connecting the infrastructure. One explicit callout for this is located on the left side of the plan, pointing to the line running between the main entrance and Bldg. 2/Bldg. 8.\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Indicated by rectangular symbols. These are located in several places, including: west of Bldg. 1, south of Bldg. 2, south of Bldg. 8, and on the east side between Bldg. 5 and Bldg. 6.\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Indicated by circular/hexagonal symbols with an \"E\" inside. These are distributed frequently along the underground lines, especially at junction points and near buildings (e.g., near Bldg. 1, Bldg. 4, Bldg. 7, etc.).\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Indicated by small square symbols attached to the sides of the residential buildings (e.g., explicitly called out at Bldg. 1, Bldg. 3, Bldg. 4, Bldg. 2, Bldg. 7, and Bldg. 6).\n\n**3. Are there any notes or callouts referencing overhead electric utilities, tree clearances, or coordination with the landscape plan?**\nThere are no dedicated notes or standard text blocks explicitly detailing radial \"clearance\" distances from the overhead utilities on this specific sheet. However, there is coordination with the landscape plan explicitly called out regarding trees. In the bottom-left area of the drawing, there is a box titled **\"Tree List\"** that references coordination with the landscape plan (detailed in the next answer).\n\n**4. What does the note at Block 5 say about \"Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule\"? What specific reference is made about trees?**\n*(Note: These specific notes are located in boxed sections at the bottom-left of the page, rather than adjacent to \"Bldg. 5\" which is on the right side of the plan).*\nThe exact transcriptions of these boxes are:\n\n*   **Tree List Note:**\n    Title: \"Tree List\"\n    Text: \"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"\n\n*   **Geologist Mitigation Rule Note:**\n    Title: \"Note\"\n    Text: \"This project is subject to the Voids and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM); provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\"\n\n**5. Based on this electrical plan, is overhead distribution expected on this site, or are all utilities underground?**\nBased on this plan, the primary electrical distribution for the interior of the development site is expected to be **underground**. While existing \"- OHE -\" (overhead) lines are shown on the perimeter street boundary, all new infrastructure routing power to the actual buildings inside the property line consists of solid blue lines explicitly labeled as **\"Underground Electric Line\"** that connect to pad-mounted transformers and pull boxes.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1468,"outputTokens":835,"totalTokens":4298,"reasoningTokens":1995},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page do