le to definitively confirm if they fall exactly within 10 lateral feet, though graphically they appear to be planted directly adjacent to or beneath the line.\n\n**(3) Whether any tree species are labeled and can be verified as utility-compatible (UC) species:**\nNo specific tree species (e.g., Oak, Elm, Crape Myrtle) are labeled on this plan, nor are there any annotations indicating that the trees are \"utility-compatible\" (UC). \nThe trees on the plan are labeled with abbreviation codes inside circles (e.g., \"SY\", \"M\", \"PL\"). The legend located below the \"KEY NOTES\" section defines these codes based on their zoning or mitigation purpose, not species:\n*   **\"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**\n*   **\"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**\n*   **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"**\n*   **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**\n\n**(4) Whether there are clearance annotations or setbacks shown from the overhead line to landscaping:**\nThere are no clearance annotations, setback dimensions, or notes shown on the plan that indicate a required distance between the overhead electric line (\"- OHE -\") and the proposed trees or landscaping.\n\n**(5) Any sprinkler or irrigation system components shown near the overhead line:**\nNo physical sprinkler or irrigation system components (such as pipes, valves, or sprinkler heads) are drawn on the plan, either near the overhead line or elsewhere on the site. \nWhile there is a detailed **\"IRRIGATION NOTES:\"** section in the top left corner that outlines requirements (stating, for example, \"AUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344...\"), the physical layout of the irrigation system is not depicted on this specific sheet, which is titled \"LANDSCAPE PLAN\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1412,"outputTokens":672,"totalTokens":4151,"reasoningTokens":2067}