haded grey area runs parallel to the western property line, positioned between the property line/sidewalk and the paved parking areas. The proposed trees are situated within or immediately adjacent to this shaded strip.\n\n**3) Look for any text labels, callouts, or symbols indicating tree species or planting details.**\n*   **Tree Labels:** The two prominent, spaced-out tree symbols in the middle section of the western boundary each contain a small circular label directly adjacent to their center cross. Both labels contain the exact text **\"SYM\"**. There is no plant schedule or legend provided on this specific sheet that defines what \"SYM\" represents in terms of species.\n*   **Area Callouts:** There are specific callout bubbles pointing to the shaded grey landscaping area along this western boundary:\n    *   A callout bubble labeled **\"H.2\"** points to the shaded area between the two middle trees. According to the \"KEY NOTES\" legend, \"H.2\" represents **\"STREET YARD\"**.\n    *   Callout bubbles labeled **\"H.4\"** point to portions of this shaded area near the top left corner. According to the \"KEY NOTES\" legend, \"H.4\" represents **\"PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\"**.\n    *   A callout bubble labeled **\"H.1\"** points to the boundary edge near the top left. The legend indicates \"H.1\" is **\"PROPOSED PAVING\"**.\n\n**4) Are there any hedges, shrubs, or other planting features shown near the sidewalk and driveway approaches?**\nAside from the large proposed trees and the overall shaded areas designated as \"STREET YARD\" and \"PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\", there are no distinct line types, symbols, or specific text callouts explicitly indicating individual shrubs, hedges, or smaller planting features near the sidewalk or the driveway approaches on the western frontage.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1450,"outputTokens":589,"totalTokens":4360,"reasoningTokens":2321},"warnings":[],"reque