{"level":30,"time":1776704542836,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KcAF3jwZCypCKXdjxtg7nG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 22 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 439S-1 for Parking Lot Bumper Curb. It shows plan, longitudinal section, and cross-section views of a concrete bumper curb.\n     4→\n     5→CITY OF AUSTIN\n     6→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n     7→PARKING LOT BUMPER CURB\n     8→STANDARD NO.\n     9→439S-1\n    10→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 3/15/06\n    11→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n    12→ADOPTED\n    13→\n    14→[Drawing showing plan view of parking lot bumper curb with dimensions and reinforcement.]\n    15→PLAN\n    16→\n    17→[Drawing showing longitudinal section view of parking lot bumper curb with dimensions and reinforcement.]\n    18→LONGITUDINAL SECTION\n    19→\n    20→[Drawing showing cross-section view of parking lot bumper curb with dimensions and reinforcement.]\n    21→CROSS SECTION\n    22→ALL CONCRETE SHALL BE CLASS \"A\" IN ACCORDANCE WITH ITEM 403S.\n    23→\n    24→## Block 2: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 710S-4 for Bicycle Rack Installation in Concrete Sidewalk-Alternate 1. It shows a basic installation drawing and a detailed installation drawing.\n    25→\n    26→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    27→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n    28→BICYCLE RACK INSTALLATION IN CONCRETE SIDEWALK-ALTERNATE 1\n    29→STANDARD NO.\n    30→710S-4\n    31→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY COUNG TRAN 09/26/12\n    32→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n    33→ADOPTED\n    34→\n    35→[Drawing showing basic installation of a bicycle rack in a concrete sidewalk.]\n    36→BASIC INSTALLATION\n    37→\n    38→[Drawing showing installation detail of a bicycle rack with expansion anchor bolts and lock nuts.]\n    39→INSTALLATION DETAIL\n    40→\n    41→GENERAL NOTES:\n    42→1. RACKS SHALL COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-1 OR 710S-2.\n    43→2. RACK PLACEMENT SHALL COMPLY WITH APPLICABLE CITY STANDARD DETAILS 710S-6A, 710S-6B, OR 710S-6C AND IN COMPLIANCE WITH CITY OF AUSTIN CODE SECTION 25-6-477 OR ITS SUCCESSOR.\n    44→*TO PREVENT THEFT OF BICYCLE RACK OR BIKES, EXPOSED BOLTS MUST BE DEFORMED AND NUTS RE-TIGHTENED TO PREVENT THEM FROM BEING EASILY UNTHREADED. NUTS SHOULD BE TESTED TO ENSURE THAT THEY CANNOT BE EASILY REMOVED AFTER DEFORMATION.\n    45→\n    46→## Block 3: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 710S-6C for Furnishing Location in 12' Wide or Less Sidewalks - Bicycle Rack Detail. It shows linear and parallel rack installation requirements.\n    47→\n    48→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    49→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n    50→FURNISHING LOCATION IN 12' WIDE OR LESS SIDEWALKS - BICYCLE RACK DETAIL\n    51→STANDARD NO.\n    52→710S-6C\n    53→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY COUNG TRAN 9/26/12\n    54→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n    55→ADOPTED\n    56→\n    57→[Drawing showing linear rack installation with dimensions and spacing requirements.]\n    58→LINEAR RACK INSTALLATION\n    59→DEDICATED FOOT PRINT: RACK SPACING AND DISTANCE TO WALL OR CURB\n    60→\n    61→[Drawing showing parallel rack installation with dimensions and spacing requirements.]\n    62→PARALLEL RACK INSTALLATION\n    63→DEDICATED FOOT PRINT: RACK SPACING AND DISTANCE TO WALL OR CURB\n    64→\n    65→GENERAL NOTES:\n    66→1. RACK MUST COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-1 OR 710S-2.\n    67→2. RACK INSTALLATION MUST COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-3, 710S-4, OR 710S-5.\n    68→3. BIKE RACKS MUST BE PLACED IN COMPLIANCE WITH CITY OF AUSTIN CODE SECTION 25-6-477 OR ITS SUCCESSOR.\n    69→4. BIKE RACKS MUST BE LOCATED WITHIN 7.32m (24') OF EITHER THE MAIN BUILDING ENTRY OR THE ENTRY TO THE PRIMARY LOCAL USE.\n    70→5. BIKE RACKS MUST BE PLACED PERPENDICULAR TO THE CURB WITH THE CENTERLINE OF THE RACK IN LINE WITH ANY ADJACENT TREES OR LIGHT POLES.\n    71→6. THE MINIMUM CLEARANCE BETWEEN BICYCLE RACK AND ANY PUBLIC OR PRIVATE UTILITY APPURTENANCE MUST BE 0.9m (3').\n    72→7. BIKE RACKS MAY NOT BE MOUNTED ON TOP OF VAULTS OR STORM DRAIN INLETS.\n    73→\n    74→## Block 4: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 710S-1 for Class III Style Bicycle Parking. It shows front and top views of a bicycle rack with base plate details.\n    75→\n    76→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    77→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n    78→CLASS III STYLE BICYCLE PARKING\n    79→STANDARD NO.\n    80→710S-1\n    81→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY COUNG TRAN 09/26/12\n    82→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n    83→ADOPTED\n    84→\n    85→[Drawing showing front view of a bicycle rack with dimensions and base plate detail.]\n    86→FRONT VIEW\n    87→\n    88→[Drawing showing top view of a bicycle rack base plate with dimensions and hole locations.]\n    89→TOP VIEW\n    90→\n    91→[Drawing showing alternate base plate details (circular or oval).]\n    92→ALT. BASE PLATE DETAIL (CIRCULAR OR OVAL PLATE)\n    93→\n    94→GENERAL NOTES:\n    95→1. RACK INSTALLATION METHOD SHALL COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-3, 710S-4, OR 710S-5.\n    96→2. RACK PLACEMENT SHALL COMPLY WITH APPLICABLE CITY STANDARD DETAILS 710S-6A, 710S-6B, OR 710S-6C AND CITY OF AUSTIN CODE SECTION 25-6-477 OR ITS SUCCESSOR.\n    97→3. BASE PLATES TO BE 6.35 mm (1/4\") PLATES, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 LOW CARBON PRIME STEEL.\n    98→\n    99→## Block 5: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 432S-1 for Sidewalk. It shows details for sidewalks over utility service lines.\n   100→\n   101→CITY OF AUSTIN\n   102→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n   103→SIDEWALK\n   104→STANDARD NO.\n   105→432S-1\n   106→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 03/26/08\n   107→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n   108→ADOPTED\n   109→\n   110→[Drawing showing plan view of sidewalk over utility service line, including expansion joint locations and dimensions.]\n   111→SIDEWALK OVER UTILITY SERVICE LINE PLAN\n   112→\n   113→[Drawing showing section view of sidewalk over utility service line, including concrete thickness, sand cushion, and pipe sleeve.]\n   114→SECTION OF SIDEWALK OVER UTILITY SERVICE LINES\n   115→NOTES: \n   116→1. THIS STANDARD APPLIES TO THE INSTALLATION OF NEW UTILITIES OR UTILITIES BEING REPLACED BY A NEW LINE.\n   117→2. NO JOINTS IN UTILITY SERVICE PIPE TO BE LOCATED INSIDE PVC PIPE SLEEVE.\n   118→\n   119→## Block 6: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type I Driveway. It shows plan and section views with slope requirements.\n   120→\n   121→CITY OF AUSTIN\n   122→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n   123→TYPE I DRIVEWAY\n   124→STANDARD NO.\n   125→433S-2\n   126→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY CUONG TRAN 02/24/10\n   127→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n   128→ADOPTED\n   129→\n   130→[Drawing showing plan view of Type I driveway with curb and gutter, including dimensions and slope requirements.]\n   131→PLAN\n   132→NOTE: ALL DRIVEWAYS SHALL BE SLOPED TOWARDS THE STREET FROM THE R.O.W. LINE. ELEVATION OF POINT(S) ABOVE POINT(S) G IS TYPICALLY A MINIMUM OF 150 mm (6\") PLUS 20 mm/m (2\"/100') OVER DISTANCE \"X\" IN METERS (FEET).\n   133→\n   134→[Drawing showing cross-section of Type I driveway with dimensions and slope requirements.]\n   135→CROSS SECTION\n   136→\n   137→## Block 7: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 430S-3 for Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail. It includes an elevation and section view of the dowel detail.\n   138→\n   139→CITY OF AUSTIN\n   140→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n   141→CURB EXPANSION JOINT DOWEL DETAIL\n   142→STANDARD NO.\n   143→430S-3\n   144→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY LINO RIVERA 3/29/99\n   145→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n   146→ADOPTED\n   147→\n   148→[Drawing showing curb expansion joint dowel detail with dimensions and material specifications.]\n   149→CURB EXPANSION JOINT DOWEL DETAIL\n   150→\n   151→[Drawing showing section A-A of the dowel detail with dimensions.]\n   152→SECTION A-A\n   153→SEE STANDARD 432S-1 FOR TYPICAL CURB AND GUTTER SECTIONS.\n   154→\n   155→## Block 9: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 432S-1 for Sidewalk. It shows a plan and section view of a sidewalk with curb and gutter.\n   156→\n   157→CITY OF AUSTIN\n   158→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n   159→SIDEWALK\n   160→STANDARD NO.\n   161→432S-1\n   162→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 03/26/08\n   163→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n   164→ADOPTED\n   165→\n   166→[Drawing showing plan view of sidewalk with curb and gutter, including dimensions and joint locations.]\n   167→PLAN\n   168→\n   169→[Drawing showing section view of sidewalk with curb and gutter, including dimensions and reinforcement requirements.]\n   170→SECTION\n   171→NOTES: POLYPROPYLENE FIBRILLATED FIBERS, OR 152 mm X 152 mm X MW 9 X MW 9 WWM (6\"X 6\"X W1.4 X W1.4) WELDED WIRE FABRIC OR ONE LAYER 10M (#3) BARS PLACED NOT MORE THAN 450 mm (18\") C.C. BOTH DIRECTIONS. REINFORCEMENT SHALL ACCURATELY PLACED AT SLAB MID-DEPTH AND HELD FIRMLY IN PLACE BY MEANS OF BAR SUPPORTS OF ADEQUATE STRENGTH AND NUMBER THAT WILL PREVENT DISPLACEMENT AND KEEP THE STEEL AT ITS PROPER ELEVATION DURING THE PLACEMENT OF THE P.C. CONCRETE. IN NO INSTANCE SHALL THE STEEL BE PLACED DIRECTLY ON THE SUBGRADE OR SAND CUSHION LAYER.\n   172→\n   173→## Block 10: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 430S-1 for Curb and Gutter Section. It shows the dimensions and specifications for a laydown curb and catch curb.\n   174→\n   175→CITY OF AUSTIN\n   176→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n   177→CURB AND GUTTER SECTION\n   178→STANDARD NO.\n   179→430S-1\n   180→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY LINO RIVERA 3/29/99\n   181→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n   182→ADOPTED\n   183→\n   184→[Drawing showing laydown curb section with dimensions R1, R2, R3, R4, and slope requirements.]\n   185→LAYDOWN CURB\n   186→\n   187→[Drawing showing catch curb section with dimensions R1, R2, R3, R4, and slope requirements.]\n   188→CATCH\n   189→\n   190→## Block 11: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 432S-1 for Sidewalk. It shows a dowel detail for sidewalk expansion joints.\n   191→\n   192→CITY OF AUSTIN\n   193→DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\n   194→SIDEWALK\n   195→STANDARD NO.\n   196→432S-1\n   197→RECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 03/26/08\n   198→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\n   199→ADOPTED\n   200→\n   201→[Drawing showing dowel detail for sidewalk expansion joint, including dimensions and material specifications.]\n   202→DOWEL DETAIL\n   203→\n   204→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","uuid":"4bbe411f-81e4-468c-a21a-29e7f95fb784","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-22/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 22 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 439S-1 for Parking Lot Bumper Curb. It shows plan, longitudinal section, and cross-section views of a concrete bumper curb.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nPARKING LOT BUMPER CURB\nSTANDARD NO.\n439S-1\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 3/15/06\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing plan view of parking lot bumper curb with dimensions and reinforcement.]\nPLAN\n\n[Drawing showing longitudinal section view of parking lot bumper curb with dimensions and reinforcement.]\nLONGITUDINAL SECTION\n\n[Drawing showing cross-section view of parking lot bumper curb with dimensions and reinforcement.]\nCROSS SECTION\nALL CONCRETE SHALL BE CLASS \"A\" IN ACCORDANCE WITH ITEM 403S.\n\n## Block 2: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 710S-4 for Bicycle Rack Installation in Concrete Sidewalk-Alternate 1. It shows a basic installation drawing and a detailed installation drawing.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nBICYCLE RACK INSTALLATION IN CONCRETE SIDEWALK-ALTERNATE 1\nSTANDARD NO.\n710S-4\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY COUNG TRAN 09/26/12\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing basic installation of a bicycle rack in a concrete sidewalk.]\nBASIC INSTALLATION\n\n[Drawing showing installation detail of a bicycle rack with expansion anchor bolts and lock nuts.]\nINSTALLATION DETAIL\n\nGENERAL NOTES:\n1. RACKS SHALL COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-1 OR 710S-2.\n2. RACK PLACEMENT SHALL COMPLY WITH APPLICABLE CITY STANDARD DETAILS 710S-6A, 710S-6B, OR 710S-6C AND IN COMPLIANCE WITH CITY OF AUSTIN CODE SECTION 25-6-477 OR ITS SUCCESSOR.\n*TO PREVENT THEFT OF BICYCLE RACK OR BIKES, EXPOSED BOLTS MUST BE DEFORMED AND NUTS RE-TIGHTENED TO PREVENT THEM FROM BEING EASILY UNTHREADED. NUTS SHOULD BE TESTED TO ENSURE THAT THEY CANNOT BE EASILY REMOVED AFTER DEFORMATION.\n\n## Block 3: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 710S-6C for Furnishing Location in 12' Wide or Less Sidewalks - Bicycle Rack Detail. It shows linear and parallel rack installation requirements.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nFURNISHING LOCATION IN 12' WIDE OR LESS SIDEWALKS - BICYCLE RACK DETAIL\nSTANDARD NO.\n710S-6C\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY COUNG TRAN 9/26/12\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing linear rack installation with dimensions and spacing requirements.]\nLINEAR RACK INSTALLATION\nDEDICATED FOOT PRINT: RACK SPACING AND DISTANCE TO WALL OR CURB\n\n[Drawing showing parallel rack installation with dimensions and spacing requirements.]\nPARALLEL RACK INSTALLATION\nDEDICATED FOOT PRINT: RACK SPACING AND DISTANCE TO WALL OR CURB\n\nGENERAL NOTES:\n1. RACK MUST COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-1 OR 710S-2.\n2. RACK INSTALLATION MUST COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-3, 710S-4, OR 710S-5.\n3. BIKE RACKS MUST BE PLACED IN COMPLIANCE WITH CITY OF AUSTIN CODE SECTION 25-6-477 OR ITS SUCCESSOR.\n4. BIKE RACKS MUST BE LOCATED WITHIN 7.32m (24') OF EITHER THE MAIN BUILDING ENTRY OR THE ENTRY TO THE PRIMARY LOCAL USE.\n5. BIKE RACKS MUST BE PLACED PERPENDICULAR TO THE CURB WITH THE CENTERLINE OF THE RACK IN LINE WITH ANY ADJACENT TREES OR LIGHT POLES.\n6. THE MINIMUM CLEARANCE BETWEEN BICYCLE RACK AND ANY PUBLIC OR PRIVATE UTILITY APPURTENANCE MUST BE 0.9m (3').\n7. BIKE RACKS MAY NOT BE MOUNTED ON TOP OF VAULTS OR STORM DRAIN INLETS.\n\n## Block 4: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 710S-1 for Class III Style Bicycle Parking. It shows front and top views of a bicycle rack with base plate details.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nCLASS III STYLE BICYCLE PARKING\nSTANDARD NO.\n710S-1\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY COUNG TRAN 09/26/12\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing front view of a bicycle rack with dimensions and base plate detail.]\nFRONT VIEW\n\n[Drawing showing top view of a bicycle rack base plate with dimensions and hole locations.]\nTOP VIEW\n\n[Drawing showing alternate base plate details (circular or oval).]\nALT. BASE PLATE DETAIL (CIRCULAR OR OVAL PLATE)\n\nGENERAL NOTES:\n1. RACK INSTALLATION METHOD SHALL COMPLY WITH CITY STANDARD DETAIL 710S-3, 710S-4, OR 710S-5.\n2. RACK PLACEMENT SHALL COMPLY WITH APPLICABLE CITY STANDARD DETAILS 710S-6A, 710S-6B, OR 710S-6C AND CITY OF AUSTIN CODE SECTION 25-6-477 OR ITS SUCCESSOR.\n3. BASE PLATES TO BE 6.35 mm (1/4\") PLATES, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 LOW CARBON PRIME STEEL.\n\n## Block 5: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 432S-1 for Sidewalk. It shows details for sidewalks over utility service lines.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nSIDEWALK\nSTANDARD NO.\n432S-1\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 03/26/08\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing plan view of sidewalk over utility service line, including expansion joint locations and dimensions.]\nSIDEWALK OVER UTILITY SERVICE LINE PLAN\n\n[Drawing showing section view of sidewalk over utility service line, including concrete thickness, sand cushion, and pipe sleeve.]\nSECTION OF SIDEWALK OVER UTILITY SERVICE LINES\nNOTES: \n1. THIS STANDARD APPLIES TO THE INSTALLATION OF NEW UTILITIES OR UTILITIES BEING REPLACED BY A NEW LINE.\n2. NO JOINTS IN UTILITY SERVICE PIPE TO BE LOCATED INSIDE PVC PIPE SLEEVE.\n\n## Block 6: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type I Driveway. It shows plan and section views with slope requirements.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nTYPE I DRIVEWAY\nSTANDARD NO.\n433S-2\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY CUONG TRAN 02/24/10\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing plan view of Type I driveway with curb and gutter, including dimensions and slope requirements.]\nPLAN\nNOTE: ALL DRIVEWAYS SHALL BE SLOPED TOWARDS THE STREET FROM THE R.O.W. LINE. ELEVATION OF POINT(S) ABOVE POINT(S) G IS TYPICALLY A MINIMUM OF 150 mm (6\") PLUS 20 mm/m (2\"/100') OVER DISTANCE \"X\" IN METERS (FEET).\n\n[Drawing showing cross-section of Type I driveway with dimensions and slope requirements.]\nCROSS SECTION\n\n## Block 7: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 430S-3 for Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail. It includes an elevation and section view of the dowel detail.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nCURB EXPANSION JOINT DOWEL DETAIL\nSTANDARD NO.\n430S-3\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY LINO RIVERA 3/29/99\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing curb expansion joint dowel detail with dimensions and material specifications.]\nCURB EXPANSION JOINT DOWEL DETAIL\n\n[Drawing showing section A-A of the dowel detail with dimensions.]\nSECTION A-A\nSEE STANDARD 432S-1 FOR TYPICAL CURB AND GUTTER SECTIONS.\n\n## Block 9: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 432S-1 for Sidewalk. It shows a plan and section view of a sidewalk with curb and gutter.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nSIDEWALK\nSTANDARD NO.\n432S-1\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 03/26/08\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing plan view of sidewalk with curb and gutter, including dimensions and joint locations.]\nPLAN\n\n[Drawing showing section view of sidewalk with curb and gutter, including dimensions and reinforcement requirements.]\nSECTION\nNOTES: POLYPROPYLENE FIBRILLATED FIBERS, OR 152 mm X 152 mm X MW 9 X MW 9 WWM (6\"X 6\"X W1.4 X W1.4) WELDED WIRE FABRIC OR ONE LAYER 10M (#3) BARS PLACED NOT MORE THAN 450 mm (18\") C.C. BOTH DIRECTIONS. REINFORCEMENT SHALL ACCURATELY PLACED AT SLAB MID-DEPTH AND HELD FIRMLY IN PLACE BY MEANS OF BAR SUPPORTS OF ADEQUATE STRENGTH AND NUMBER THAT WILL PREVENT DISPLACEMENT AND KEEP THE STEEL AT ITS PROPER ELEVATION DURING THE PLACEMENT OF THE P.C. CONCRETE. IN NO INSTANCE SHALL THE STEEL BE PLACED DIRECTLY ON THE SUBGRADE OR SAND CUSHION LAYER.\n\n## Block 10: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 430S-1 for Curb and Gutter Section. It shows the dimensions and specifications for a laydown curb and catch curb.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nCURB AND GUTTER SECTION\nSTANDARD NO.\n430S-1\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY LINO RIVERA 3/29/99\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing laydown curb section with dimensions R1, R2, R3, R4, and slope requirements.]\nLAYDOWN CURB\n\n[Drawing showing catch curb section with dimensions R1, R2, R3, R4, and slope requirements.]\nCATCH\n\n## Block 11: diagram — City of Austin standard detail 432S-1 for Sidewalk. It shows a dowel detail for sidewalk expansion joints.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nSIDEWALK\nSTANDARD NO.\n432S-1\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY BILL GARDNER 03/26/08\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nADOPTED\n\n[Drawing showing dowel detail for sidewalk expansion joint, including dimensions and material specifications.]\nDOWEL DETAIL\n\n","numLines":204,"startLine":1,"totalLines":204}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776704542836,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BkmJ72qiqhQpiKhikUkxRb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The construction details on Sheet 22 show standard driveway and sidewalk details, but there is NO mention of overhead electric line clearances or vertical clearance requirements from overhead lines. The driveway details don't reference any clearance from overhead conductors.\n\nThis is a major finding - the driveways are designed without showing any vertical clearance from the overhead electric lines that cross over them.\n\nNow let me check if there are any building elevation sheets that might show clearances. I should look for sheets that show building elevations or sections. Let me check the sheet index again to see if there are any elevation or section sheets.\n\nFrom the README, I can see there are sheets for various details but I didn't see specific \"Building Elevation\" sheets mentioned. However, I should check if there are any section views or profiles on existing sheets that show vertical clearances.\n\nLet me examine the site plan vision more carefully or check if there are any sheet sections that show vertical clearances from overhead lines. The key issue is:\n\n1. EL-1.18: Driveways do not maintain minimum 16-foot vertical clearance (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot vertical clearance (areas with truck traffic) from lowest point of overhead electric facilities\n\nThe site plan shows driveways in the ROW where OHE lines are present, but there are NO vertical clearance dimensions provided on any of the sheets reviewed so far.\n\nLet me compile my findings and create the deficiency report. Based on my research:\n\nDEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED:\n\n1. EL-1.18 - Driveways: No vertical clearance dimensions shown from overhead lines to driveway surfaces. Two proposed driveways cross the overhead electric lines, but no verification that 16-18 feet of clearance is maintained.\n\n2. EL-1.31 - Vertical Clearance Survey: No registered surveyor data provided showing pole locations and mid-span clearances for the overhead lines that cross the driveways.\n\n3. EL-1.46 - 48-Hour Notification Note: No plan note requiring the owner/contractor to notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near the overhead high-voltage lines.\n\n\n4. EL-1.37 - Trees near overhead lines: The western boundary shows proposed trees adjacent to the overhead electric lines, but the species aren't specified on the plans, so I can't confirm they meet utility-compatibility requirements for plantings within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors. I also need to verify whether building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and dimension annotations from outer conductors to buildings are present, as these appear to be missing as well.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5567,"cache_read_input_tokens":72038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5567},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","uuid":"fcc7a265-d5fd-42e3-ad1b-af714984d8e9"}
