{"level":30,"time":1776704542836,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014BthtCK9vdrQLWH5ggSFgK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see from the README that the 39 sheets are listed. Looking at the sheet descriptions from the README, I see:\n- Sheet 38: Wall Plan\n- Sheet 39: Wall Plan Details And Notes\n\nBut I don't see any specific \"Building Elevation\" sheets. The site plan set appears to focus on plan views, grading, and utility details rather than building elevations. This is typical for site plan submissions which are not building design documents.\n\nHowever, for a multi-family project with proposed buildings near overhead electric lines, building elevations would be required to verify clearances, but those would be part of the building permit submittal, not necessarily part of the site plan submittal.\n\nLet me now compile all my findings into the final output. Based on my comprehensive research, here are the deficiencies I've identified:\n\nFAIL/NOT-VERIFIABLE ITEMS:\n\n1. **EL-1.18** - FAIL: Driveways do not show minimum 16-18 foot vertical clearance from overhead electric lines. Two driveways proposed where OHE lines cross, but no vertical clearance dimensions provided.\n\n2. **EL-1.31** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: No registered surveyor data provided showing pole locations and mid-span clearances. This is required when vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features appears marginal or insufficient.\n\n3. **EL-1.46** - FAIL: Plans do not include required 48-hour notification note to Austin Energy before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines.\n\n4. **EL-1.37** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors, but specific species not identified on plans. Cannot verify utility-compatible species compliance.\n\n5. **EL-1.7** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: No surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors included on building elevation sheets to demonstrate required clearances. (Note: Building elevations not provided in this site plan submittal)\n\n6. **EL-1.8** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings for clearance verification.\n   \n7. **EL-1.23** - NOT-VERIFIABLE: The plans lack clarity on whether any clearance measurements are taken from the outside conductor or pole centerline as required. No such dimensional references are evident in the submitted documents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1978,"cache_read_input_tokens":77605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1978},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","uuid":"2f0f3d57-d93b-4573-8e42-2ef6ac5999a5"}
