{"level":30,"time":1776704542836,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HKRMmmT8LfSypRDoVjULxE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've successfully submitted the structured output with 7 deficiency findings. These represent all the items from the EL-1 overhead electric clearance grouping that I found to be either \"fail\" or \"not-verifiable\" based on my comprehensive research.\n\nLet me summarize what I found:\n\n**PASS ITEMS (not included in output):**\n- Most items were either not applicable because certain features weren't proposed, or they passed when evaluated against the evidence found. For example:\n  - EL-1.1 (7.5 ft horizontal clearance from buildings) - Buildings are setback 26+ feet from property line; overhead lines are in ROW beyond property line; clearance appears adequate\n  - EL-1.2 (15-foot radial clearance from distribution) - Similar setback situation\n  - EL-1.3 (Building projections) - No detailed elevation information to evaluate, but initial setbacks appear adequate\n  - EL-1.4 (Gas pump canopies) - No gas pumps proposed\n  - EL-1.5, 1.6 (Stairs/walkways, building in ROW) - No such features proposed\n  - EL-1.9 (Fences) - No perimeter fences proposed along western boundary\n  - EL-1.10, 1.11, 1.12, 1.13, 1.14, 1.15 (Fences, substation fences) - Fences/substations don't apply\n  - EL-1.16 through EL-1.30 (Emergency structures, retaining walls, metering, etc.) - These features either don't apply or the overhead lines are in the ROW where clearance requirements are different\n  - EL-1.32 through EL-1.45 - Most of these weren't applicable to this project\n\n**FAIL ITEMS (included in output):**\n- EL-1.46: No 48-hour notification note (clear violation - note must be on cover sheet)\n\n\n- EL-1.18: Driveway vertical clearance dimensions are missing from the plans\n- EL-1.31: Surveyor mid-span clearance data not provided\n- EL-1.37: Tree species near overhead lines remain unidentified\n- EL-1.7: Building elevation sheets lack surveyed conductor information\n- EL-1.8: Section views don't show clearance dimensions\n- EL-1.23: Can't verify whether clearance measurements originate from conductor or pole centerline\n\nThe site plan sheets provide sufficient documentation to support these observations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2421,"cache_read_input_tokens":79583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2421},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","uuid":"6d9beb52-d13b-4040-8e92-48e0523198db"}
{"level":30,"time":1776704542836,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HKRMmmT8LfSypRDoVjULxE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the review of Grouping EL-1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan. Here are my key findings:\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Identified:**\n- Existing overhead electric lines (OHE) run along the western property boundary on Valley View Road\n- Three utility poles visible on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4)\n- Two proposed driveways cross directly over these overhead lines in the right-of-way\n- A proposed sidewalk runs along the entire western frontage beneath the overhead lines\n\n**Deficiencies Documented:**\n\n1. **EL-1.46 (FAIL)** - Missing 48-Hour Notification Note: The cover sheet does not include the required note that the owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near these high-voltage overhead lines.\n\n2. **EL-1.18 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Driveway Vertical Clearances: The two proposed driveways lack any vertical clearance dimensions from the overhead conductors. Minimum 16-18 feet clearance is required but cannot be verified.\n\n3. **EL-1.31 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Survey Data Missing: No registered surveyor data provided showing pole locations and mid-span clearances for the overhead lines crossing the driveways.\n\n4. **EL-1.37 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Non-Utility-Compatible Trees: Proposed trees are shown along the western boundary near the overhead distribution lines, but their specific species are not identified on the plans. Cannot verify utility-compatible species compliance (trees within 10 feet of overhead distribution lines must be utility-compatible).\n\n5. **EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.23 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Missing Elevation and Section Details: No building elevation sheets, section views, or dimension annotations showing clearances from the outside conductor to site features.\n\nAll findings have been submitted in structured format with specific code citations, applicable areas, sheet references, and detailed comments."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2421,"cache_read_input_tokens":79583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2421},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","uuid":"a78f14f7-303a-4cfe-8f1c-efd9169a9d77"}
{"level":30,"time":1776704542837,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1047393,"duration_api_ms":143379,"num_turns":26,"result":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the review of Grouping EL-1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan. Here are my key findings:\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Identified:**\n- Existing overhead electric lines (OHE) run along the western property boundary on Valley View Road\n- Three utility poles visible on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4)\n- Two proposed driveways cross directly over these overhead lines in the right-of-way\n- A proposed sidewalk runs along the entire western frontage beneath the overhead lines\n\n**Deficiencies Documented:**\n\n1. **EL-1.46 (FAIL)** - Missing 48-Hour Notification Note: The cover sheet does not include the required note that the owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near these high-voltage overhead lines.\n\n2. **EL-1.18 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Driveway Vertical Clearances: The two proposed driveways lack any vertical clearance dimensions from the overhead conductors. Minimum 16-18 feet clearance is required but cannot be verified.\n\n3. **EL-1.31 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Survey Data Missing: No registered surveyor data provided showing pole locations and mid-span clearances for the overhead lines crossing the driveways.\n\n4. **EL-1.37 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Non-Utility-Compatible Trees: Proposed trees are shown along the western boundary near the overhead distribution lines, but their specific species are not identified on the plans. Cannot verify utility-compatible species compliance (trees within 10 feet of overhead distribution lines must be utility-compatible).\n\n5. **EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.23 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Missing Elevation and Section Details: No building elevation sheets, section views, or dimension annotations showing clearances from the outside conductor to site features.\n\nAll findings have been submitted in structured format with specific code citations, applicable areas, sheet references, and detailed comments.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5f760423-269f-4053-9cd7-9b700986aecc","total_cost_usd":0.2637368,"usage":{"input_tokens":144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82004,"cache_read_input_tokens":1074228,"output_tokens":10733,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82004,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":144,"outputTokens":10733,"cacheReadInputTokens":1074228,"cacheCreationInputTokens":82004,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2637368,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed driveways along western boundary (Valley View Road right-of-way)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two proposed driveways cross overhead electric lines in the Valley View Road right-of-way. Site plan shows OHE line crossing directly over both driveway aprons, but no vertical clearance dimensions are provided from the lowest point of the overhead conductors to the finished driveway surface. Minimum 16-foot vertical clearance (for parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot vertical clearance (for areas with truck traffic) required per UCM § 1.10.6.2, but cannot be verified from available plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways beneath overhead electric lines on western boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No survey data from a registered surveyor provided showing pole locations and mid-span clearances from overhead electric conductors to finished driveway grades. When existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements, registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is required per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["General site - entire property with overhead electric infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. This notification requirement must be prominently noted on the cover sheet per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003, as referenced in UCM § 1.10.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Street yard and parking lot landscaping areas along western boundary where overhead distribution conductors are present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed trees are shown on the landscape plan along the western boundary within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors. The specific species of these proposed trees are not identified on the plans (labeled only as 'SYM' with no species key provided). Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, species generally with mature height ≤20 feet marked 'UC'). Utility-compatible species status cannot be verified from available landscape documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1 and 8 (closest to western boundary with overhead lines)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are included on building elevation sheets to demonstrate that required clearances are met. Building elevation sheets showing surveyed conductor elevation data with clearance dimension annotations are required per UCM § 1.10.3 when buildings are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities. Building elevations are not provided in this site plan submittal."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed buildings and site features near overhead electric lines on western boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings, building projections, or other site features for clearance verification. Dimension lines with clearance measurements from outside conductor (not pole centerline) to all building features are required per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line clearance