{"level":30,"time":1776704542838,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012jUWWctBHKAkESHiz1V8MN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I found the plant list. The proposed trees include:\n- SHADE TREES:\n  - 2 Live Oak (QUERCUS VIRGINIANA) - 100 gal, 4\" cal, 16' ht\n  - 10 Cedar Elm (ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA) - 100 gal, 4\" cal, 16' ht\n  \n- ORNAMENTAL TREES:\n  - 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (SOPHORA SECUNDIFLORA) - 45 gal, 2.5\" cal, 8' ht\n  - 6 Mexican Redbud (CERCIS CANADENSIS VAR. MEXICANA) - 45 gal, 2.5\" cal, 10' ht\n\nCRITICAL ISSUE: Live Oak and Cedar Elm are large shade trees that are NOT utility-compatible. They're both typically 40+ feet at maturity, NOT under 20 feet. The Texas Mountain Laurel is smaller (8' ht) but still needs checking. Mexican Redbud (10' ht specified) could be considered a smaller tree.\n\nI need to check if any of these are on the Utility Compatible list. From my knowledge of the ECM Appendix F, Live Oak and Cedar Elm are definitely NOT utility compatible. The smaller ornamental trees might be, but I would need to verify.\n\nMore importantly, the landscape plan shows these trees planted directly on or within the overhead electric line zone along the southern property boundary, and there are NO clearance dimensions or annotations.\n\nThis is a major deficiency. Let me now compile my findings for the checklist evaluation.\n\nRESEARCH SUMMARY - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:\n1. Building elevation sheets showing vertical clearances from overhead conductors to buildings - NOT FOUND\n2. Surveyed elevations of overhead conductor heights - NOT FOUND\n3. Section/profile views showing clearances from conductors to buildings/structures - NOT FOUND\n\n\n4. Vertical clearance dimensions for driveways under overhead lines - NOT FOUND\n5. Distance/clearance dimensions between proposed trees and the overhead electric line - NOT FOUND\n6. 48-hour notification note for work near overhead lines - NOT FOUND on cover sheet\n7. Clearance verification that the large shade trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) proposed for planting near overhead line are Utility Compatible species - NOT VERIFIED\n8. Proximity survey showing existing pole locations and overhead line routing relative to proposed improvements - NOT FOUND\n\nSeveral critical documents are missing from the set. The plans lack any vertical clearance details for driveways crossing under the overhead lines, and there's no documentation of distances between the proposed trees and the electric line itself. The cover sheet is also missing the required 48-hour notification language for work near utilities. Additionally, I can't verify that the large shade trees meet utility compatibility standards, and there's no survey showing pole locations or overhead line routing relative to the site improvements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4638,"cache_read_input_tokens":64147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4638},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d43314f-ffee-4c09-9531-73169237fb4a","uuid":"03ebd57f-451f-4f97-945f-095fbd62b543"}
