this document as the transformer pads and their access doors are not shown.\n\n**3. Trees within 15 lateral feet of where overhead electric conductors might be located:**\nWhile the transformers are absent, the plan *does* indicate the location of overhead electric lines.\n*   A line labeled **\"-OHE-\"** runs west-to-east along the southern boundary of the site plan (bottom of the page), just outside the \"-LOC-\" (Limits of Construction) line.\n*   Based on the provided graphic scale (1\" = 20'-0\"):\n    *   In the far Southwest corner, there is one proposed tree labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree) located immediately adjacent to the \"-OHE-\" line, clearly within 15 lateral feet.\n    *   In the Southeast corner area, there are two proposed trees labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree) located immediately adjacent to the \"-OHE-\" line, clearly within 15 lateral feet.\n    *   *Note: There are no OHE lines shown near the Northwest, West Central, or East Central areas of the plan.*\n\n**4. Whether any required root barriers are shown or can be inferred from the drawings:**\nThere are **no** indications of root barriers. I have scanned the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\", \"KEY NOTES\", and the entire graphic plan. There are no symbols, line types, or text notes indicating the presence or requirement of root barriers on this sheet.\n\n***\n\n### Document Transcription Details\n\nTo assist the review agent with context found on this page, here are exact transcriptions of the relevant legends and labels used to identify the landscaping elements mentioned above.\n\n**KEY NOTES:**\n*   **H-1** : PROPOSED PAVING\n*   **H-2** : STREET YARD\n*   **H-3** : STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n*   **H-4** : PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n*   **H-5** : PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n*   **H-6** : WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n*   **H-7** : SOD\n\n**Tree Identifiers (located directly below the Key Notes):**\n*   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n*   **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n\n**Project Details (Title Block):**\n*   **PROJECT NAME:** VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\n*   **OWNER:** WM 41 AUSTIN RE, LLC\n*   **PROJECT LOCATION:** 3759 VALLEY VIEW ROAD, AUSTIN, TEXAS 78704\n*   **DRAWING TITLE:** LANDSCAPE PLAN\n*   **SHEET NO.:** 28 of 35","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1457,"outputTokens":855,"totalTokens":4344,"reasoningTokens":2032},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Identify the locations of all proposed trees a