{"level":30,"time":1776704787167,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Looking at the specific tree symbols and their labels on the Landscape Plan, please:\n\n1. For the +M (Mitigation Tree) symbol located in the southeast corner (very close to the utility pole), can you identify what specific species it is or what label/notation is associated with it?\n\n2. For all the trees shown along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line (OHE), identify their symbols and any species designations or labels.\n\n3. Can you see any text labels or symbol keys that indicate which species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are planted at specific locations?\n\n4. Looking at the overall landscape design, describe which tree species appear to be planted in each major area (northern boundary, southern boundary, parking areas, common spaces, etc.).\n\n5. Are there any crosshatches, color coding, or other visual distinctions that differentiate between the different tree species?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan document, here are the answers to your questions:\n\n**1. Identification of the +M (Mitigation Tree) symbol in the southeast corner:**\nLocating the tree symbol in the southeast corner (bottom right, near the property lines and existing tree symbols), it consists of an open circle with a cross (+) in the center and is labeled simply with the letter **\"M\"**.\n\nThere is **no specific species label, notation, or abbreviation** (such as 'CE', 'LO', etc.) associated with this specific symbol anywhere near it on the plan. According to the text below the Key Notes, \"M\" is defined exactly as:\n`M - MITIGATION TREE`\n\n**2. Trees shown along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line (OHE):**\nScanning the southern boundary (bottom edge) along the line labeled \"--- OHE ---\", there are three symbols representing newly planted trees. Moving from west to east (left to right):\n*   Near the southwest corner: A simple circle symbol with a central cross (+) labeled **\"M\"**.\n*   Near the middle of the southern boundary: A simple circle symbol with a central cross (+) labeled **\"M\"**.\n*   Near the southeast corner: A simple circle symbol with a central cross (+) labeled **\"M\"**.\n\nThere are **no species designations or specific plant labels** provided for any of these trees. They are only categorized by the \"M\" label.\n\n**3. Text labels or symbol keys indicating specific species:**\nBased on the visible portion of this specific sheet, **there are no text labels, symbol keys, or plant schedules indicating specific plant species** such as Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, or Mexican Redbud.\n\nThe only key provided for trees is located below the \"KEY NOTES\" section on the right side of the page, which categorizes trees by function rather than species:\n*   `ST - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE`\n*   `M - MITIGATION TREE`\n\nSpecific species information would likely be found on a separate \"Planting Plan\" sheet or in a \"Plant Schedule\" not present in this image.\n\n**4. Tree distribution in major areas:**\nBecause specific species names are not provided on this sheet, the distribution can only be described based on the functional category labels (M, ST, PL) found next to the tree symbols:\n*   **Northern Boundary:** The trees planted along the northern property line are predominantly labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree).\n*   **Southern Boundary:** As noted above, the trees planted along the southern property line are exclusively labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree).\n*   **Western Boundary (Street Frontage):** The trees planted in the street yard area along Valley View Road are a mix of labels **\"ST\"** (Street Yard Tree) and **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree).\n*   **Parking Areas/Interior:** Trees planted within parking lot islands or immediately adjacent to interior parking spaces (e.g., near the filtration basin, or interior islands) are labeled **\"PL\"** (Parking Lot Tree).\n\n**5. Visual distinctions between tree species:**\nLooking exclusively at the proposed/planted tree symbols (those labeled M, ST, PL), **there are no visual distinctions utilized to differentiate between different types of trees.**\n\nEvery proposed tree utilizes the exact same graphic representation: a simple, solid-line circle with an identical cross (+) in the center. There are no crosshatches, differing textures, unique symbol shapes, or internal graphics used for planted trees. The only way to differentiate the trees on this specific plan is by reading the alphanumeric labels (M, ST, PL) placed next to the identical circle symbols. (Note: The document is black and white, so color coding is not applicable. Symbols with irregular, squiggly outlines and internal 'x' marks represent existing trees to remain or be removed, not newly planted species).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1501,"outputTokens":880,"totalTokens":4908,"reasoningTokens":2527},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather tha