roposed new tree locations**\nProposed new trees (typically indicated by crosshairs at the trunk center and specific letter tags) are distributed in the following areas:\n*   **West Area:** Running parallel to Valley View Road within a shaded grey region (identified in the legend as \"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\").\n*   **North Area:** Arrayed linearly along the upper (northern) Limit of Construction (LOC) boundary.\n*   **South Area:** A cluster located near the southeast corner along the southern boundary.\n*   **Central/East Area:** A few isolated proposed trees are located near the \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\" in the northeast section.\n\n**4. Tree symbols/tags and their locations relative to the OHE line**\nBased on the \"KEY NOTES:\" on the right side of the document:\n*   **\"SY\" (Street Yard) trees:** Located exclusively on the far West boundary along Valley View Road. Several are tagged with a combined \"SY/M\". These are located on the opposite side of the site from the OHE line (West vs. South) and are hundreds of feet away based on the scale.\n*   **\"PL\" (Parking Lot) trees:** Located centrally and to the east. One tree is tagged \"PL/M\" near the north-central boundary. Another is tagged \"PL\" near the northeast basins. These are significantly north of the OHE line.\n*   **\"M\" (Mitigation) trees:** These are distributed in multiple locations. A large quantity is planted along the North boundary. Some are mixed into the West street yard (\"SY/M\"). Notably, there is a cluster of three trees tagged solely \"M\" located near the East end of the South boundary.\n*   **Existing trees (dot in circle):** The vast majority are clustered along the North boundary, often overlapping the LOC line. A few are visible outside the eastern LOC, and there is one clear existing tree symbol near the southwest corner, relatively close to the OHE line.\n\n**5. Trees closest to or adjacent to the OHE line**\nThe tree symbols located closest to the \"---OHE---\" line are situated along the South boundary. \nSpecifically, in the southeast quadrant (bottom right of the plan), there is a group of three proposed trees explicitly tagged **\"M\"** (Mitigation). \n\n*Distance approximation based on scale:* Using the provided graphic scale of 1\"=20'-0\", the trunk symbols (center crosshairs) of these three \"M\" tagged trees on the south boundary are positioned approximately 10 to 15 feet north of the \"---OHE---\" line. The drawn canopy circles for these specific mitigation trees directly intersect and overlap the OHE line.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1531,"outputTokens":748,"totalTokens":4592,"reasoningTokens":2313},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document direc