{"level":30,"time":1776704795793,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAACTzoZ5qV96zKdiBwaCd","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 22 — Construction Details 1\n     2→\n     3→Construction details for curbs, sidewalks, driveways, and bicycle parking.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains standard construction details, primarily City of Austin (COA) standard specifications, for site civil elements. Its primary purpose is to provide the required dimensions, reinforcement, and installation procedures for curbs, gutters, sidewalks, driveways, bicycle parking, and bumper curbs.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Driveway Thickness:** Passenger vehicle parking lots = 150 mm (6\") min.; All others = 175 mm (7\") min.\n    11→*   **Driveway Reinforcement:** 125 mm (5\") min. concrete with one layer 13M (#4) bars placed at max 450 mm (18\") O.C. both directions.\n    12→*   **Driveway Allowable Grades:** >1500 ADT = 5% max; 500-1500 ADT = 6% max; <500 ADT = 8% (up to 15% max for emergency access).\n    13→*   **Type I Driveway Slope:** Elevation typically min. 150 mm (6\") plus 20 mm/m (2\"/100') over distance.\n    14→*   **Sidewalk Reinforcement:** 152x152xMW9xMW9 welded wire fabric or one layer 10M (#3) bars max 450 mm (18\") C.C. both directions.\n    15→*   **Bicycle Rack Base Plates:** 6.35 mm (1/4\") plates, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 low carbon prime steel.\n    16→*   **Bicycle Rack Siting:** Must be within 7.32m (24') of main building entry; minimum clearance from utilities is 0.9m (3').\n    17→*   **Bumper Curb Concrete:** Class \"A\" in accordance with Item 403S.\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 1: diagram — Sidewalk Dowel Detail (COA 432S-1)**. Shows dowel specifications for sidewalk expansion joints. Use VISION for spatial layout and dimensions.\n    22→*   **Block 2: diagram — Curb and Gutter Section (COA 430S-1)**. Displays laydown and catch curb profiles. Use VISION to examine curb slope requirements and radii.\n    23→*   **Block 3: diagram — Sidewalk Plan and Section (COA 432S-1)**. Shows sidewalk layout with adjacent curb. READ for exact reinforcement requirements (WWM or #3 bars) and VISION for joint spacing layout.\n    24→*   **Block 4: table and text — Type II Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Contains structural specifications and layout rules for driveways. READ for exact driveway thickness, reinforcement specs, allowable grade tables, and general driveway notes.\n    25→*   **Block 5: diagram — Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail (COA 430S-3)**. Elevation and cross-section of the dowel joint. Use VISION to examine the positioning of the dowel sleeve and joint dimensions.\n    26→*   **Block 6: diagram — Type I Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Plan and section views for standard driveways. Use VISION for geometric layout and READ for specific slope calculation notes.\n    27→*   **Block 7: diagram — Sidewalk Over Utility Service Lines (COA 432S-1)**. Details the PVC pipe sleeve and sand cushion arrangement. Use VISION to verify utility crossing protection details.\n    28→*   **Block 8: diagram — Class III Style Bicycle Parking (COA 710S-1)**. Rack fabrication details. VISION for rack dimensions and READ for base plate material thickness and steel grade requirements.\n    29→*   **Block 9: diagram — Furnishing Location for Bicycle Racks (COA 710S-6C)**. Shows linear and parallel rack installation footprints. READ for strict spacing rules, utility clearances, and building entry proximity limits; VISION for spatial arrangement diagrams.\n    30→*   **Block 10: diagram — Bicycle Rack Installation (COA 710S-4)**. Concrete anchor details. Use VISION for mechanical expansion anchor bolt setup and READ the note regarding anti-theft bolt deformation.\n    31→*   **Block 11: diagram — Parking Lot Bumper Curb (COA 439S-1)**. Plan, section, and profile of concrete wheel stops. Use VISION for rebar placement/dimensions and READ for the required concrete class specification.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→- `block-8.md` — diagram: City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type II Driveway. It includes a table for allowable grades\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dccfafa3-f785-4cc2-a45b-b26d9e2e76f8","uuid":"9d0c349c-2fe6-4342-be1d-8ca76f296943","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-22/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 22 — Construction Details 1\n\nConstruction details for curbs, sidewalks, driveways, and bicycle parking.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains standard construction details, primarily City of Austin (COA) standard specifications, for site civil elements. Its primary purpose is to provide the required dimensions, reinforcement, and installation procedures for curbs, gutters, sidewalks, driveways, bicycle parking, and bumper curbs.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Driveway Thickness:** Passenger vehicle parking lots = 150 mm (6\") min.; All others = 175 mm (7\") min.\n*   **Driveway Reinforcement:** 125 mm (5\") min. concrete with one layer 13M (#4) bars placed at max 450 mm (18\") O.C. both directions.\n*   **Driveway Allowable Grades:** >1500 ADT = 5% max; 500-1500 ADT = 6% max; <500 ADT = 8% (up to 15% max for emergency access).\n*   **Type I Driveway Slope:** Elevation typically min. 150 mm (6\") plus 20 mm/m (2\"/100') over distance.\n*   **Sidewalk Reinforcement:** 152x152xMW9xMW9 welded wire fabric or one layer 10M (#3) bars max 450 mm (18\") C.C. both directions.\n*   **Bicycle Rack Base Plates:** 6.35 mm (1/4\") plates, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 low carbon prime steel.\n*   **Bicycle Rack Siting:** Must be within 7.32m (24') of main building entry; minimum clearance from utilities is 0.9m (3').\n*   **Bumper Curb Concrete:** Class \"A\" in accordance with Item 403S.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Sidewalk Dowel Detail (COA 432S-1)**. Shows dowel specifications for sidewalk expansion joints. Use VISION for spatial layout and dimensions.\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Curb and Gutter Section (COA 430S-1)**. Displays laydown and catch curb profiles. Use VISION to examine curb slope requirements and radii.\n*   **Block 3: diagram — Sidewalk Plan and Section (COA 432S-1)**. Shows sidewalk layout with adjacent curb. READ for exact reinforcement requirements (WWM or #3 bars) and VISION for joint spacing layout.\n*   **Block 4: table and text — Type II Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Contains structural specifications and layout rules for driveways. READ for exact driveway thickness, reinforcement specs, allowable grade tables, and general driveway notes.\n*   **Block 5: diagram — Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail (COA 430S-3)**. Elevation and cross-section of the dowel joint. Use VISION to examine the positioning of the dowel sleeve and joint dimensions.\n*   **Block 6: diagram — Type I Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Plan and section views for standard driveways. Use VISION for geometric layout and READ for specific slope calculation notes.\n*   **Block 7: diagram — Sidewalk Over Utility Service Lines (COA 432S-1)**. Details the PVC pipe sleeve and sand cushion arrangement. Use VISION to verify utility crossing protection details.\n*   **Block 8: diagram — Class III Style Bicycle Parking (COA 710S-1)**. Rack fabrication details. VISION for rack dimensions and READ for base plate material thickness and steel grade requirements.\n*   **Block 9: diagram — Furnishing Location for Bicycle Racks (COA 710S-6C)**. Shows linear and parallel rack installation footprints. READ for strict spacing rules, utility clearances, and building entry proximity limits; VISION for spatial arrangement diagrams.\n*   **Block 10: diagram — Bicycle Rack Installation (COA 710S-4)**. Concrete anchor details. Use VISION for mechanical expansion anchor bolt setup and READ the note regarding anti-theft bolt deformation.\n*   **Block 11: diagram — Parking Lot Bumper Curb (COA 439S-1)**. Plan, section, and profile of concrete wheel stops. Use VISION for rebar placement/dimensions and READ for the required concrete class specification.\n\n---\n\n- `block-8.md` — diagram: City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type II Driveway. It includes a table for allowable grades\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
