ughout the entire site.\n\nThe key issue is:\n1. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows \"+M\" tree symbols along the southern boundary near the OHE line\n2. These are labeled only as \"Mitigation Trees\" with NO species designation\n3. The plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists the tree species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but doesn't indicate WHERE on the site each species is planted\n\n\n4. The species allocation to the \"+M\" locations on the southern boundary isn't clearly documented anywhere. This could be a deficiency under EL-2.10, which requires the plant legend or schedule to identify tree species near electric facilities. I need to check if any other sheets show this allocation or if the landscape plan notes specify where each species goes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2220,"cache_read_input_tokens":66504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2220},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b700214-8b92-4820-b37e-6e650418c2d5","uuid":"77130b28-a035-4285-83d6-3ae827aaa478"}
