{"level":30,"time":1776704920249,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KoYbXQoJ2aau1T3BjQQm1h","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 25 — Construction Details 4\n     2→\n     3→Standard details, plan, and section views for fire line meters.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides City of Austin standard construction details for a 6\", 8\", or 10\" fire line meter vault installation for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes a comprehensive plan layout, vertical cross-sections, a material schedule, and specifications for vault dimensions based on meter size.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   Applicable Meter Sizes: 6\", 8\", or 10\"\n    11→*   Vault Dimensions (Inside): 8' x 12' (for 6\" meter), 10' x 12' (for 8\" meter), 10' x 15' (for 10\" meter)\n    12→*   Access Hatch Size: 48\" x 72\"\n    13→*   Minimum Clearances: 18\" clearance between vault wall and bypass piping/meter components\n    14→*   Gasket Specification: Full face 1/8\" thick red rubber\n    15→*   Pipe Material: Ductile Iron Class 53\n    16→*   Fasteners: 5/8\" diameter x 8\" long stainless steel wedge-all anchors\n    17→*   City of Austin Standard Number: 512-AW-02 (Adopted 03/10/2025)\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 3**: drawing — Plan view of the pipe system layout within the concrete vault. Use VISION to examine component placement, pipe routing, and minimum horizontal dimensional clearances.\n    22→*   **Block 2**: diagram — Section A-A view showing longitudinal vertical elevation. Use VISION for final grade relationships, concrete pad locations, and support stand configurations.\n    23→*   **Block 1**: diagram — Section B-B view showing transverse vertical elevation. Use VISION for alternative structural details and vertical clearance perspectives.\n    24→*   **Block 6**: table — Vault Schedule. READ for exact inside vault dimensions and offset dimensions corresponding to the specific fire line meter size being installed.\n    25→*   **Block 7**: table — Fire Line Meter Material List. READ for specific component descriptions, sizes, material types, and approved City of Austin part designations (e.g., link-seal modular seals, dismantling joints).\n    26→*   **Block 4**: notes — General construction and installation notes. READ for material specifications on nuts/bolts, gaskets, bedding, encasement, and drainage slope requirements.\n    27→*   **Block 13**: text_block — \"Use of This Standard\". READ for stipulations regarding when a project-specific structural design is required versus when this standard can be directly applied.\n    28→*   **Blocks 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the main title (\"6\", 8\" AND 10\" FIRE LINE METER\"), standard identifier (512-AW-02), adoption date (03/10/2025), agency info (City of Austin Water), disclaimers, and the professional engineer's seal.\n    29→\n    30→---\n    31→\n    32→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    33→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dccfafa3-f785-4cc2-a45b-b26d9e2e76f8","uuid":"25af35b2-14fc-4119-a952-2ea65097688d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 25 — Construction Details 4\n\nStandard details, plan, and section views for fire line meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides City of Austin standard construction details for a 6\", 8\", or 10\" fire line meter vault installation for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes a comprehensive plan layout, vertical cross-sections, a material schedule, and specifications for vault dimensions based on meter size.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   Applicable Meter Sizes: 6\", 8\", or 10\"\n*   Vault Dimensions (Inside): 8' x 12' (for 6\" meter), 10' x 12' (for 8\" meter), 10' x 15' (for 10\" meter)\n*   Access Hatch Size: 48\" x 72\"\n*   Minimum Clearances: 18\" clearance between vault wall and bypass piping/meter components\n*   Gasket Specification: Full face 1/8\" thick red rubber\n*   Pipe Material: Ductile Iron Class 53\n*   Fasteners: 5/8\" diameter x 8\" long stainless steel wedge-all anchors\n*   City of Austin Standard Number: 512-AW-02 (Adopted 03/10/2025)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 3**: drawing — Plan view of the pipe system layout within the concrete vault. Use VISION to examine component placement, pipe routing, and minimum horizontal dimensional clearances.\n*   **Block 2**: diagram — Section A-A view showing longitudinal vertical elevation. Use VISION for final grade relationships, concrete pad locations, and support stand configurations.\n*   **Block 1**: diagram — Section B-B view showing transverse vertical elevation. Use VISION for alternative structural details and vertical clearance perspectives.\n*   **Block 6**: table — Vault Schedule. READ for exact inside vault dimensions and offset dimensions corresponding to the specific fire line meter size being installed.\n*   **Block 7**: table — Fire Line Meter Material List. READ for specific component descriptions, sizes, material types, and approved City of Austin part designations (e.g., link-seal modular seals, dismantling joints).\n*   **Block 4**: notes — General construction and installation notes. READ for material specifications on nuts/bolts, gaskets, bedding, encasement, and drainage slope requirements.\n*   **Block 13**: text_block — \"Use of This Standard\". READ for stipulations regarding when a project-specific structural design is required versus when this standard can be directly applied.\n*   **Blocks 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the main title (\"6\", 8\" AND 10\" FIRE LINE METER\"), standard identifier (512-AW-02), adoption date (03/10/2025), agency info (City of Austin Water), disclaimers, and the professional engineer's seal.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
