{"level":30,"time":1776704920249,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UxhAd5GzaeHiADtPDKY1TK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 28 — Construction Details 7\n     2→\n     3→Construction details for storm drain manholes and catch basins.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides construction details and standard specifications for storm drainage infrastructure, specifically focusing on City of Austin standards for manholes and ParkUSA catch basins. It includes detailed cross-sections, plan views, and dimensional tables to guide the installation of pre-cast and cast-in-place drainage structures.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Catch Basin Concrete Specification:** 4500 PSI design strength at 28 days\n    11→*   **Catch Basin Reinforcement:** Grade 60 steel rebar conforming to ASTM A615\n    12→*   **Catch Basin Castings:** Grey cast iron conforming to ASTM A48-76 Class 30\n    13→*   **Catch Basin Sizes:** Models range from CB-12 (12\"x12\"x24\", 180 lbs) to CB-84 (84\"x84\"x72\", 19,500 lbs)\n    14→*   **Manhole Frame & Cover Size:** 800 mm (32\") or 813 mm (32\")\n    15→*   **Manhole Lid Weights:** 325 N (73 lbs) for cast iron; 778 N (175 lbs) for ductile iron\n    16→*   **Manhole Lid Load Test Requirement:** 20,000-pound proof load test (AASHTO M-306)\n    17→*   **Minimum Manhole Diameter to Pipe Size Ratios:**\n    18→    *   1.2 m (4') dia. for 450 to 600 mm (18\" to 24\") pipes\n    19→    *   1.5 m (5') dia. for 750 to 1.05 m (30\" to 42\") pipes\n    20→    *   1.8 m (6') dia. for 1.2 to 1.6 m (48\" to 64\") pipes\n    21→    *   2.1 m (7') dia. for 1.5 to 1.7 m (60\" to 66\") pipes\n    22→*   **Junction Manhole Intersecting Pipes:** Diagram shows 460 mm (18\"), 610 mm (24\"), and 760 mm (30\") I.D. pipes\n    23→*   **Box Manhole Requirement:** Used for 760 mm (30\") and larger pipes, requiring Class \"A\" Concrete and Item 406 reinforcing steel\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 3: diagram — Catch Basin Details (ParkUSA)**. Contains a comprehensive dimensional schedule (Models CB-12 through CB-84) alongside structural diagrams. READ for precise model dimensions, grate sizes, weights, and material specifications (concrete, reinforcement, castings). Use VISION to understand the isometric view and section layout parameters (W1, H1, T1, etc.).\n    28→*   **Blocks 8 & 1: diagrams — Pre-Cast Concrete Storm Drain Manhole (City of Austin Std 506S-3, Parts 1 & 2)**. Block 8 shows the primary cross-section and sizing tables, while Block 1 shows adjusting rings and alternative section details. READ Block 8 for minimum manhole diameter to pipe size requirements. Use VISION on both blocks to examine the structural geometry, base slab configurations, and optional step placements.\n    29→*   **Blocks 6, 7 & 9: diagrams — Storm Drain Manhole Ring and 813 mm (32\") Cover (City of Austin Std 503S-4S, Parts 1-3)**. Detailed drawings of the lid, ring section, and manufacturing notes. READ Block 9 for casting specifications, specific weight requirements, and load testing standards. Use VISION on Blocks 6 and 7 to examine the physical lid layout, pick bar placement, and machine finish details.\n    30→*   **Block 5: diagram — Typical Box Manhole for 760 mm (30\") & Larger Pipe (City of Austin Std 506S-5)**. Cross-section of a cast-in-place box manhole with associated construction notes. READ the notes for concrete class and steel reinforcement requirements. Use VISION for spatial layout, reinforcement placement, and mortar details.\n    31→*   **Blocks 2 & 4: diagrams — Manhole Plan Views**. Plan views illustrating a typical manhole at an angle (Block 2) and a typical junction manhole (Block 4) showing intersecting pipe diameters. Use VISION to examine the flow inverts, pipe configurations, and how the manhole invert must be formed to provide smooth water flow.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→- `block-7.md` — diagram: Detailed diagram and specifications for a catch basin, including model dimensions, grate options, an\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dccfafa3-f785-4cc2-a45b-b26d9e2e76f8","uuid":"d7f7c750-a036-4c92-8df6-38b1c86c0035","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-28/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 28 — Construction Details 7\n\nConstruction details for storm drain manholes and catch basins.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides construction details and standard specifications for storm drainage infrastructure, specifically focusing on City of Austin standards for manholes and ParkUSA catch basins. It includes detailed cross-sections, plan views, and dimensional tables to guide the installation of pre-cast and cast-in-place drainage structures.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Catch Basin Concrete Specification:** 4500 PSI design strength at 28 days\n*   **Catch Basin Reinforcement:** Grade 60 steel rebar conforming to ASTM A615\n*   **Catch Basin Castings:** Grey cast iron conforming to ASTM A48-76 Class 30\n*   **Catch Basin Sizes:** Models range from CB-12 (12\"x12\"x24\", 180 lbs) to CB-84 (84\"x84\"x72\", 19,500 lbs)\n*   **Manhole Frame & Cover Size:** 800 mm (32\") or 813 mm (32\")\n*   **Manhole Lid Weights:** 325 N (73 lbs) for cast iron; 778 N (175 lbs) for ductile iron\n*   **Manhole Lid Load Test Requirement:** 20,000-pound proof load test (AASHTO M-306)\n*   **Minimum Manhole Diameter to Pipe Size Ratios:**\n    *   1.2 m (4') dia. for 450 to 600 mm (18\" to 24\") pipes\n    *   1.5 m (5') dia. for 750 to 1.05 m (30\" to 42\") pipes\n    *   1.8 m (6') dia. for 1.2 to 1.6 m (48\" to 64\") pipes\n    *   2.1 m (7') dia. for 1.5 to 1.7 m (60\" to 66\") pipes\n*   **Junction Manhole Intersecting Pipes:** Diagram shows 460 mm (18\"), 610 mm (24\"), and 760 mm (30\") I.D. pipes\n*   **Box Manhole Requirement:** Used for 760 mm (30\") and larger pipes, requiring Class \"A\" Concrete and Item 406 reinforcing steel\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: diagram — Catch Basin Details (ParkUSA)**. Contains a comprehensive dimensional schedule (Models CB-12 through CB-84) alongside structural diagrams. READ for precise model dimensions, grate sizes, weights, and material specifications (concrete, reinforcement, castings). Use VISION to understand the isometric view and section layout parameters (W1, H1, T1, etc.).\n*   **Blocks 8 & 1: diagrams — Pre-Cast Concrete Storm Drain Manhole (City of Austin Std 506S-3, Parts 1 & 2)**. Block 8 shows the primary cross-section and sizing tables, while Block 1 shows adjusting rings and alternative section details. READ Block 8 for minimum manhole diameter to pipe size requirements. Use VISION on both blocks to examine the structural geometry, base slab configurations, and optional step placements.\n*   **Blocks 6, 7 & 9: diagrams — Storm Drain Manhole Ring and 813 mm (32\") Cover (City of Austin Std 503S-4S, Parts 1-3)**. Detailed drawings of the lid, ring section, and manufacturing notes. READ Block 9 for casting specifications, specific weight requirements, and load testing standards. Use VISION on Blocks 6 and 7 to examine the physical lid layout, pick bar placement, and machine finish details.\n*   **Block 5: diagram — Typical Box Manhole for 760 mm (30\") & Larger Pipe (City of Austin Std 506S-5)**. Cross-section of a cast-in-place box manhole with associated construction notes. READ the notes for concrete class and steel reinforcement requirements. Use VISION for spatial layout, reinforcement placement, and mortar details.\n*   **Blocks 2 & 4: diagrams — Manhole Plan Views**. Plan views illustrating a typical manhole at an angle (Block 2) and a typical junction manhole (Block 4) showing intersecting pipe diameters. Use VISION to examine the flow inverts, pipe configurations, and how the manhole invert must be formed to provide smooth water flow.\n\n---\n\n- `block-7.md` — diagram: Detailed diagram and specifications for a catch basin, including model dimensions, grate options, an\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
