{"level":30,"time":1776704920249,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CdXQwaYQuDAeL4HTeJ4ABA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Consolidated Site Plan Application\n     2→\n     3→Completeness check submittal for a consolidated site plan permit application in the City of Austin.\n     4→\n     5→## Sections\n     6→\n     7→1. **Project Information** (pp. 1-2)\n     8→   Details the project type, name, street address, proposed development description, and legal deed references.\n     9→   File: `01-project-information.md`\n    10→2. **Contacts Information** (pp. 2-3)\n    11→   Provides contact details for the applicant, owner, engineer, and other professionals involved in the project.\n    12→   File: `02-contacts-information.md`\n    13→3. **Property Attributes** (pp. 3-4)\n    14→   Outlines jurisdictional boundaries, housing program participation, watershed details, and street/neighborhood plans for the site.\n    15→   File: `03-property-attributes.md`\n    16→4. **Application Assessment and Site Area** (p. 5)\n    17→   Contains traffic impact analysis requirements, site area calculations, existing/proposed zoning use tables, and impervious cover percentages.\n    18→   File: `04-application-assessment-and-site-area.md`\n    19→5. **Land Use, Waivers, and Arborist Review** (p. 6)\n    20→   Details compatibility standards, requested waivers or variances, and tree counts within and adjacent to the limits of construction.\n    21→   File: `05-land-use-waivers-and-arborist-review.md`\n    22→6. **Authorizations and Acknowledgments** (pp. 7-8)\n    23→   Contains applicant signatures for submittal verification, inspection authorization, and general acknowledgments regarding property restrictions.\n    24→   File: `06-authorizations-and-acknowledgments.md`\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dccfafa3-f785-4cc2-a45b-b26d9e2e76f8","uuid":"a0dc64bc-04a1-4510-b674-ef46efd4dba8","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/consolidated-site-plan-application/overview.md","content":"# Consolidated Site Plan Application\n\nCompleteness check submittal for a consolidated site plan permit application in the City of Austin.\n\n## Sections\n\n1. **Project Information** (pp. 1-2)\n   Details the project type, name, street address, proposed development description, and legal deed references.\n   File: `01-project-information.md`\n2. **Contacts Information** (pp. 2-3)\n   Provides contact details for the applicant, owner, engineer, and other professionals involved in the project.\n   File: `02-contacts-information.md`\n3. **Property Attributes** (pp. 3-4)\n   Outlines jurisdictional boundaries, housing program participation, watershed details, and street/neighborhood plans for the site.\n   File: `03-property-attributes.md`\n4. **Application Assessment and Site Area** (p. 5)\n   Contains traffic impact analysis requirements, site area calculations, existing/proposed zoning use tables, and impervious cover percentages.\n   File: `04-application-assessment-and-site-area.md`\n5. **Land Use, Waivers, and Arborist Review** (p. 6)\n   Details compatibility standards, requested waivers or variances, and tree counts within and adjacent to the limits of construction.\n   File: `05-land-use-waivers-and-arborist-review.md`\n6. **Authorizations and Acknowledgments** (pp. 7-8)\n   Contains applicant signatures for submittal verification, inspection authorization, and general acknowledgments regarding property restrictions.\n   File: `06-authorizations-and-acknowledgments.md`\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
