 no mention of \"kV\" or specific voltage numbers). Furthermore, the words \"distribution\" or \"transmission\" do not appear anywhere on this plan, including in the \"Utility Notes\" section.\n\n**3. References to utility poles, pad-mounted equipment, or overhead conductors:**\n*   **Pad-mounted equipment:** The plan explicitly labels several proposed pad-mounted structures throughout the site. The exact text used for these labels is **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Overhead conductors:** The overhead lines are indicated by the dashed lines labeled **\"OHE\"** mentioned in point 1. The specific term \"overhead conductors\" is not used.\n*   **Utility poles:** While there are circular symbols with dots in the center (and sometimes lines indicating guy wires) placed along the \"OHE\" lines—which are standard visual symbols for utility poles—there is **no explicit text label** stating \"Utility Pole\" on this document.\n*   **Other equipment:** The plan also explicitly labels numerous instances of an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** and **\"Electrical Meters\"** along the proposed underground routes.\n\n**4. Relationship between electrical design plan and the southeast corner:**\nLooking at the southeast area of the property (the bottom right corner of the drawing area, near Building 6 / Unit 603):\n*   The proposed electrical infrastructure on this plan (indicated by the solid blue lines representing the \"Underground Electric Line\") routes closely around the proposed buildings.\n*   Relative to the absolute southeast corner of the property lines, the proposed electrical equipment is set back toward the interior of the lot.\n*   Specifically, on the east side of Building 6 (near the SE corner of the site), there is an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** and a bank of **\"Electrical Meters\"** attached to the building.\n*   There are no proposed \"Electrical Transformer Pads\" located in the immediate southeast corner; the closest one is located to the west, between Building 6 and Building 7.\n*   The extreme southeast corner of the property boundary itself appears devoid of *proposed* electrical infrastructure on this plan. However, the existing overhead line labeled **\"OHE\"** runs horizontally along the outside of the southern property boundary, passing adjacent to this southeast corner area.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1478,"outputTokens":643,"totalTokens":4324,"reasoningTokens":2203},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine this electrical design plan and identify:\n\n1. Whether any overhead electric lines or dis