ne passes through the southern edge of its drawn canopy. The trunk of this tree is located further north of the overhead line compared to Trees 1 and 2.\n\n**(3) Whether any tree IDs/tag numbers are labeled:**\nYes, there are small text labels placed next to the center points (trunks) of the tree symbols, which indicate tree IDs or tag numbers. However, due to the resolution of the image and the very small size of the text, the specific numbers for the trees along the southern \"- OHE -\" line are **text unclear** and cannot be transcribed accurately."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b2822d9-59e1-40b7-8c44-f04e0d31c7f2","uuid":"44c0b5ea-6ac8-4029-9602-13385452fed3","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"EXISTING TREE PLAN\" document, here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**(4) Whether the overhead electric line is shown on this plan:**\nYes, the overhead electric line is explicitly shown. It is represented by a dashed line interspersed with the text label \"**- OHE -**\". This line runs horizontally along the southern property boundary (the bottom edge of the drawing), and another similar line runs along the western boundary.\n\n**(1) & (2) Existing trees shown near or beneath the overhead electric line at the southern property boundary, their locations, and approximate distances:**\nScanning the southern boundary (bottom of the plan) from west to east along the \"- OHE -\" line, there are three distinct existing tree symbols shown in close proximity to or beneath the line:\n\n*   **Tree 1 (South of Bldg. 8, Unit 805):** Located centrally along the southern boundary, directly south of the building footprint labeled \"Bldg. 8\", specifically near \"Unit 805\". The dashed \"- OHE -\" line passes directly through the outer circle representing the tree's canopy. The trunk (indicated by the center dot) is located just slightly north of the overhead line.\n*   **Tree 2 (South of Bldg. 8, Unit 806):** Located immediately east of Tree 1, directly south of \"Unit 806\". Similar to Tree 1, the \"- OHE -\" line intersects the southern portion of its drawn canopy. Its trunk is also located slightly north of the overhead line.\n*   **Tree 3 (Southeast area, south of Bldg. 6):** Located towards the southeast corner of the site plan, south of the building labeled \"Bldg. 6\" (near \"Unit 604\"). The dashed \"- OHE -\" line passes through the southern edge of its drawn canopy. The trunk of this tree is located further north of the overhead line compared to Trees 1 and 2.\n\n**(3) Whether any tree IDs/tag numbers are labeled:**\nYes, there are small text labels placed next to the center points (trunks) of the tree symbols, which indicate tree IDs or tag numbers. However, due to the resolution of the image and the very small size of the text, the specific numbers for the trees along the southern \"- OHE -\" line are **text unclear** and cannot be transcribed accurately."}]}
