{"level":30,"time":1776705408378,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017LmSCychFoeGQUPMhMK89c","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 10 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — The block contains a technical drawing of a \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" sign, which is City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6. The drawing includes dimensions for the sign and its text, as well as notes regarding the background and lettering colors.\n     4→\n     5→Drawing of a rectangular sign with rounded corners.\n     6→Text on sign:\n     7→NO\n     8→PARKING\n     9→FIRE\n    10→ZONE\n    11→[left/right arrow symbol]\n    12→TOW-AWAY\n    13→ZONE\n    14→Dimensions are provided for the overall sign size (305 mm x 457 mm), letter heights (ranging from 38 mm to 76.2 mm), and spacing between lines of text. The arrow symbol is 19 mm x 76 mm.\n    15→Notes at the bottom left state:\n    16→LETTERING, ARROW AND BORDER - RED TRANSPARENT\n    17→BACKGROUND - SILVER REFLECTIVE SHEETING\n    18→NOTE: ARROW MAY BE LEFT, RIGHT, OR DOUBLE\n    19→Title block at the bottom states:\n    20→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    21→FIRE DEPARTMENT\n    22→RESTRICTED ZONE SIGNS, TYPE II\n    23→[Signature]\n    24→9/16/92\n    25→ADOPTED\n    26→THE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD\n    27→STANDARD NO.\n    28→901S-6\n    29→\n    30→## Block 2: drawing — The block contains a detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8), units, parking areas, fire lanes, fire hydrants, concrete walls, sidewalks, and various easements. It also includes elevation contours, property lines, and adjacent streets like Valley View Road. The drawing includes annotations for building dimensions, square footage, Finished Floor Elevations (FFE), and existing features like a wastewater manhole and existing trees. The drawing is a plan view with a north arrow pointing up and slightly to the right.\n    31→\n    32→Site plan drawing showing the proposed development. \n    33→- **Bldg. 1**: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n    34→- **Bldg. 2**: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    35→- **Bldg. 3**: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    36→- **Bldg. 4**: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    37→- **Bldg. 5**: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    38→- **Bldg. 6**: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    39→- **Bldg. 7**: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n    40→- **Bldg. 8**: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    41→Features include fire lanes, proposed fire hydrants, existing fire hydrants, concrete walls, wood fences, guardrails, sidewalks, and various easements (drainage, electric, telecommunication, water, wastewater). Property boundary lines are shown with bearings and distances. Adjacent properties and streets are labeled. Elevation contours are visible.\n    42→\n    43→## Block 3: notes — The block contains two disclaimer notes regarding the application and the location of existing utilities.\n    44→\n    45→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\n    46→applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\n    47→submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    48→\n    49→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\n    50→match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\n    51→locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\n    52→construction.\n    53→\n    54→## Block 4: notes — The block contains a numbered list of Fire Zone Notes, specifying requirements for signage, painting, underground mains, and private hydrants.\n    55→\n    56→Fire Zone Notes\n    57→1. Restricted Zone signage to be placed on front of lockers and along boat slip retaining walls as necessary or\n    58→required.\n    59→2. Stencil the words \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" in white letters at least 4\" high at 30 foot intervals along the\n    60→curb and the entire curb shall be painted red to serve as the background for the white letters.\n    61→3. Signs stating \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" shall be posted at both ends of a fire zone and at each entry\n    62→and exit point which constitutes a portion of the fire zone or fire lane. Signs shall comply with Standard City of\n    63→Austin Detail 901S-6.\n    64→4. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA-24, and the\n    65→Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at\n    66→one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n    67→5. All private hydrants shall be painted red.\n    68→\n    69→## Block 5: notes — The block contains the legal description of the property.\n    70→\n    71→Legal Description\n    72→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    73→\n    74→## Block 6: notes — The block contains a numbered list of general Notes regarding the installation and testing of underground mains for sprinkler systems and private hydrants, as well as the location of a Knox-box.\n    75→\n    76→Notes\n    77→1. Underground mains feeding NFPAR 13 sprinkler systems must be installed and tested in accordance with\n    78→NFPAR 13, and the Fire Code, by a licensed sprinkler contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must\n    79→be hydrostatically tested at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n    80→2. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA 24, and\n    81→the Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested\n    82→at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n    83→3. The Knox-box is to be located at exterior fire riser room door (non-hinged side).\n    84→\n    85→## Block 7: notes — The block contains a brief note directing the reader to another sheet for fire flow test results.\n    86→\n    87→Fire Flow Test\n    88→See Sheet 18, Austin Water General Notes, for the fire flow test results.\n    89→\n    90→## Block 8: notes — The block contains a note regarding the requirements for private fire hydrants on the property, per the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility Special Services Division.\n    91→\n    92→City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\n    93→This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin\n    94→Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of\n    95→this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced,\n    96→maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project\n    97→includes __1__ private hydrants.\n    98→\n    99→## Block 9: notes — The block provides information on two benchmarks, including their location, elevation, and datum.\n   100→\n   101→Benchmarks\n   102→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n   103→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n   104→\n   105→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n   106→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n   107→\n   108→## Block 10: notes — The block contains a note specifying the required fire suppression system for all buildings.\n   109→\n   110→Fire Riser Room Note\n   111→All buildings are to have a NFPA 13D fire suppression system.\n   112→\n   113→## Block 11: notes — The block contains a brief note directing the reader to the landscape plan for the tree list.\n   114→\n   115→Tree List\n   116→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n   117→\n   118→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d43314f-ffee-4c09-9531-73169237fb4a","uuid":"27bd992f-03d3-453d-99ed-29515edd5178","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 10 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — The block contains a technical drawing of a \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" sign, which is City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6. The drawing includes dimensions for the sign and its text, as well as notes regarding the background and lettering colors.\n\nDrawing of a rectangular sign with rounded corners.\nText on sign:\nNO\nPARKING\nFIRE\nZONE\n[left/right arrow symbol]\nTOW-AWAY\nZONE\nDimensions are provided for the overall sign size (305 mm x 457 mm), letter heights (ranging from 38 mm to 76.2 mm), and spacing between lines of text. The arrow symbol is 19 mm x 76 mm.\nNotes at the bottom left state:\nLETTERING, ARROW AND BORDER - RED TRANSPARENT\nBACKGROUND - SILVER REFLECTIVE SHEETING\nNOTE: ARROW MAY BE LEFT, RIGHT, OR DOUBLE\nTitle block at the bottom states:\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nFIRE DEPARTMENT\nRESTRICTED ZONE SIGNS, TYPE II\n[Signature]\n9/16/92\nADOPTED\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD\nSTANDARD NO.\n901S-6\n\n## Block 2: drawing — The block contains a detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8), units, parking areas, fire lanes, fire hydrants, concrete walls, sidewalks, and various easements. It also includes elevation contours, property lines, and adjacent streets like Valley View Road. The drawing includes annotations for building dimensions, square footage, Finished Floor Elevations (FFE), and existing features like a wastewater manhole and existing trees. The drawing is a plan view with a north arrow pointing up and slightly to the right.\n\nSite plan drawing showing the proposed development. \n- **Bldg. 1**: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n- **Bldg. 2**: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n- **Bldg. 3**: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n- **Bldg. 4**: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n- **Bldg. 5**: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n- **Bldg. 6**: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n- **Bldg. 7**: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n- **Bldg. 8**: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\nFeatures include fire lanes, proposed fire hydrants, existing fire hydrants, concrete walls, wood fences, guardrails, sidewalks, and various easements (drainage, electric, telecommunication, water, wastewater). Property boundary lines are shown with bearings and distances. Adjacent properties and streets are labeled. Elevation contours are visible.\n\n## Block 3: notes — The block contains two disclaimer notes regarding the application and the location of existing utilities.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\napplicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\nsubmittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\nmatch locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\nlocations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\nconstruction.\n\n## Block 4: notes — The block contains a numbered list of Fire Zone Notes, specifying requirements for signage, painting, underground mains, and private hydrants.\n\nFire Zone Notes\n1. Restricted Zone signage to be placed on front of lockers and along boat slip retaining walls as necessary or\nrequired.\n2. Stencil the words \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" in white letters at least 4\" high at 30 foot intervals along the\ncurb and the entire curb shall be painted red to serve as the background for the white letters.\n3. Signs stating \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" shall be posted at both ends of a fire zone and at each entry\nand exit point which constitutes a portion of the fire zone or fire lane. Signs shall comply with Standard City of\nAustin Detail 901S-6.\n4. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA-24, and the\nFire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at\none time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n5. All private hydrants shall be painted red.\n\n## Block 5: notes — The block contains the legal description of the property.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 6: notes — The block contains a numbered list of general Notes regarding the installation and testing of underground mains for sprinkler systems and private hydrants, as well as the location of a Knox-box.\n\nNotes\n1. Underground mains feeding NFPAR 13 sprinkler systems must be installed and tested in accordance with\nNFPAR 13, and the Fire Code, by a licensed sprinkler contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must\nbe hydrostatically tested at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n2. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA 24, and\nthe Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested\nat one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n3. The Knox-box is to be located at exterior fire riser room door (non-hinged side).\n\n## Block 7: notes — The block contains a brief note directing the reader to another sheet for fire flow test results.\n\nFire Flow Test\nSee Sheet 18, Austin Water General Notes, for the fire flow test results.\n\n## Block 8: notes — The block contains a note regarding the requirements for private fire hydrants on the property, per the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility Special Services Division.\n\nCity of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\nThis project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin\nFire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of\nthis obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced,\nmaintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project\nincludes __1__ private hydrants.\n\n## Block 9: notes — The block provides information on two benchmarks, including their location, elevation, and datum.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 10: notes — The block contains a note specifying the required fire suppression system for all buildings.\n\nFire Riser Room Note\nAll buildings are to have a NFPA 13D fire suppression system.\n\n## Block 11: notes — The block contains a brief note directing the reader to the landscape plan for the tree list.\n\nTree List\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
