{"level":30,"time":1776705412838,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Can you identify: 1) The location of the overhead electric line (OHE) shown on the grading plan; 2) Are there any driveways, parking areas, or roads shown directly under or crossing the overhead electric line; 3) Are there any vertical clearance dimensions shown from the finished grade or road surface to the overhead electric line; 4) Are there any section views or profile details that show vertical clearances under the overhead line?","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (11)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705416084,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TAQdYH7ZDa494T8c7UjUne","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good findings! There are existing trees with canopies that intersect the overhead electric line area - the OHE line passes through or very near the tree canopies. This is significant. \n\nNow let me compile my comprehensive research summary and begin evaluating the checklist items systematically. Let me create a research summary of what I found:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n**APPLICABILITY:** YES - The site has overhead electric infrastructure shown on the existing conditions survey and the site plan.\n\n**OVERHEAD ELECTRIC INFRASTRUCTURE FOUND:**\n1. Existing overhead utility poles and lines shown on Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4)\n2. Marked as \"O.H. ELECTRIC\" (Overhead Electric)\n3. Runs along southern property boundary\n4. Electric easements labeled: 5' Electric Easements (multiple references to Vol. 69, Vol. 73, etc.)\n5. Also references to transmission structures based on Sheet 3 notes\n\n**LOCATIONS:**\n- Main overhead line runs along south/southwest property boundary adjacent to Valley View Road\n- Site plan shows poles and line labeled \"OHE\" at southern boundary\n- Line crosses at driveway entrance\n- Buildings 7 and 8 are closest to the line\n\n**CRITICAL FINDINGS:**\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n1. **NO CLEARANCE DIMENSIONS** - Site plan shows OHE line but includes NO dimensioned clearance annotations:\n   - No horizontal clearance from buildings to outside conductor\n   - No vertical clearance for driveway (16-18 feet required per UCM § 1.10.6.2)\n   - No radial clearance zones shown\n   - No dimension lines originating from \"outside conductor\" as required\n\n2. **NO BUILDING ELEVATIONS** with conductor elevation data:\n   - No building elevation sheets provided\n   - Cannot verify vertical clearances from roof/projections to conductors\n   - Cannot verify 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance for buildings\n   \n3. The landscape plan proposes trees near the OHE line, but species aren't identified, so I can't confirm they're utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F. No setback distances are marked from the line to plantings, and I can't verify the 10-lateral-foot requirement for distribution lines is met. The driveway passes under or near the OHE line at the southern boundary, yet no vertical clearance dimension appears on the plans, and there's no profile showing how the driveway grade relates to the conductor elevation.\n\n4. Without registered surveyor data for pole locations and conductor heights, I cannot determine if the required 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearances are adequate. The existing trees shown beneath the OHE line lack clear species identification and UC status verification, and their removal or retention isn't clearly coordinated with clearance requirements. Additionally, the notes reference transmission structures with 25-foot clearance zones and down guys, but it's unclear whether these are the same facilities shown on the overhead line plans.\n\nService-drop routing and clearances aren't identified anywhere. There are no cross-sections or elevation views showing clearances from conductors to building faces, driveway grades, fence tops, or retaining walls. The documentation also doesn't clearly distinguish whether the lines are distribution or transmission—Facts.md references 5-foot electric easements typical of distribution, while Sheet 3 notes suggest transmission facilities with different easement requirements, creating ambiguity about which standard applies.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1536,"cache_read_input_tokens":64642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1536},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b2822d9-59e1-40b7-8c44-f04e0d31c7f2","uuid":"f74410e0-3faa-4f42-8e91-215fb2911295"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705417982,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TAQdYH7ZDa494T8c7UjUne","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan documents, I now have sufficient evidence to evaluate all checklist items. Let me proceed with the systematic evaluation.\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY - Critical Findings:**\n\n✓ **OVERHEAD ELECTRIC INFRASTRUCTURE EXISTS** - Utility poles and overhead lines clearly shown on Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) and Site Plan (Sheet 9), marked as \"O.H. ELECTRIC\" running along southern property boundary\n\n✗ **MAJOR DEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED:**\n1. **NO CLEARANCE DIMENSIONS SHOWN** - Site plan shows overhead line but includes zero dimensioned clearance annotations to buildings, driveway, or other features\n2. **NO BUILDING ELEVATIONS** with overhead conductor elevation data - Cannot verify vertical clearances\n3. **NO VERTICAL CLEARANCE FOR DRIVEWAY** - Entrance driveway shown passing under overhead line with no elevation data or clearance verification\n4. **TREE SPECIES NOT IDENTIFIED** - Landscape plan shows trees adjacent to overhead line but species not labeled; cannot verify UC (utility-compatible) status per ECM Appendix F\n5. **EXISTING TREES UNDER OVERHEAD LINE** - Existing tree plan shows multiple trees with canopies beneath/adjacent to OHE line; species/UC status not verified\n6. **NO SURVEYED CONDUCTOR ELEVATION DATA** - No registered surveyor data for pole locations or conductor elevations; no mid-span clearance measurements\n7. **NO SECTION/PROFILE VIEWS** - No cross-sections showing clearances from conductors to buildings, driveways, walls, or other features\n8. **TRANSMISSION FACILITIES REFERENCED** but not clearly distinguished from distribution lines\n\nNow I'll evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1536,"cache_read_input_tokens":64642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1536},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b2822d9-59e1-40b7-8c44-f04e0d31c7f2","uuid":"b8100f33-50ec-418f-b6e1-6fcab275b5eb"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705418024,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UW1fUfVKYfU6LggTVwvRPb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good information. So:\n1. There ARE overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on the electrical plan along the south and west boundaries\n2. The voltage level is NOT specified on the electrical plan (no kV designation shown)\n3. There ARE utility poles indicated (circular symbols with dots)\n4. There are pad-mounted electrical transformers proposed at the site\n5. The extreme southeast corner appears to have the existing overhead line running along the south boundary\n\nThe fact that the voltage is NOT specified is a problem. Without knowing if it's distribution (< 60kV) or transmission (≥ 60kV), it's difficult to determine the applicable clearance zones.\n\nHowever, the grouping document notes: \"Most overhead facilities on typical development sites are distribution unless explicitly labeled as transmission or located within transmission easements.\"\n\nSo I should probably treat this as distribution (< 60kV) since:\n1. It's not explicitly labeled as transmission\n2. There's no mention of transmission easements in this area (though there are other easements)\n3. This is a typical townhome development site\n\nWith distribution voltage, the clearance requirements are:\n- < 15 ft lateral: Only utility-compatible trees\n- 15-25 ft lateral: Utility-compatible OR trees < 40 ft mature height\n- > 25 ft lateral: All trees OK\n- From pole: 10 ft minimum from any tree\n- Pad-mounted: 10 ft from any tree\n- Underground: 5 ft from any tree, 20 ft requires root barriers\n\nThe problem is that I still don't know:\n1. Which species the three southeast corner trees are\n2. Their mature heights\n3. Whether they're utility-compatible\n\nGiven that the three trees are marked as \"M\" (mitigation trees), they're likely being planted as mitigation for tree removal. From the plant schedule:\n- 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal) - shade trees\n- 2 Live Oak (100 gal) - shade trees\n\n\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal) - ornamental trees\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal) - ornamental trees\n\nBut the landscape plan shows \"M\" symbols without identifying which species are planted at each location. This is a plant identification problem—the plan proposes trees near the overhead electric line but doesn't specify species assignments. This appears to be EL-2.10: \"Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities.\"\n\nThe plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists the species available, yet fails to connect them to the specific tree locations on the plan. Since I can't determine which species are actually planted near the overhead electric facilities, this constitutes a FAIL. The deficiency exists because the schedule doesn't adequately link species to locations. Without this information, I also cannot verify other requirements like EL-2.1 (non-UC trees within 15 ft of distribution conductors) or EL-2.2 (non-UC trees within 50 ft), as those checks depend on knowing both the species and their exact distances from the electric facilities. CAN'T VERIFY if we don't know species. EL-2.12 and EL-2.13 both show the same issue—no clearance dimensions are provided on the plans at all, just tree canopies shown as circles without distance callouts. EL-2.14 displays trees in relation to overhead facilities, but again without dimensioned clearances. EL-2.15 requires checking whether Austin Energy approval is documented for any trees in prohibited zones.\n\nThe definitive failures emerging are the missing species identification for trees adjacent to overhead electric lines and the complete absence of dimensioned clearances between tree canopies and conductors.\n\nI should measure the actual distances from those three trees at the southeast corner to the overhead electric line to determine if they violate the clearance standards.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2237,"cache_read_input_tokens":57081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2237},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"6498469c-5952-4455-b29a-6f6094bc71d3"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705418041,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UW1fUfVKYfU6LggTVwvRPb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is helpful. The overhead lines are shown but their voltage classification is not specified. In this case, per the grouping guidance, I should treat them as distribution (< 60kV) since they're not explicitly labeled as transmission and there are no transmission easements noted.\n\nNow let me measure the actual distance from those three southeast corner mitigation trees to the overhead electric line to determine if they violate clearance requirements."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2237,"cache_read_input_tokens":57081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2237},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"dd0e82f6-8051-4964-90b8-23f609296261"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705421532,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UW1fUfVKYfU6LggTVwvRPb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VUkTNj9jy6z63hrLPwXQtt","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__run_measure_distance","input":{"reasoning":"The landscape plan visually shows three mitigation trees (\"M\" symbols) in the southeast corner with their drawn canopy circles overlapping the overhead electric (OHE) line at the southern property boundary. The grouping requires verification of tree clearances from overhead electric conductors. I need to measure the actual lateral distance from each of these three tree trunks (planting locations) to the overhead electric line to determine if they violate UCM § 1.10.10.4 clearance requirements for distribution lines (15 ft for non-UC trees, 25 ft for large trees). The visual overlap of the drawn canopy circles suggests potential violations, but actual trunk-to-conductor distances must be measured to confirm.","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"scaleInchesPerFoot":0.05,"objectPairs":[{"objectA":"First mitigation tree (M) in southeast corner - trunk center point","objectB":"Overhead Electric line (OHE) at southern property boundary"},{"objectA":"Second mitigation tree (M) in southeast corner - trunk center point","objectB":"Overhead Electric line (OHE) at southern property boundary"},{"objectA":"Third mitigation tree (M) in southeast corner - trunk center point","objectB":"Overhead Electric line (OHE) at southern property boundary"}],"applicable_checklist_items":[{"checklist_id":"EL-2.1","checklist_deficiency_text":"Non-utility-compatible trees proposed within 15 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment"},{"checklist_id":"EL-2.3","checklist_deficiency_text":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) proposed within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment"},{"checklist_id":"EL-2.6","checklist_deficiency_text":"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility pole"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2237,"cache_read_input_tokens":57081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2237},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"14c60972-369b-4a06-827d-00e43eaf058a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705421535,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","tool":"run_measure_distance","command":"npx tsx /Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/workflows/review/scripts/measure-distance.ts --outputPath='/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/output/measure-distance.json' --reasoning='The landscape plan visually shows three mitigation trees (\"M\" symbols) in the southeast corner with their drawn canopy circles overlapping the overhead electric (OHE) line at the southern property boundary. The grouping requires verification of tree clearances from overhead electric conductors. I need to measure the actual lateral distance from each of these three tree trunks (planting locations) to the overhead electric line to determine if they violate UCM § 1.10.10.4 clearance requirements for distribution lines (15 ft for non-UC trees, 25 ft for large trees). The visual overlap of the drawn canopy circles suggests potential violations, but actual trunk-to-conductor distances must be measured to confirm.' --applicable_checklist_items='[{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-2.1\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Non-utility-compatible trees proposed within 15 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-2.3\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) proposed within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-2.6\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility pole\"}]' --documentId='1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777' --sheetNum='31' --objectPairs='[{\"objectA\":\"First mitigation tree (M) in southeast corner - trunk center point\",\"objectB\":\"Overhead Electric line (OHE) at southern property boundary\"},{\"objectA\":\"Second mitigation tree (M) in southeast corner - trunk center point\",\"objectB\":\"Overhead Electric line (OHE) at southern property boundary\"},{\"objectA\":\"Third mitigation tree (M) in southeast corner - trunk center point\",\"objectB\":\"Overhead Electric line (OHE) at southern property boundary\"}]' --scaleInchesPerFoot='0.05'","msg":"Executing typed script tool"}
