{"level":30,"time":1776705569913,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015EAn6P2t9ynSKkWayj8JMK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Site Plan Review Summary - EL-1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\nI have completed the comprehensive review of grouping **EL-1** for the Valley View Townhomes project. Here's what I found:\n\n### **APPLICABILITY: YES**\nThe site has existing overhead electric infrastructure clearly documented on the Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) and shown on the Site Plan (Sheet 9), marked as \"O.H. ELECTRIC\" running along the southern property boundary adjacent to Valley View Road.\n\n### **KEY FINDINGS**\n\n**Overhead Infrastructure Present:**\n- Utility poles and overhead electric lines at southern property boundary\n- Electric easements labeled (5' Electric Easements)\n- Poles positioned where driveway entrance and buildings are located\n- Existing trees with canopies beneath/adjacent to overhead lines\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n\n1. **NO CLEARANCE DIMENSIONS SHOWN** - The most pervasive deficiency:\n   - Site plan shows overhead line but contains ZERO dimension lines from the outside conductor to buildings, driveways, walls, or other features\n   - No vertical clearance shown for driveway\n   - No horizontal/radial clearance zones dimensioned\n\n2. **MISSING BUILDING ELEVATIONS** - Required surveyor data absent:\n   - No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n   - No clearance dimensions from conductors to building faces or projections\n   - Buildings 7 and 8 nearest to overhead line with no verification of compliance\n\n3. **DRIVEWAY VERTICAL CLEARANCE UNVERIFIED**:\n   - Driveway entrance passes under/near overhead line\n   - No profile/section showing finish grade elevation relative to overhead conductors\n   - No verification of 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearance requirement\n\n4. **TREE SPECIES NOT IDENTIFIED**:\n   - Landscape plan shows trees adjacent to overhead line\n   - Trees labeled only by category (SY, M, PL, P) - NOT by species\n   - Cannot verify compliance with ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible species requirement\n\n5. **GUY WIRE CONFLICTS NOT RESOLVED**:\n   - Existing conditions survey shows guy anchors near driveway\n   - Down guy anchor locations not clearly documented or resolved\n\n### **FINDINGS SUMMARY**\nI identified **18 deficient items**:\n- **7 items marked FAIL** - Missing required documentation/clearances\n- **11 items marked NOT-VERIFIABLE** - Evidence insufficient to determine compliance\n\nAll findings have been returned in the structured output format for processing."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4537,"cache_read_input_tokens":75098,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4537},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b2822d9-59e1-40b7-8c44-f04e0d31c7f2","uuid":"085dcefb-4530-4643-981e-16c3c20839c3"}
