{"level":30,"time":1776705569917,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015wZm1ohiyQpPWjMciHvgR5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Grading Plan (Sheet 11 of 39 for Valley View Townhomes), here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**1. All retaining walls shown and their locations relative to transformer pads**\nSeveral retaining walls are explicitly labeled along the perimeter of the site. They are labeled exactly as follows:\n*   **Top Right (Near Bldg. 5):** \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\" (with TW/BW elevation callouts).\n*   **Right Edge (Near Bldg. 5 and 6):** \"Existing Stone Retaining Wall\".\n*   **Bottom Right (Near Bldg. 6):** \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\".\n*   **Bottom Edge (Moving right to left):** Multiple callouts stating \"Existing Retaining Wall\". Near the middle-left of the bottom edge, a note reads \"Tie into existing Retaining Wall / Match existing Wall Elevations\". Further left, a callout reads \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n*   **Transformer Pads:** After a thorough scan of the entire sheet, **no transformer pads are shown or labeled** on this Grading Plan. There are small square pads behind the residential units, but these are clearly labeled \"AC\" (Air Conditioning). Because no transformer pads are depicted, their locations relative to the retaining walls cannot be determined from this document.\n\n**2. Dimension callouts showing distances from transformer pads to retaining walls**\nBecause no transformer pads are located on this plan, there are **no dimension callouts** showing distances from transformer pads to retaining walls.\n\n**3. Any cross-sections or elevation profiles shown**\nThis document is strictly a plan (top-down) view. **No cross-sections or elevation profiles are drawn on this sheet.** There are a couple of detail callouts enclosed in dashed ovals (e.g., \"X5.2\" near Bldg. 5 and \"X5.3\" near Bldg. 6), which likely reference cross-sections or details located on a different sheet in the plan set, but the visual profiles themselves are not present here.\n\n**4. Drainage direction/flow patterns indicated around transformer pad locations**\nBecause transformer pads are not shown, drainage specifically around them cannot be analyzed. However, general site drainage is heavily indicated:\n*   **General Flow:** Dozens of small directional arrows show surface water flow patterns. The arrows predominantly indicate flow moving away from the building footprints (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) and directing runoff into the central drive aisles, parking areas, and designated drainage swales.\n*   The overall site topography slopes downward from the rear/right side of the property (elevations around 685-686) toward the front/left entrance (elevations dropping to around 679-680). \n\n**5. Transformer pads shown on plan and easement area status**\nAs previously noted, **transformer pads are not shown** on this Grading Plan. \nWhile the pads themselves are missing, there are several clearly marked utility and drainage easements where such infrastructure might be intended to go, including:\n*   \"5' Electric Easement\" along the right property boundary.\n*   \"3' Elec. Easement\" along the bottom boundary.\n*   \"15' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" near the bottom right corner.\n*   Various \"P.U.E.\" (Public Utility Easement), \"Drainage Easement\", and \"Wastewater Easement\" areas throughout the site."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fa6dd19-b9c0-47f2-aaf9-fa9fde6b7270","uuid":"ec5befb2-f2ae-4b6d-85d3-7c9610890d0d","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Grading Plan (Sheet 11 of 39 for Valley View Townhomes), here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**1. All retai