**\"SY,M\"**.\n\n**3. Other trees mixed in with or near SY trees:**\nYes. As noted above, the two southernmost trees in this specific grouping are labeled **\"SY,M\"**. According to the legend below the Key Notes, \"M\" stands for \"MITIGATION TREE\". This indicates these two trees are serving a dual purpose. There are no standalone \"PL\" or strictly \"M\" proposed trees located within the immediate shaded Street Yard (H-2) strip on the western boundary; other tree types are located further east into the site.\n\n**4. Approximate distance between proposed SY trees and the property line:**\nUsing a visual estimation based on the provided graphic scale in the bottom right corner (where the bar indicates 0 to 20 feet equals 1 inch), the center points of the proposed SY trees appear to be located approximately **10 to 15 feet** east of the western property line. They appear to be placed just to the east of the parallel \"-W-\" utility line.\n\n**5. Dimension callouts or clearance notes for trees in relation to utilities:**\n**No.** There are no explicit dimension lines (e.g., arrowed lines with distance measurements) or textual clearance notes provided in the western Street Yard area to indicate a required separation distance between the proposed trees and the adjacent \"-W-\" utility line or the property line."}]}
