{"level":30,"time":1776705581515,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014PCv4BCS3rmPGCgFA9nmkk","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 11 — Grading Plan\n     2→\n     3→This sheet displays the detailed grading plan for the development site.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   **Benchmark 1**: Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n    12→*   **Benchmark 2**: Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n    13→*   **Bldg 1**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 687.50\n    14→*   **Bldg 2**: 4,830 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    15→*   **Bldg 3**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    16→*   **Bldg 4**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    17→*   **Bldg 5**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n    18→*   **Bldg 6**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n    19→*   **Bldg 7**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.00\n    20→*   **Bldg 8**: 4,997 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    21→*   **ADA Ramp Maximum Slope**: 8.33%\n    22→*   **Level Landing Maximum Slope**: 2%\n    23→\n    24→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    25→\n    26→*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\n    27→*   **Block 7**: Plan legend detailing line types and symbols for contours, limits of construction, storm drains, curb details, and ADA compliance parameters. READ for exact symbol definitions and maximum allowable slopes.\n    28→*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n    29→*   **Block 5**: Curb grading note detailing conditions for catch curbs vs. spill curbs. READ for grading flow instructions. \n    30→*   **Block 6**: Tree list reference directing the user to landscape plan sheet 32. READ for sheet reference.\n    31→*   **Block 4**: Legal description of the subject property (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision). READ to confirm property identity.\n    32→*   **Block 1**: Graphic scale bar. READ to confirm the 1\" = 20' measurement baseline.\n    33→*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: Boilerplate & Administrative information, including the Texas 811 call warning, engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), project metadata (Sheet 11 of 39, Project No. RJ3 70496), title block, and standard utility and design disclaimers. READ for project details or administrative tracking; otherwise, these can be skipped during a technical review.\n    34→\n    35→---\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"7ebe8e15-98bf-4c38-bf6f-880dc707a11c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 11 — Grading Plan\n\nThis sheet displays the detailed grading plan for the development site.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n*   **Benchmark 1**: Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   **Benchmark 2**: Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   **Bldg 1**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 687.50\n*   **Bldg 2**: 4,830 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 3**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 4**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 5**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 6**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 7**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.00\n*   **Bldg 8**: 4,997 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **ADA Ramp Maximum Slope**: 8.33%\n*   **Level Landing Maximum Slope**: 2%\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\n*   **Block 7**: Plan legend detailing line types and symbols for contours, limits of construction, storm drains, curb details, and ADA compliance parameters. READ for exact symbol definitions and maximum allowable slopes.\n*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n*   **Block 5**: Curb grading note detailing conditions for catch curbs vs. spill curbs. READ for grading flow instructions. \n*   **Block 6**: Tree list reference directing the user to landscape plan sheet 32. READ for sheet reference.\n*   **Block 4**: Legal description of the subject property (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision). READ to confirm property identity.\n*   **Block 1**: Graphic scale bar. READ to confirm the 1\" = 20' measurement baseline.\n*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: Boilerplate & Administrative information, including the Texas 811 call warning, engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), project metadata (Sheet 11 of 39, Project No. RJ3 70496), title block, and standard utility and design disclaimers. READ for project details or administrative tracking; otherwise, these can be skipped during a technical review.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776705583320,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01EG6jxRHW9ExV4sU7YRC9Uh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have comprehensive evidence. Let me evaluate each checklist item systematically based on my research:\n\n## Research Summary - Key Findings\n\n**Evidence Gathered:**\n1. **5 transformer pads identified** on Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) at: NW (Bldg 1), W-Central (Bldg 2), SW (Bldg 8), E-Central (Bldg 4-5), SE (Bldg 7)\n2. **Clearances from buildings**: Measured 8.3-19.5 ft - all exceed 5-foot minimum\n3. **Clearances from sidewalks**: Measured 6.8-15.6 ft - all exceed 2-foot minimum  \n4. **CRITICAL DRAINAGE ISSUE**: Grading plan shows drainage at E-Central transformer (Bldg 4-5 location) flows TOWARD Building 5 foundation - FAIL for oil-filled equipment\n5. **Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)**: Does NOT show transformer locations or any vegetation clearances - CANNOT VERIFY tree/shrub requirements\n6. **NO AE Design Transformer Pad Details**: No AE-approved transformer pad specifications, bollard details, or pad dimensions found in site plan or supplementary docs\n7. **NO Transformer Easements**: Transformer easement widths not specified\n8. **NO Bollard Details**: No 4-inch diameter bollards or protective specifications provided despite potentially close proximity to parking/driveways\n9. **NO Transformer Service Type Documentation**: Whether single-phase or three-phase not specified in plans\n10. **Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10)**: Does not label transformer locations; unclear if any are within fire lanes\n11. **Utility Notes**: Refer to tree list on Sheet 32 for vegetation clearance verification\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Austin Energy Design written approvals or clearance reductions\n- Transformer pad detail sheets showing dimensions and specifications\n- Root barrier details for trees near transformers\n- Transformer easement boundaries and widths\n- Bollard specifications and placement details\n- Documentation of transformer service type (single-phase vs three-phase)\n- Oil-filled vs. dry-type transformer designation\n- Transformer accessibility easement requirements\n\nNow I'll evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3265,"cache_read_input_tokens":76066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3265},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dccfafa3-f785-4cc2-a45b-b26d9e2e76f8","uuid":"6c2f56d2-b3ff-4a12-9e2f-01aeb8ddf6fb"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705584935,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FTpzVsLbGHBv2gzPmNeBgw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014Vp4drpou9Y3eE1tzYZEr5","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building elevation sheets for all 8 proposed buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead electric conductors are not included on building elevation sheets. Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) documents overhead utility poles and lines along Valley View Road and crossing the property, but no registered surveyor data for conductor elevations or clearance verification from proposed buildings is provided on elevations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All 8 proposed buildings and their relationships to overhead electric line shown on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and building projections for clearance verification. Overhead utility line (marked OHE) is shown on site plan and landscape plan, but no dimension lines, callouts, or clearance annotations are provided demonstrating compliance with the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Northern and southern driveway entrances along Valley View Road where overhead electric lines span across the entry points"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways do not show minimum vertical clearance verification from lowest point of overhead electric facilities including telecommunications attachments. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows two driveway entrances (northern entrance west of Building 1 and southern entrance west of Building 8) that cross under the overhead utility line along Valley View Road, but no vertical clearance dimensions, mid-span clearance survey data, or section views are provided demonstrating compliance with the 16-foot minimum (for parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot minimum (for areas with truck traffic) vertical clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along overhead electric line where trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductors are not verified as being from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows a row of trees planted directly on or immediately adjacent to the overhead electric line (OHE) along the southern boundary. Plant list (Sheet 35) specifies 2 Live Oak and 10 Cedar Elm as shade trees to be planted in this location. These species are not utility-compatible and exceed the 20-foot mature height typically required for utility-compatible trees. No distance clearance dimensions are provided between tree planting locations and the conductor."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. Overhead electric poles and lines exist on the site (documented on existing conditions survey Sheet 4) and construction is proposed; the required 48-hour notification note per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 is absent from the cover sheet and general notes."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":76818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1066},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d43314f-ffee-4c09-9531-73169237fb4a","uuid":"7a7a7764-3adc-4454-8bcd-4e8b8badf5e2"}
