{"level":30,"time":1776705588463,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AYWek5dFKRNqTiSKVqvmRj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014FmuMhZ8BztUt5zhjnbWGu","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Please examine the grading plan and identify:\n\n1. Any easement boundaries shown on this plan, specifically:\n   - Transmission easement boundaries (these would typically be labeled as \"Transmission Easement\" or similar)\n   - Electric utility easements\n   - Drainage easements\n   - Public utility easements\n\n2. The location of these easements relative to the proposed buildings and proposed landscape areas\n\n3. Whether the two known problematic easements from the property facts (Greenbelt Access & Use Easement covering 0.31 acres in the NE interior, and City of Austin Drainage Easement covering 0.130 acres in the NE corner) are depicted on this plan\n\n4. Any notes or callouts about easement restrictions or tree planting prohibitions\n\nThis information will help determine if any proposed trees are located within transmission easement boundaries, which would violate EL-2.5 (categorical prohibition on trees within transmission easement boundaries)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2130,"cache_read_input_tokens":63325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2130},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"dd4fa230-f7f8-4049-a8b6-814f4dbed55b"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705588465,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Please examine the grading plan and identify:\n\n1. Any easement boundaries shown on this plan, specifically:\n   - Transmission easement boundaries (these would typically be labeled as \"Transmission Easement\" or similar)\n   - Electric utility easements\n   - Drainage easements\n   - Public utility easements\n\n2. The location of these easements relative to the proposed buildings and proposed landscape areas\n\n3. Whether the two known problematic easements from the property facts (Greenbelt Access & Use Easement covering 0.31 acres in the NE interior, and City of Austin Drainage Easement covering 0.130 acres in the NE corner) are depicted on this plan\n\n4. Any notes or callouts about easement restrictions or tree planting prohibitions\n\nThis information will help determine if any proposed trees are located within transmission easement boundaries, which would violate EL-2.5 (categorical prohibition on trees within transmission easement boundaries).","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (11)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705592671,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AtdUY4rvqDRqdvB64fxN2k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice that the construction details shown (sheets 22, 23) don't include transformer pad details. Let me check if any construction details sheets might have transformer specs. Based on the Sheet Index in the README, sheets 22-28 are construction details. Let me quickly verify if any of them mention transformer pads, and then I'll wrap up my evaluation based on what I've found.\n\nActually, let me consolidate my findings now. I have enough information to evaluate most items. Let me systematically go through each checklist item and determine pass/fail/n/a/not-verifiable:\n\n**Items I can definitively evaluate:**\n\nEL-13.1 (5-foot from buildings): PASS\n- Measurements show 7.6-20 feet clearance from all pads to buildings\n\nEL-13.7 (2-foot from sidewalks): FAIL (for pads 1 and 3)\n- Pad 1: 1.1 feet - FAIL\n- Pad 3: 0.5 feet - FAIL\n- Pads 2, 4, 5: PASS\n\nEL-13.10 (10-foot hot-stick clearance): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Clearances to \"open area\" not dimensioned; without specific hot-stick use area dimensions and location details, cannot verify\n\nEL-13.12 (5-foot from fire hydrants): PASS\n- Fire hydrants are 251.8-283 feet from nearest transformer pads\n\nEL-13.20 (5-foot between pads): PASS\n- All pad-to-pad distances exceed 5 feet (49.9-83 feet)\n\nEL-13.37 (AE Design-approved pad details): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- No transformer pad detail sheets visible in plan set\n- No specification of dimensions or single-phase/three-phase service visible\n\nEL-13.35 (Transformer easements shown): NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n\n- Easement labels for transformer pads aren't explicitly marked on the plan, though general electric easements are indicated. For the remaining items, I can't verify property ownership or easement restrictions from the electrical plan alone. EL-13.36 requires routing confirmation on private property, EL-13.33 needs property boundary verification against the plat, and EL-13.34 depends on comparing transformer pad locations against the grading plan's easement designations—information that isn't clearly cross-referenced in the available documentation.\n\nPad 1 clears the bollard requirement at 15.3 feet from the nearest parking curb. Cross-sections for overhead structures aren't provided on the grading plan, so clearances can't be verified. The equipment specifications don't indicate whether the transformers are oil-filled or dry-type, and drainage patterns around individual pads aren't shown, making it impossible to confirm compliance with drainage requirements.\n\nSeveral measurements still need to be taken against existing site features: retaining wall distances, fence clearances, and setbacks from building elements like balconies, overhangs, windows, and doors. I need to verify whether stairwells, fire escapes, or confined spaces exist on the property that would trigger additional clearance rules. The landscaping plan requires closer review for tree proximity requirements, and I haven't yet confirmed the locations of dumpsters\n\n, bike racks, and light poles relative to the transformer. Fire lanes are present and need distance verification. Utility line separations will require measurements, including checking for gas service and overhead lines—both for the 7.5-foot clearance and 15-foot radius conductor requirements. Niche requirements likely don't apply unless specifically proposed. Starting with measurements from the transformer pads to the retaining walls.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3441,"cache_read_input_tokens":76796,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3441},"