{"level":30,"time":1776705784640,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Please examine the grading plan and identify:\n\n1. Any easement boundaries shown on this plan, specifically:\n   - Transmission easement boundaries (these would typically be labeled as \"Transmission Easement\" or similar)\n   - Electric utility easements\n   - Drainage easements\n   - Public utility easements\n\n2. The location of these easements relative to the proposed buildings and proposed landscape areas\n\n3. Whether the two known problematic easements from the property facts (Greenbelt Access & Use Easement covering 0.31 acres in the NE interior, and City of Austin Drainage Easement covering 0.130 acres in the NE corner) are depicted on this plan\n\n4. Any notes or callouts about easement restrictions or tree planting prohibitions\n\nThis information will help determine if any proposed trees are located within transmission easement boundaries, which would violate EL-2.5 (categorical prohibition on trees within transmission easement boundaries).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Grading Plan\" (Sheet 11 of 39), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. Easement boundaries shown on this plan:**\n*   **Transmission easement boundaries:** There are **no** easements explicitly labeled as \"Transmission Easement\" on this plan.\n*   **Electric utility easements:** \n    *   \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located along the eastern property line, adjacent to Bldg 6).\n    *   \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located in the southeast corner).\n    *   \"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located along the southern property line, southeast of Bldg 6).\n*   **Drainage easements:** \n    *   \"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located in the extreme northeast corner).\n    *   \"15' Drainage Easement\" (Located along the southern boundary, near the southeast corner).\n*   **Public utility easements:** \n    *   \"7.5' P.U.E.\" (Located along the northern property boundary).\n*   **Other notable easements:**\n    *   \"Greenbelt Access & Use Easement Doc. 2010149121 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located in the northeast interior).\n    *   \"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located along the eastern property line, overlapping/adjacent to the 5' Electric Easement).\n    *   \"Wastewater Easement Doc#...\" (Located in the northwest corner near the entrance).\n    *   \"Sidewalk Easement Doc#...\" (Located along the western boundary facing Valley View Road).\n\n**2. Location of these easements relative to proposed buildings and proposed landscape areas:**\n*   The **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** is located east/northeast of **Bldg 5** (Units 501-504), running along the northeastern property boundary.\n*   The **\"Greenbelt Access & Use Easement\"** is located east of **Bldg 4** (Unit 405) and southeast of **Bldg 5**. It occupies the open space between these buildings and the eastern property line/existing retaining walls.\n*   The **\"7.5' P.U.E.\"** runs along the northern boundary line, providing a buffer space north of **Bldg 3** (Units 302-305).\n*   The **\"5' Electric Easement\"** and **\"15' Easement\"** run along the eastern boundary, east of **Bldg 6** (Units 601-604).\n*   *Note on landscape areas:* This specific sheet is a grading plan and does not explicitly delineate or label \"proposed landscape areas\" or individual proposed trees. The open spaces where these easements reside will likely contain the landscaping, but a Tree List box on the plan explicitly states: *\"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"*\n\n**3. Depiction of the two known problematic easements:**\n*   **Greenbelt Access & Use Easement:** **Yes**, this is clearly depicted. It is explicitly labeled as *\"Greenbelt Access & Use Easement Doc. 2010149121 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"* located in the northeast interior section of the site, bordered by existing retaining walls.\n*   **City of Austin Drainage Easement:** **Yes**, this is depicted. It is explicitly labeled as *\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"* in the extreme northeast corner of the property.\n\n**4. Notes or callouts about easement restrictions or tree planting prohibitions:**\n*   A thorough scan of the general notes, title block, and the text immediately surrounding the easements on this specific sheet reveals **no notes or callouts** regarding easement restrictions or tree planting prohibitions. \n*   Because this is a Grading Plan, its notes primarily focus on benchmarks, contours, and legal descriptions. As noted above, it directs the viewer to Sheet 32 for landscaping details. \n\n**Summary for EL-2.5 Compliance Checking:**\nBased strictly on this Grading Plan sheet, there are **no transmission easements labeled**. Therefore, there is no evidence *on this specific page* that proposed trees would be placed within a transmission easement boundary. You will need to consult the Landscape Plan (Sheet 32) to see exact tree placement and check if any trees conflict with the other various utility and drainage easements identified here.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1495,"outputTokens":1106,"totalTokens":4405,"reasoningTokens":1804},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2337396]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appe