 CAL., 8' HT. MINIMUM, CONTAINER GROWN\n*   **Species:** MEXICAN REDBUD, CERCIS CANADENSIS VAR. MEXICANA\n    *   **Quantity:** 6\n    *   **Minimum Specifications:** 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL., 10' HT. MINIMUM, CONTAINER GROWN\n\n**2. Species Proposed to Fulfill the 13 Required Inches**\nThe \"COA REQUIRED TREES CHART\" calculates a \"Total tree inches required\" of \"A = 13\" (comprised of Streetyard, Buffer, and Parking Lot requirements). However, the chart does **not** specify which exact species from the Plant List will fulfill these 13 required inches. It simply points to the aggregate total of all trees proposed on the site (\"PER PLANT LIST 12 @ 4\"\", \"8 @ 2.5\"\") to fulfill and exceed the requirement.\n\n**3. Breakdown of \"12 @ 4\"\" and \"8 @ 2.5\"\"**\nCross-referencing the \"COA REQUIRED TREES CHART\" with the \"PLANT LIST\" quantities and caliper specifications:\n*   **\"12 @ 4\"** refers to the Shade Trees: 2 Live Oaks (4\" CAL.) + 10 Cedar Elms (4\" CAL.) = 12 trees.\n*   **\"8 @ 2.5\"** refers to the Ornamental Trees: 2 Texas Mountain Laurels (2.5\" CAL.) + 6 Mexican Redbuds (2.5\" CAL.) = 8 trees.\n\n**4. Notes on Where Mitigation Trees are Being Placed**\nThere are **no notes** on Sheet 35 that specify the physical location (e.g., \"southern boundary,\" \"buffer area\") of where mitigation trees are being planted. The \"CITY OF AUSTIN LANDSCAPE CALCULATIONS\" section under \"URBAN FORESTRY INFORMATION\" merely states: \"TOTAL MITIGATION INCHES PLANTED ON SITE  55 INCHES\". \n\n**5. Mature Heights and ECM Appendix F Utility-Compatible Designations**\nThis information is **not present** on Sheet 35. \n*   The Plant List only provides minimum planting heights (e.g., \"16' HT. MINIMUM\", \"8' HT. MINIMUM\") under the \"MIN. SPEC.\" column, rather than mature heights. \n*   While \"ECM APP. F TREES\" are mentioned in the \"TREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS\" regarding existing trees to be surveyed/removed, there is no text linking the specific proposed specie