f Austin Land Development Code.\n3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776705802758,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JJSCvYPbj1ARAJcNkwnWbA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019BodCb4jJijaaNVJEm9N9s","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) and identify the locations of:\n1. All electrical transformer pads on the site. Describe their locations (north, south, east, west, near which building).\n2. All electrical pull boxes shown. Are they clustered or distributed?\n3. Are there any pad-mounted equipment access doors or notes visible? Describe their orientation.\n4. Approximately how many feet from the transformer pads and pull boxes are the proposed buildings?\n\nThis information will help determine if proposed trees might be within prohibited clearance zones from these underground electrical facilities per UCM § 1.10.10.4."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1804,"cache_read_input_tokens":71632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1804},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b09093e-77f3-4183-964d-6ca1d8b22912","uuid":"05e7d6ab-91ac-4c67-a777-576824139927"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705802759,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) and identify the locations of:\n1. All electrical transformer pads on the site. Describe their locations (north, south, east, west, near which building).\n2. All electrical pull boxes shown. Are they clustered or distributed?\n3. Are there any pad-mounted equipment access doors or notes visible? Describe their orientation.\n4. Approximately how many feet from the transformer pads and pull boxes are the proposed buildings?\n\nThis information will help determine if proposed trees might be within prohibited clearance zones from these underground electrical facilities per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (21)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705803019,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LLZdV21qsf9ZuBE1XNu4XB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have tree information available. Now let me look at the actual tree list table (Sheet 32 Block 3) to see if any trees are near transformer pads. But first, let me think about how much more investigation I need.\n\nAt this point, I have identified:\n1. Two clear FAILS: EL-13.7 for Pads 1 and 3 (sidewalk clearances)\n2. Several PASS items from measurements\n3. Several NOT-VERIFIABLE items due to missing documentation\n\nFor the remaining items, let me think about whether they require more investigation:\n\nItems that might need tree analysis:\n- EL-13.13: Trees within 10 lateral feet of equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution - needs tree/landscape check\n- EL-13.14: Shrubs 10 feet from access door side, 5 feet from other sides - needs landscape check\n- EL-13.15: Root barriers for trees within 20 feet - needs landscape check\n\nItems that might need utility separation analysis:\n- EL-13.21-28: Utility separations - need to check if visible on sheets\n\nItems that might be N/A:\n- EL-13.3: Fence clearances - only if fences directly adjacent\n- EL-13.5: Balconies/overhangs - only if present\n- EL-13.6: Windows/doors - only if present and less than 12 feet from grade\n- EL-13.8: Stairwells - only if serving as fire exits\n- EL-13.9: Fire escapes - only if oil-filled equipment and fire escapes present\n- EL-13.11: Confined space - only if niches proposed\n- EL-13.16-18: Dumpsters, bike racks, light poles - only if present\n- EL-13.24: Gas lines - only if gas service\n\n\n- EL-13.27-28: Overhead distribution - only if present\n- EL-13.29-30: Niches - only if niches proposed\n- EL-13.39: Structures over overhead - only if overhead present\n\nLet me check the Tree List table to see if any trees are explicitly noted as being near electrical equipment or transformers.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2802,"cache_read_input_tokens":84376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2802},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fa6dd19-b9c0-47f2-aaf9-fa9fde6b7270","uuid":"20439f39-e862-4831-95d9-97eb76f44925"}
