fically crossing over the proposed driveways (labeled \"Construct Type III Driveway\") and proposed sidewalk areas along the western boundary. They also run in close proximity to, or over, proposed retaining walls (e.g., \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" at the bottom right and bottom left).\n\n**2) At the points where the OHE line crosses the western property boundary near Valley View Road, are there sidewalks shown?**\n\nYes. Where the \"- OHE -\" line runs along and crosses the western property boundary near Valley View Road, it intersects with areas explicitly designated as sidewalks.\n*   Near the northernmost driveway entrance on the west side, the OHE line crosses directly over a hatched rectangular path labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 432S-1\"**.\n*   Moving south along that western boundary, the OHE line runs parallel to and crosses over sections of a similarly hatched path labeled **\"Sidewalk Easement\"**.\n\n**3) Are sidewalks shown at both ends of the property along the Valley View Road frontage, particularly where the utility poles are located?**\n\nNo, sidewalks are not shown extending to the absolute ends of the property frontage near the utility poles on *both* sides.\n*   **Northern end (Top Left):** Yes. There is a cluster of utility infrastructure (poles/manholes) near the top left corner of the property boundary. The hatched path labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 432S-1\"** is shown extending to this northern property line near the poles.\n*   **Southern end (Bottom Left):** No. There is a utility pole shown at the very bottom-left corner of the property boundary where the OHE lines turn. However, the shaded sidewalk path along the western frontage is shown terminating at the northern edge of the lower **\"Construct Type III Driveway\"**. The plan does not show the shaded sidewalk hatching continuing south of this driveway to reach the utility pole at the southern corner of the property."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776705825226,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0128TCPFS7YT3DNTNiAmzBjK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"EXCELLENT! Now I have critical information:\n\n**Block 20 - Electric Transmission Notes (Note 1):**\n\"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.\"\n\n**Block 14 & Block 8 - Austin Energy Notes:**\nBoth mention that \"The owner shall be responsible for...any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project.\"\n\nSo the site plans DO reference Austin Energy requirements and clearances. The notes specifically state:\n- No trees within 25 feet of transmission structures\n- The owner is responsible for tree pruning/removal within 10 feet of overhead electric facilities\n\nHowever, there are NO specific Austin Energy APPROVALS shown on the plans for trees within prohibited clearance zones. The notes just say what the owner's responsibility is.\n\nThe transmission notes are quite detailed (16 points), but they ONLY apply to **transmission facilities**. \n\nThe question is: Are there transmission facilities on this property?\n\nFrom my earlier findings:\n- The vision analysis of Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) found NO transmission easements labeled\n- Block 20 shows detailed transmission notes, suggesting transmission facilities ARE present on the property\n- But the exact location isn't clear to me yet\n\nLet me check if there's specific reference to transmission facilities on this property. The general notes mention \"Electric Transmission Clearances: No digging/grading/trees within 25 feet of transmission structures\" which suggests transmission facilities DO exist.\n\nBut wait - those notes are GENERAL notes on Sheet 3. They may be boilerplate notes that apply to all developments, not necessarily specific to this site.\n\nThe key point is: From my grading plan vision analysis, there were **NO transmission easements labeled**. There were only distribution electric easements (5' Electric Easements).\n\nSo the question is: Are there TRANSMISSION facilities on this site or not?\n\nThe notes suggest the site might have them, but the grading plan doesn't show them. \n\nIf transmission facilities do exist but aren't clearly depicted, that's a potential deficiency. Focusing on what I can actually verify: the plant legend fails to identify specific species for trees near overhead electric facilities, making it impossible to confirm utility compatibility or mature heights. Additionally, at least one mitigation tree sits at 2.3 feet from the overhead line, which falls significantly below the required 15-foot minimum clearance.\n\nThe plans also lack dimensioned clearances between trees and overhead conductors, with no notes explaining measurement methodology. Most critically, there's no documented Austin Energy written approval for trees positioned within prohibited clearance zones, despite general code references in the notes.\n\nFor EL-2.1, the non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution conductors fail because the first mitigation tree sits at 2.3 feet from the overhead line. Without species identification, I can't verify utility compatibility, but at that proximity only UC trees are permitted—and the distance alone suggests non-compliance regardless. EL-2.2 doesn't apply since no transmission facilities appear on the grading plan. EL-2.3 also fails: the large tree at 2.3 feet from distribution lines violates the 25-foot minimum for trees 40 feet or taller.\n\nEL-2.4 and EL-2.5 are not applicable—no transmission easements are shown. EL-2.6 is possibly failing because the first mitigation tree may fall within 10 feet of a utility pole, though pole locations need closer verification. EL-2.7 cannot be fully evaluated since pad-mounted transformers are proposed but tree species remain unidentified, making distance measurements difficult to assess. EL-2.8\n\n: Trees within 5 feet of underground equipment cannot be verified without knowing what underground infrastructure exists beyond distribution lines and which species are planted. EL-2.9 similarly cannot be determined. EL-2.10 is a clear failure—the plant schedule lists species generically without tying them to specific plan locations, making it impossible to verify UC status or mature heights for individual trees. EL-2.11 cannot be resolved because determining which trees are large (40+ feet) requires species identification.\n\nFor clearance requirements, the landscape plan lacks any dimensioned distances from trees to conductors, so both EL-2.12 and EL-2.13 fail. The canopy circles visually overlap the overhead electric line, but no measurements are provided. However, EL-2.14 passes since trees are shown in relation to overhead facilities on Sheet 31.\n\nThe mitigation tree positioned at 2.3 feet presents a critical issue—it falls within a prohibited clearance zone unless it meets specific criteria. Without visible Austin Energy approval documentation and without species identification on the plan, I can't verify whether this tree qualifies as utility-compatible or meets the height restrictions that would allow it in that zone. The tree's actual mature height and species designation are essential to determining compliance, but neither is documented.\n\nThis creates cascading failures: the species identification itself is missing (EL-2.10), the clearance distances aren't dimensioned on the plan (EL-2.12 & EL-2.13), and I cannot verify whether the non-UC trees maintain adequate separation since I don't know what species they are. Given the 2.3-foot distance, even if the tree were utility-compatible, the lack of documentation makes this not-verifiable at best and likely a violation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2531,"cache_read_input_tokens":71342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2531},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"3a54cb0c-7c16-4950-9416-1a6da4870473"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705826062,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) and identify the locations of:\n1. All electrical transformer pads on the site. Describe their locations (north, south, east, west, near which building).\n2. All electrical pull boxes shown. Are they clustered or distributed?\n3. Are there any pad-mounted equipment access doors or notes visible? Describe their orientation.\n4. Approximately how many feet from the transformer pads and pull boxes are the proposed buildings?\n\nThis information will help determine if proposed trees might be within prohibited clearance zones from these underground electrical facilities per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 21, \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here are the findings regarding the electrical facilities, using the site's North arrow (pointing generally toward the top of the page) and the provided scale (1\" = 20') for reference:\n\n**1. Locations of Electrical Transformer Pads:**\nThere are three clearly labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations on the site. They are situated along the primary underground electrical line (depicted as a blue line with 'E' markers):\n\n*   **West location:** Situated on the western side of the site, located between the western property line and the gap between **Bldg. 2** (specifically near Unit 201) and **Bldg. 8** (specifically near Unit 801).\n*   **Southwest location:** Situated near the southwest corner of the site, located southwest of **Bldg. 8** (specifically near Unit 801) and near the western property line.\n*   **East location:** Situated on the eastern side of the site, located in the gap between **Bldg. 5** (specifically near Unit 504) and **Bldg. 6** (specifically near Unit 601), near the eastern property boundary.\n\n**2. Locations of Electrical Pull Boxes:**\nThe structures labeled \"Electrical Pull Box\" are **distributed** throughout the site, rather than clustered in one single area. They serve as nodes along the looping underground electrical line. Specific labeled locations include:\n\n*   Northwest: North of Bldg. 1.\n*   North-Central: North of Bldg. 3.\n*   Northeast: Near the northeast corner, east of Bldg. 3 / north of Bldg. 5.\n*   East: Near the Electrical Transformer Pad between Bldg. 5 and Bldg. 6.\n*   Central: In the center of the site, located in the gap between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7.\n*   West: Near the Electrical Transformer Pad located between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8.\n*   Southwest: Near the Electrical Transformer Pad located southwest of Bldg. 8.\n*   South-Central: South of Bldg. 7.\n\n**3. Pad-mounted equipment access doors or notes:**\nBased on the visual evidence on this specific sheet, there are **no visible notes, dashed clearance lines, or indications of access door orientations** drawn on or immediately adjacent to the three \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" rectangles. They are depicted simply as solid rectangles connected to the utility line.\n\n**4. Approximate distance from transformer pads and pull boxes to proposed buildings:**\nUsing the provided graphic scale (\"Scale 1\\\" = 20'\") to visually estimate distances on the plan:\n\n*   **Transformer Pads:** The transformer pads appear to be located very close to the proposed building footprints.\n    *   The West pad (near Bldg. 2/8) appears to be approximately **5 to 10 feet** from the nearest building corners.\n    *   The East pad (between Bldg. 5/6) appears to be approximately **5 to 10 feet** from the building lines.\n    *   The Southwest pad (near Bldg. 8) appears slightly further away, approximately **10 to 15 feet** from the building footprint.\n*   **Pull Boxes:** The pull boxes are distributed at varying distances.\n    *   Some pull boxes running along the northern perimeter (north of Bldg. 1 and 3) appear to be roughly **15 to 20 feet** away from the buildings.\n    *   However, pull boxes located between buildings (such as the one centrally located between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7) are situated very close to the building lines, appearing to be within **5 feet** of the structures.\n\n*(Note: These are visual approximations based on comparing the drawn distance on the plan to the graphical scale bar provided).*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1444,"outputTokens":834,"totalTokens":3932,"reasoningTokens":1654},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"ty