\nBased on the visual evidence on this specific sheet, there are **no visible notes, dashed clearance lines, or indications of access door orientations** drawn on or immediately adjacent to the three \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" rectangles. They are depicted simply as solid rectangles connected to the utility line.\n\n**4. Approximate distance from transformer pads and pull boxes to proposed buildings:**\nUsing the provided graphic scale (\"Scale 1\\\" = 20'\") to visually estimate distances on the plan:\n\n*   **Transformer Pads:** The transformer pads appear to be located very close to the proposed building footprints.\n    *   The West pad (near Bldg. 2/8) appears to be approximately **5 to 10 feet** from the nearest building corners.\n    *   The East pad (between Bldg. 5/6) appears to be approximately **5 to 10 feet** from the building lines.\n    *   The Southwest pad (near Bldg. 8) appears slightly further away, approximately **10 to 15 feet** from the building footprint.\n*   **Pull Boxes:** The pull boxes are distributed at varying distances.\n    *   Some pull boxes running along the northern perimeter (north of Bldg. 1 and 3) appear to be roughly **15 to 20 feet** away from the buildings.\n    *   However, pull boxes located between buildings (such as the one centrally located between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7) are situated very close to the building lines, appearing to be within **5 feet** of the structures.\n\n*(Note: These are visual approximations based on comparing the drawn distance on the plan to the graphical scale bar provided).*"}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776705826687,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012TAbsw4DHbmnJoTgsz9BKe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good findings. This shows that:\n1. No buildings/parking directly under the OHE\n2. Sidewalks ARE shown at the northern end where poles exist\n3. Sidewalks NOT shown at the southern end near the pole\n\nThis could be a deficiency under EL-1.25 (sidewalks not cleared from poles at property ends). However, I should be careful here - the item says \"Sidewalks not cleared from existing power poles at each end of property along right-of-way.\" The question is whether this applies if the sidewalk simply isn't extended to that corner, or if it's specifically about sidewalks that ARE present but too close to poles.\n\nLooking at the checklist item more carefully: \"Only when new or modified sidewalks are proposed and existing power poles are located within or immediately adjacent to sidewalk alignment at property limits along ROW frontage.\"\n\nThis seems to be asking: IF there's a sidewalk at the property limit where a pole exists, is it properly cleared? Not asking: MUST sidewalks be extended to every corner.\n\nSince sidewalks ARE shown at one end (north) where a pole exists, I should check if that sidewalk shows proper clearance from the pole. The vision analysis said the sidewalk \"is shown extending to this northern property line near the poles\" - so it appears to reach the pole area. I might not have enough evidence to make a clear determination here.\n\nLet me also reconsider EL-1.27: \"Customer facilities proposed to be installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities in violation of prohibition, or items within electric easements do not maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor.\"\n\nThe driveway entrances and sidewalks might be considered \"items\" that are under the overhead distribution facilities. However, the item's description seems to focus on more permanent \"customer facilities\" like buildings, parking garages, etc. A driveway or sidewalk passing under an overhead line might be acceptable as long as it has the required vertical clearance - which is already covered under EL-1.18.\n\n\nEL-1.31 about survey documentation for marginal clearances could be relevant since I've flagged driveways under overhead lines without verified clearance data. The four main findings I've identified—EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.18, EL-1.37, and EL-1.46—appear to be the most substantial issues. I should verify whether EL-1.31 applies when survey data showing pole locations and mid-span clearances hasn't been provided for existing overhead facilities that may not meet minimum requirements.\n\nThe condition triggers when vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed features like driveways or parking appears marginal or insufficient based on available site plan information. Since I've documented driveways crossing beneath the overhead line without any clearance dimensions shown, this qualifies as a marginal situation requiring a registered surveyor's verification of mid-span clearances. I'll include EL-1.31 in my findings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1690,"cache_read_input_tokens":79348,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1690},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d43314f-ffee-4c09-9531-73169237fb4a","uuid":"bcf5f865-6802-4472-8c99-8828c6cc6397"}
