{"level":30,"time":1776705833638,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0128TCPFS7YT3DNTNiAmzBjK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review, I now have sufficient evidence to evaluate the checklist items. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary of Research Phase\n\nI have reviewed the relevant site plan sheets and supplementary materials:\n\n**Electrical Infrastructure Found:**\n- Overhead Electric (OHE) lines shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) running along southern and western property boundaries\n- Voltage classification NOT specified (defaulting to distribution per grouping guidance)\n- Five-foot electric easements shown on Grading Plan (Sheet 11)\n- NO transmission easements labeled on the plans\n- No Austin Energy approval letters visible for tree clearances\n\n**Trees Proposed Near Overhead Facilities:**\n- Three mitigation trees (\"M\" symbols) in southeast corner of landscape plan near overhead electric line\n- Measured distances from tree trunk centers to overhead electric line:\n  - **First tree: 2.3 feet** (MEDIUM confidence) - **WELL BELOW all clearance thresholds**\n  - Second tree: 116.9 feet\n  - Third tree: 127 feet\n- Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists species generically (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but does NOT identify which species are at which locations on the landscape plan\n\n**CRITICAL DEFICIENCY: Plant Species Identification**\n- Landscape plan shows \"M\" tree symbols but provides no callouts or legend indicating species\n- Plant schedule exists but is not keyed to specific tree locations on the landscape plan\n- Therefore, utility compatibility and mature height cannot be verified for the trees near overhead facilities\n\n**CRITICAL DEFICIENCY: Missing Clearance Dimensions**\n- No distance callouts or dimensions shown from any trees to the overhead electric line on the landscape plan\n- No notes addressing tree clearances from overhead electric facilities\n- Visual overlap of drawn canopy circles with OHE line is depicted but not quantified\n\n**General Notes References (Sheet 3):**\n- Austin Energy requirements stated in Block 14 and Block 8\n- Electric Transmission Notes (Block 20) reference 25-foot clearances from transmission structures - but no transmission easements are shown\n- Notes acknowledge owner responsibility for clearances but no approval letters are included for non-compliant plantings\n\n---\n\n## Checklist Item Evaluation\n\nBased on the evidence, here are my determinations:\n\n**EL-2.1**: Non-UC trees within 15 ft of distribution - **FAIL** (First tree at 2.3 ft; cannot verify UC status due to missing species identification; at this distance, only UC trees permitted)\n\n**EL-2.2**: Non-UC trees within 50 ft of transmission - **NOT APPLICABLE** (No transmission easements shown)\n\n**EL-2.3**: Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution - **FAIL** (First tree at 2.3 ft; cannot verify if large due to missing species identification)\n\n**EL-2.4**: Large trees within 50 ft of transmission - **NOT APPLICABLE** (No transmission easements shown)\n\n**EL-2.5**: Trees in transmission easement - **NOT APPLICABLE** (No transmission easements shown on grading plan)\n\n**EL-2.6**: Trees within 10 ft of utility pole - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (Pole locations not clearly dimensioned; without species identification and specific pole locations, cannot confirm violation)\n\n**EL-2.7**: Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (Pad-mounted transformers shown on Sheet 21 but distances not dimensioned; cannot verify without species identification)\n\n**EL-2.8**: Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (Underground equipment locations on Sheet 21 but distances not dimensioned; species not identified)\n\n**EL-2.9**: Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment lack root barriers - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (No root barrier specifications shown on landscape plan; cannot verify without identified species and documented underground equipment locations)\n\n**EL-2.10**: Plant legend/schedule doesn't identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities - **FAIL** (Plant schedule lists species generically but does not tie specific species to specific tree locations shown on landscape plan)\n\n**EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plans - **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (Cannot determine which trees are large without species identification)\n\n**EL-2.12**: Clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor - **FAIL** (No clearances are dimensioned on plans; no distance callouts from trees to conductors visible; measurement methodology cannot be verified)\n\n**EL-2.13**: Clearances measured from canopy instead of trunk - **FAIL** (No clearances are dimensioned on plans; visual overlap shown but no distance callouts demonstrating proper measurement from trunk to conductor)\n\n**EL-2.14**: Trees not shown in relation to overhead facilities - **PASS** (Trees are shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric line; sufficient clarity exists for spatial relationship)\n\n**EL-2.15**: Trees proposed in prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval - **FAIL** (First mitigation tree at 2.3 ft from overhead distribution line appears to be in prohibited clearance zone with no documented Austin Energy written approval visible on the plans)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2531,"cache_read_input_tokens":71342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2531},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"beece159-f5e0-45d7-9273-1986309591cc"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705839403,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012TAbsw4DHbmnJoTgsz9BKe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LcrUxxjxsAXDyVC3bp1VKb","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building elevation sheets for all 8 proposed buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead electric conductors are not included on building elevation sheets. Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) documents overhead utility poles and lines along Valley View Road and crossing the property, but no registered surveyor data for conductor elevations or clearance verification from proposed buildings is provided on elevations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All 8 proposed buildings and their relationships to overhead electric line shown on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and building projections for clearance verification. Overhead utility line (marked OHE) is shown on site plan and landscape plan, but no dimension lines, callouts, or clearance annotations are provided demonstrating compliance with the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearance requirements."},{"defici