{"level":30,"time":1776705843215,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan carefully. Locate all proposed trees on the plan. For each major cluster of trees, note their location relative to the buildings and any marked utility locations (look for \"T\" symbols or any utility marking). Specifically identify if there are any trees shown within 20 feet of: (1) the northwest area near Building 1, (2) the west area near Building 2, (3) the southwest area near Building 8, (4) the east area between Buildings 4-5, or (5) the southeast area between Buildings 6-7. Note tree species labels if visible and whether any trees are labeled with species codes (like SY, PL, P, M).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the findings regarding the proposed trees, their locations relative to the buildings, marked utilities, and specific tree codes. \n\n*Note: The building sections themselves are not explicitly labeled with \"Building 1\", \"Building 2\", etc., on this specific sheet. The analysis below uses the directional cues provided in your prompt to infer these locations on the primary structure footprint.*\n\n**Tree Legend / Key Notes (Transcribed exactly as written):**\n*   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n**Utility Lines Identified:**\nWhile standalone \"T\" symbols for utilities are not clearly evident, standard utility lines are marked with alphanumeric codes between dashes throughout the plan:\n*   **-W-** (Water)\n*   **-E-** (Electric)\n*   **-SD-** (Storm Drain)\n*   **-OHE-** (Overhead Electric)\n*   **-LOC-** (Limits of Construction)\n\n---\n\n### Area Analysis (Based on 1\"=20'-0\" Scale):\n\n**(1) Northwest Area (implied near Building 1)**\n*   **Trees & Distance:** There is a cluster of trees along the northern property line. Based on the scale, there is at least one tree explicitly labeled **\"PL\"** located immediately adjacent to the northern building facade, well within 20 feet. Another tree slightly further west is labeled **\"SY\"**.\n*   **Utilities:** A horizontal limit line labeled **\"---LOC---\"** runs north of these trees. Vertical utility lines labeled **\"-W-\"** and **\"-E-\"** run to the west of this building section.\n*   **Species Codes:** \"PL\", \"SY\", and a cluster further north labeled \"M\".\n\n**(2) West Area (implied near Building 2)**\n*   **Trees & Distance:** Trees are located within shaded median/island areas along the western frontage (indicated by notes H.1, H.2, H.3). Based on the scale, the easternmost trees within these islands appear to sit roughly 20 feet from the western building facade, with some potentially just within that 20-foot threshold.\n*   **Utilities:** Vertical utility lines labeled **\"-W-\"** and **\"-E-\"** run directly through this western area.\n*   **Species Codes:** Several trees in this cluster are explicitly labeled with codes, including **\"SY\"**, **\"M\"**, and combined **\"SY M\"**.\n\n**(3) Southwest Area (implied near Building 8)**\n*   **Trees & Distance:** There are trees planted near the southwest corner of the main structure. Based on the scale, there is a tree explicitly labeled **\"M\"** located extremely close to the southern facade of this southwest building section, definitively within 20 feet. \n*   **Utilities:** Horizontal utility lines marked **\"-SD-\"** and **\"-OHE-\"** run east-west just south of this building area.\n*   **Species Codes:** The tree closest to the building, as well as several along the southern property line below it, are labeled **\"M\"**.\n\n**(4) East Area (implied between Buildings 4-5)**\n*   **Trees & Distance:** This area contains a courtyard-like space featuring a **\"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\"** and a **\"FILTRATION BASIN\"**. Trees are located to the east of these basins along the property line. Based on the scale, it is difficult to confirm if the trees on the far eastern edge are within 20 feet of the eastern building facades, but they appear to be further out (likely 30+ feet away).\n*   **Utilities:** A vertical boundary line labeled **\"---LOC---\"** runs through this area.\n*   **Species Codes:** The trees depicted here are drawn as standard circles with crosshairs but do not contain visible letter codes (like SY, PL, P, M) inside them.\n\n**(5) Southeast Area (implied between Buildings 6-7)**\n*   **Trees & Distance:** There is a cluster of proposed trees in the southeast corner. Based on the scale, there are three distinct trees located immediately adjacent to the southern and eastern facades of this building section, definitively within 20 feet.\n*   **Utilities:** Horizontal utility lines marked **\"-SD-\"** and **\"-OHE-\"** run east-west just south of these trees, and a vertical **\"---LOC---\"** line is to their east.\n*   **Species Codes:** These three trees closest to the building are all explicitly labeled **\"M\"**.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1457,"outputTokens":1057,"totalTokens":5402,"reasoningTokens":2888},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read somethin