ting compliance with the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Northern and southern driveway entrances along Valley View Road where overhead electric lines span across the entry points"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways do not show minimum vertical clearance verification from lowest point of overhead electric facilities including telecommunications attachments. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows two driveway entrances (northern entrance west of Building 1 and southern entrance west of Building 8) that cross under the overhead utility line along Valley View Road, but no vertical clearance dimensions, mid-span clearance survey data, or section views are provided demonstrating compliance with the 16-foot minimum (for parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot minimum (for areas with truck traffic) vertical clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway entrances crossing under overhead electric line at western property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Survey by registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span clearances not provided when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements. Driveway vertical clearances to overhead lines appear marginal based on site plan elevations; no surveyor-verified mid-span clearance data is provided to confirm driveways maintain the required 16-foot or 18-foot minimum vertical clearance from the lowest point of the overhead conductors and any attachments."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along overhead electric line where trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductors are not verified as being from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows a row of trees planted directly on or immediately adjacent to the overhead electric line (OHE) along the southern boundary. Plant list (Sheet 35) specifies 2 Live Oak and 10 Cedar Elm as shade trees to be planted in this location. These species are not utility-compatible and exceed the 20-foot mature height typically required for utility-compatible trees. No distance clearance dimensions are provided between tree planting locations and the conductor."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. Overhead electric poles and lines exist on the site (documented on existing conditions survey Sheet 4) and construction is proposed; the required 48-hour notification note per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 is absent from the cover sheet and general notes."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ef0c9296-0d60-499f-bcfb-6e787e62ef3c"}
{"level":30,"time":1776705846245,"pid":50886,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0128TCPFS7YT3DNTNiAmzBjK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016fbpX7d6ekkFbD3s1MJgy3","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of property near southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21)"}],"comment":"First mitigation tree in southeast corner is positioned approximately 2.3 feet laterally from the overhead electric distribution line (measured trunk center to conductor). This distance is far below the minimum 15-foot clearance required for non-utility-compatible trees from distribution conductors. However, species of this tree is not identified on the landscape plan, preventing verification of utility compatibility status. If non-utility-compatible, tree placement violates clearance requirement; if utility-compatible, it may be acceptable. Species identification is required to confirm compliance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of property near southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21)"}],"comment":"First mitigation tree in southeast corner is positioned at approximately 2.3 feet laterally from the overhead electric distribution line, well within the 25-foot minimum clearance zone for large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F). Species identity and mature height cannot be verified from the landscape plan. If this tree is ≥40 feet at maturity, it violates the 25-foot clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed near overhead electric facilities throughout the site, particularly southeast corner"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Calculations (Sheet 35)"}],"comment":"Plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists tree species generically (e.g., Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but does not identify which species are proposed at which specific tree locations shown on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31). Without species-to-location linkage, utility compatibility status (UC designation per ECM Appendix F) and mature height cannot be verified for trees proposed near overhead electric facilities, preventing compliance verification for clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"}],"comment":"No distance dimensions or callouts are shown on the Landscape Plan indicating clearances from tree locations to the overhead electric line or from tree trunks to utility poles or pad-mounted equipment. Clearance measurement methodology cannot be verified; plans do not demonstrate that measurements are taken from the outside conductor (not pole centerline) as required by UCM § 1.10.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"}],"comment":"No distance dimensions or callouts on the Landscape Plan indicate whether clearances from trees to utilities are measured from tree trunk centers (planting location) or from projected canopy edges. The visual representation shows tree canopy circles overlapping the overhead electric line, but no dimension callouts demonstrate that measurements comply with the requirement to measure from tree trunk center rather than canopy edge."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of property near southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21)"}],"comment":"First mitigation tree proposed at approximately 2.3 feet from the overhead electric distribution line is positioned in a prohibited clearance zone (less than 15 feet, where only utility-compatible trees are permitted by distribution clearance zones). No documented written approval from Austin Energy is visible on the submitted plans authorizing this tree placement in the restricted zone. Plans must include explicit written Austin Energy approval if trees are to be planted within clearance-restricted areas."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2531,"cache_read_input_tokens":71342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2531},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988f0669-90e8-4f1d-9dca-90ae9f4ae41d","uuid":"1a8cda05-9ee9-46af-8e94-ec180bbf321b"}
