ads are positioned 5-15 feet from buildings and trees cluster around the perimeter, but without precise measurements between specific trees and equipment, I can't confirm a violation. Similarly for EL-2.8 with pull boxes distributed throughout—I'd need to identify which trees are actually within 5 feet of underground infrastructure. For EL-2.9, the root barrier specifications aren't detailed enough in the available documents to make a definitive call.\n\nSince the task requires only flagging clear deficiencies or items where compliance truly cannot be verified, these three don't meet that threshold. I have insufficient evidence of actual violations, so excluding them is the right call.\n\nThe six flagged items remain solid based on documented evidence.\n\nNow I need to evaluate EL-2.10.\n\nThe plant schedule lists specific species—Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud—but the landscape plan itself uses generic symbols (SY, PL, M, P) without directly correlating them to species. While Sheet 35 contains the plant list, the landscape drawing doesn't show which species corresponds to which symbol on the plan. This appears to be a legitimate violation since the species identification isn't present on the landscape plan itself. flag EL-2.10 since the plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies the species and is cross-referenced on the landscape plan itself. The requirement is satisfied even though the legend on Sheet 31 uses generic symbols rather than species names.\n\nMy six flagged items seem solid. I should verify that my comments are precise and clearly explain each deficiency.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3648,"cache_read_input_tokens":76149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3648},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":nu