 feet of overhead distribution conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows proposed shrubs and vegetation but does not show transformer pad locations. Therefore, clearance distances from transformer access door sides (10 lateral feet required) and from other sides (5 lateral feet required) cannot be verified. Landscape plan must explicitly show transformer pad locations with callouts indicating shrub/vegetation clearance zones."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not show transformer pad locations, and no root barrier details are provided. If trees are proposed within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads, root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, installed 5 feet from equipment) must be detailed and shown on landscape plan. Cannot verify compliance without transformer pad overlay and root barrier specifications."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Although measurements from transformer pads to identified utility lines (water, wastewater, storm drain) show clearances well in excess of 12 inches (40-78 feet), the plans do not explicitly dimension all 12-inch minimum clearances from transformer pads to other underground utilitie