not dimensioned in relation to transformer pad locations on either the landscape plan or electrical plan. Tree species cross-reference to ECM Appendix F 'UC' (Utility Compatible) column is not provided, making verification of utility compatibility impossible for trees within 10 lateral feet of equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows proposed shrubs and vegetation but does not show transformer pad locations. Therefore, clearance distances from transformer access door sides (10 lateral feet required) and from other sides (5 lateral feet required) cannot be verified. Landscape plan must explicitly show transformer pad locations with callouts indicating shrub/vegetation clearance zones."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not show transformer pad locations, and no root barrier details are provided. If trees are proposed within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads, root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, installed 5 feet from equipment) must be detailed and shown on landscape plan. Cannot verify compliance without transformer pad overlay and root barrier specifications."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Although measurements from transformer pads to identified utility lines (water, wastewater, storm drain) show clearances well in excess of 12 inches (40-78 feet), the plans do not explicitly dimension all 12-inch minimum clearances from transformer pads to other underground utilities (reclaimed water, communications, gas, fuel, steam). Specific dimension callouts confirming 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearances from all other underground utilities must be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include explicit dimension callouts or notes confirming that transformer pads and Austin Energy underground facilities are not located over or under other utility lines, and that customer buildings/foundations/structures are not installed over Austin Energy underground facilities. Cross-utility coordination notes or dimension callouts confirming no conflicts must be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If overhead distribution lines are present on the site, minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution line conductors (primary, neutral, secondary extending from ground to sky) must be verified. Overhead line locations and transformer pad locations are not overlaid on site plan with dimension callouts. If overhead distribution exists, clearance callouts must be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors exist on the site, minimum 15-foot radius clearance measured from the conductor centerline must be shown. Overhead conductor locations relative to transformer pad locations are not dimensioned on the utility or site plan. If overhead distribution exists, 15-foot radius clearance zone callouts must be provided."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f6c74af9-1ed6-4cf9-8b5c-cc209752d8ec"}
